      "content": [
        "Luke"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "toc2",
      "content": [
        "Luke"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "toc3",
      "content": [
        "LUK"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "mt1",
      "content": [
        "Luke"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "1",
      "sid": "LUK 1"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Dedication to Theophilus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ACT 1:1-3",
          "content": [
            "Acts 1:1–3"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "LUK 1:1"
        },
        "Many have undertaken to compose an account of the things that have been fulfilled among us, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "LUK 1:2"
        },
        "just as they were handed down to us by the initial eyewitnesses and servants of the word. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "LUK 1:3"
        },
        "Therefore, having carefully investigated everything from the beginning, it seemed good also to me to write an orderly account for you, most excellent Theophilus, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "LUK 1:4"
        },
        "so that you may know the certainty of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " things you have been taught."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Gabriel Foretells John’s Birth"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "LUK 1:5"
        },
        "In the time of Herod king of Judea there was a priest named Zechariah, who belonged to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " priestly division of Abijah, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "whose"
          ]
        },
        " wife Elizabeth ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "was"
          ]
        },
        " a descendant of Aaron. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "LUK 1:6"
        },
        "Both of them were righteous in the sight of God, walking blamelessly in all the commandments and decrees of the Lord. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "LUK 1:7"
        },
        "But they had no children, because Elizabeth was barren, and they were both well along in years."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "LUK 1:8"
        },
        "One day while ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Zechariah’s"
          ]
        },
        " division was on duty ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " he was serving as priest before God, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "LUK 1:9"
        },
        "he was chosen by lot, according to the custom of the priesthood, to enter the temple of the Lord ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " burn incense. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "LUK 1:10"
        },
        "And at the hour of the incense offering, the whole congregation was praying outside."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "LUK 1:11"
        },
        "Just then an angel of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord appeared to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Zechariah"
          ]
        },
        ", standing at ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " right side of the altar of incense. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "LUK 1:12"
        },
        "When Zechariah saw ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        ", he was startled and gripped with fear."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "LUK 1:13"
        },
        "But the angel said to him, “",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Do"
          ]
        },
        " not be afraid, Zechariah, because your prayer has been heard. Your wife Elizabeth will bear you a son, and you are to give him the name John. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "LUK 1:14"
        },
        "He will be a joy and delight to you, and many will rejoice at his birth, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "LUK 1:15"
        },
        "for he will be great in the sight of the Lord. He shall never take wine ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " strong drink, and he will be filled ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "with the"
          ]
        },
        " Holy Spirit even from his mother’s womb. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "LUK 1:16"
        },
        "Many of the sons of Israel he will turn back to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord their God. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "LUK 1:17"
        },
        "And he will go on before ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the Lord"
          ]
        },
        " in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " spirit and power of Elijah, to turn ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " hearts of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " fathers to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " children",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "1:17 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "MAL 4:5-6",
                  "content": [
                    "Malachi 4:5–6"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " disobedient to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " wisdom of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " righteous — to make ready a people prepared for ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "LUK 1:18"
        },
        "“How can I be sure of this?” Zechariah asked the angel. “I am an old man, and my wife is well along in years.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "LUK 1:19"
        },
        "“I am Gabriel,” replied the angel. “I stand in the presence of God, and I have been sent to speak to you and to bring you this good news. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "LUK 1:20"
        },
        "And now you will be silent and unable to speak until the day ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        " comes to pass, because you did not believe my words, which will be fulfilled at their proper time.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "LUK 1:21"
        },
        "Meanwhile, the people were waiting for Zechariah and wondering why he took so long in the temple. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "LUK 1:22"
        },
        "When he came out ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " was unable to speak to them, they realized he had seen a vision in the temple. He kept making signs to them but remained unable to speak. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "LUK 1:23"
        },
        "And when the days of his service were complete, he returned home."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "LUK 1:24"
        },
        "After these days, his wife Elizabeth became pregnant and for five months remained in seclusion. She declared, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "LUK 1:25"
        },
        "“The Lord has done ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        " for me. In ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "these"
          ]
        },
        " days He has shown me favor and taken away my disgrace among the people.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Gabriel Foretells Jesus’ Birth"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "LUK 1:26"
        },
        "In the sixth month, God sent the angel Gabriel to a town in Galilee called Nazareth, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "LUK 1:27"
        },
        "to a virgin pledged in marriage to a man named Joseph, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who was"
          ]
        },
        " of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " house of David. And the virgin’s name ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "was"
          ]
        },
        " Mary. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "LUK 1:28"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "The angel"
          ]
        },
        " appeared to her ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, “Greetings,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "1:28 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Rejoice"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " you who are highly favored! The Lord ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " with you.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "1:28 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "BYZ and TR include "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Blessed are you among women!"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "LUK 1:29"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Mary"
          ]
        },
        " was greatly troubled at ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " words and wondered what kind of greeting this might be. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "LUK 1:30"
        },
        "So the angel told her, “",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Do"
          ]
        },
        " not be afraid, Mary, for you have found favor with God. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "LUK 1:31"
        },
        "Behold, you will conceive and give birth to a son, and you are to give Him the name Jesus. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "LUK 1:32"
        },
        "He will be great and will be called ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Son of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Most High. The Lord God will give Him the throne of His father David, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "LUK 1:33"
        },
        "and He will reign over the house of Jacob forever. His kingdom will never end!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "LUK 1:34"
        },
        "“How can this be,” Mary asked the angel, “since I am a virgin?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "LUK 1:35"
        },
        "The angel replied, “",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "The"
          ]
        },
        " Holy Spirit will come upon you, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " power of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Most High will overshadow you. So the Holy One to be born",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "1:35 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "TR "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "born of you"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " will be called ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Son of God. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "36",
          "sid": "LUK 1:36"
        },
        "Look, even Elizabeth your relative has conceived a son in her old age, and she who ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "was"
          ]
        },
        " called barren is in her sixth month. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "LUK 1:37"
        },
        "For no word from God will ever fail.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "1:37 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "For nothing will be impossible with God."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "38",
          "sid": "LUK 1:38"
        },
        "“",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "I am"
          ]
        },
        " the Lord’s servant,” Mary answered. “May it happen to me according to your word.” Then the angel left her."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Mary Visits Elizabeth"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "39",
          "sid": "LUK 1:39"
        },
        "In those days Mary got ready ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " hurried to a town in the hill country of Judah, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "40",
          "sid": "LUK 1:40"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "where"
          ]
        },
        " she entered the home of Zechariah and greeted Elizabeth."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "41",
          "sid": "LUK 1:41"
        },
        "When Elizabeth heard Mary’s greeting, the baby leaped in her womb, and Elizabeth was filled with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Holy Spirit. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "42",
          "sid": "LUK 1:42"
        },
        "In a loud voice she exclaimed, “Blessed are you among women, and blessed is the fruit of your womb! ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "43",
          "sid": "LUK 1:43"
        },
        "And why am I so ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "honored"
          ]
        },
        ", that the mother of my Lord should come to me? ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "44",
          "sid": "LUK 1:44"
        },
        "For as soon as the sound of your greeting reached my ears, the baby in my womb leaped for joy. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "45",
          "sid": "LUK 1:45"
        },
        "Blessed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " she who has believed that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord’s word to her will be fulfilled.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Mary’s Song"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "1SA 2:1-11",
          "content": [
            "1 Samuel 2:1–11"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "46",
          "sid": "LUK 1:46"
        },
        "Then Mary said:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“My soul magnifies the Lord,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "47",
          "sid": "LUK 1:47"
        },
        "and my spirit rejoices in God my Savior!"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "48",
          "sid": "LUK 1:48"
        },
        "For He has looked with favor on the humble state of His servant."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "From now on all generations will call me blessed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "49",
          "sid": "LUK 1:49"
        },
        "For the Mighty One has done great things for me."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "Holy ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " His name."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "50",
          "sid": "LUK 1:50"
        },
        "His mercy ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "extends"
          ]
        },
        " to those who fear Him,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "from generation to generation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "51",
          "sid": "LUK 1:51"
        },
        "He has performed mighty deeds with His arm;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "He has scattered ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "those who are"
          ]
        },
        " proud"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " thoughts of their hearts."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "52",
          "sid": "LUK 1:52"
        },
        "He has brought down rulers from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " thrones,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "but"
          ]
        },
        " has exalted ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " humble."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "53",
          "sid": "LUK 1:53"
        },
        "He has filled ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " hungry with good things,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "but"
          ]
        },
        " has sent ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " rich ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "away"
          ]
        },
        " empty."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "54",
          "sid": "LUK 1:54"
        },
        "He has helped His servant Israel,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "remembering to be merciful,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "55",
          "sid": "LUK 1:55"
        },
        "as He promised to our fathers,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "to Abraham and his descendants forever.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "56",
          "sid": "LUK 1:56"
        },
        "Mary stayed with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Elizabeth"
          ]
        },
        " for about three months and then returned home."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Birth of John the Baptist"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "57",
          "sid": "LUK 1:57"
        },
        "When the time came for Elizabeth to have her child, she gave birth to a son. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "58",
          "sid": "LUK 1:58"
        },
        "Her neighbors and relatives heard that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord had shown her great mercy, and they rejoiced with her."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "59",
          "sid": "LUK 1:59"
        },
        "On the eighth day, when they came to circumcise the child, they were going to name ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " after his father Zechariah. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "60",
          "sid": "LUK 1:60"
        },
        "But his mother replied, “No! He shall be called John.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "61",
          "sid": "LUK 1:61"
        },
        "They said to her, “There is no one among your relatives who bears this name.” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "62",
          "sid": "LUK 1:62"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        " they made signs to his father ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to find out"
          ]
        },
        " what he wanted to name ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the child"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "63",
          "sid": "LUK 1:63"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Zechariah"
          ]
        },
        " asked for a tablet ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " wrote, “His name is John.” And they were all amazed. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "64",
          "sid": "LUK 1:64"
        },
        "Immediately ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Zechariah’s"
          ]
        },
        " mouth was opened and his tongue ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "was released"
          ]
        },
        ", and he began to speak, praising God."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "65",
          "sid": "LUK 1:65"
        },
        "All their neighbors were filled with awe, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "people"
          ]
        },
        " throughout the hill country of Judea were talking about these events. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "66",
          "sid": "LUK 1:66"
        },
        "And all who heard ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        " wondered in their hearts ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " asked, “What then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "will"
          ]
        },
        " this child become?” For the Lord’s hand was with him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Zechariah’s Song"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "67",
          "sid": "LUK 1:67"
        },
        "Then his father Zechariah was filled with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Holy Spirit and prophesied:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "68",
          "sid": "LUK 1:68"
        },
        "“Blessed be ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord, the God of Israel,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "because He has visited and redeemed His people."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "69",
          "sid": "LUK 1:69"
        },
        "He has raised up a horn of salvation for us"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " house of His servant David,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "70",
          "sid": "LUK 1:70"
        },
        "as He spoke through His holy prophets,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "those"
          ]
        },
        " of ages past,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "71",
          "sid": "LUK 1:71"
        },
        "salvation from our enemies"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " hand of all who hate us,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "72",
          "sid": "LUK 1:72"
        },
        "to show mercy to our fathers"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and to remember His holy covenant,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "73",
          "sid": "LUK 1:73"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " oath He swore to our father Abraham,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "to grant us ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "74",
          "sid": "LUK 1:74"
        },
        "deliverance from hostile hands,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "that we may serve Him without fear,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "75",
          "sid": "LUK 1:75"
        },
        "in holiness and righteousness before Him"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "all the days of our lives."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "76",
          "sid": "LUK 1:76"
        },
        "And you, child, will be called"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "a prophet of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Most High;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "for you will go on before the Lord"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "to prepare the way for Him,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "77",
          "sid": "LUK 1:77"
        },
        "to give to His people the knowledge of salvation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "through ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " forgiveness of their sins,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "78",
          "sid": "LUK 1:78"
        },
        "because of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " tender mercy of our God,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "by which ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Dawn",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "1:78 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the Morning Light "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the Sunrise"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " will visit us from on high,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "79",
          "sid": "LUK 1:79"
        },
        "to shine on those who live in darkness"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " shadow of death,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "to guide our feet"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "into ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " path of peace.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "80",
          "sid": "LUK 1:80"
        },
        "And the child grew and became strong in spirit;",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "1:80 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "in the Spirit"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " and he lived in the wilderness until ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " time of his public appearance to Israel."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "2",
      "sid": "LUK 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Birth of Jesus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 1:18-25",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 1:18–25"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "LUK 2:1"
        },
        "Now in those days a decree went out from Caesar Augustus that a census should be taken of the whole empire.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:1 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "of the whole land "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "of the whole world"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "LUK 2:2"
        },
        "This ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "was the"
          ]
        },
        " first census to take place ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "while"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:2 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "This was the census before"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " Quirinius was governor of Syria. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "LUK 2:3"
        },
        "And everyone went to his own town to register."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "LUK 2:4"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        " Joseph also went up from Nazareth in Galilee to Judea, to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " city of David called Bethlehem, since he was from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " house and line of David. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "LUK 2:5"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He went there"
          ]
        },
        " to register with Mary, who was pledged to him in marriage ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " was expecting a child."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "LUK 2:6"
        },
        "While they were there, the time came for her Child to be born. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "LUK 2:7"
        },
        "And she gave birth to her firstborn, a Son. She wrapped Him in swaddling cloths and laid Him in a manger, because there was no room for them in the inn."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Shepherds and the Angels"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "LUK 2:8"
        },
        "And there were shepherds residing in the fields nearby, keeping watch over their flocks by night. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "LUK 2:9"
        },
        "Just then an angel of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord stood before them, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " glory of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord shone around them, and they were terrified. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "LUK 2:10"
        },
        "But the angel said to them, “",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Do"
          ]
        },
        " not be afraid! For behold, I bring you good news ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of"
          ]
        },
        " great joy that will be for all the people: ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "LUK 2:11"
        },
        "Today in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " city of David a Savior has been born to you. He is Christ ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord! ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "LUK 2:12"
        },
        "And this ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "will be"
          ]
        },
        " a sign to you: You will find a baby wrapped in swaddling cloths and lying in a manger.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "LUK 2:13"
        },
        "And suddenly there appeared with the angel a great multitude of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " heavenly host, praising God and saying:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "LUK 2:14"
        },
        "“Glory to God in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " highest,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and on earth peace to men"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "on whom His favor rests!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "LUK 2:15"
        },
        "When the angels had left them ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and gone"
          ]
        },
        " into heaven, the shepherds said to one another, “Let us go to Bethlehem and see this ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "thing"
          ]
        },
        " that has happened, which the Lord has made known to us.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "LUK 2:16"
        },
        "So they hurried off and found Mary and Joseph and the Baby, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who"
          ]
        },
        " was lying in the manger. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "LUK 2:17"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "After"
          ]
        },
        " they had seen ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the Child"
          ]
        },
        ", they spread the message they had received about ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "LUK 2:18"
        },
        "And all who heard ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        " were amazed at what the shepherds said to them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "LUK 2:19"
        },
        "But Mary treasured up all these things ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " pondered ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " in her heart."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "LUK 2:20"
        },
        "The shepherds returned, glorifying and praising God for all they had heard and seen, which was just as ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the angel"
          ]
        },
        " had told them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Jesus Presented at the Temple"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "LUK 2:21"
        },
        "When ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " eight days before His circumcision had passed, He was named Jesus, the name the angel had given ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        " before He was conceived."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "LUK 2:22"
        },
        "And when the time of purification according to the Law of Moses was complete, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His parents"
          ]
        },
        " brought Him to Jerusalem to present ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        " to the Lord ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "LUK 2:23"
        },
        "(as it is written in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Law of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord: “Every firstborn male shall be consecrated to the Lord”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:23 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "EXO 13:2",
                  "content": [
                    "Exodus 13:2"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "), ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "LUK 2:24"
        },
        "and to offer ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " sacrifice specified in the Law of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord: “A pair of turtledoves or two young pigeons.”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:24 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "LEV 12:8",
                  "content": [
                    "Leviticus 12:8"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Prophecy of Simeon"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "LUK 2:25"
        },
        "Now there was a man in Jerusalem named Simeon, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "was"
          ]
        },
        " righteous and devout. He was waiting for ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " consolation of Israel, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Holy Spirit was upon him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "LUK 2:26"
        },
        "The Holy Spirit had revealed to him ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that he would"
          ]
        },
        " not see death before he had seen the Lord’s Christ. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "LUK 2:27"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Led by"
          ]
        },
        " the Spirit, he went into the temple ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "courts"
          ]
        },
        ".",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:27 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the temple"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; also in verse 46"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " And when the parents brought in the child Jesus to do for Him what was customary under the Law, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "LUK 2:28"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Simeon"
          ]
        },
        " took Him in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " arms and blessed God, saying:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "LUK 2:29"
        },
        "“Sovereign Lord, as You have promised,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "You now dismiss Your servant in peace."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "LUK 2:30"
        },
        "For my eyes have seen Your salvation,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "LUK 2:31"
        },
        "which You have prepared in the sight of all people,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "LUK 2:32"
        },
        "a light for revelation to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Gentiles,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and for glory to Your people Israel.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "LUK 2:33"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "The Child’s"
          ]
        },
        " father and mother were amazed at what was spoken about Him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "LUK 2:34"
        },
        "Then Simeon blessed them and said to His mother Mary:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“Behold, this ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Child"
          ]
        },
        " is appointed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to cause"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " rise and fall of many in Israel,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to be"
          ]
        },
        " a sign that will be spoken against,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "LUK 2:35"
        },
        "so that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " thoughts of many hearts will be revealed —"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and a sword will pierce your soul as well.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Prophecy of Anna"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "36",
          "sid": "LUK 2:36"
        },
        "There was also a prophetess ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "named"
          ]
        },
        " Anna, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " daughter of Phanuel, of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " tribe of Asher, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who"
          ]
        },
        " was well along in years. She had been married for seven years, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "LUK 2:37"
        },
        "and then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "was"
          ]
        },
        " a widow ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to the age of"
          ]
        },
        " eighty-four.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:37 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "was a widow for eighty-four years"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "She"
          ]
        },
        " never left the temple, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "but"
          ]
        },
        " worshiped night and day, fasting and praying."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "38",
          "sid": "LUK 2:38"
        },
        "Coming forward at that moment, she gave thanks to God and spoke about ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the Child"
          ]
        },
        " to all who were waiting for ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " redemption of Jerusalem."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Return to Nazareth"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 2:19-23",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 2:19–23"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "39",
          "sid": "LUK 2:39"
        },
        "When ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus’ parents"
          ]
        },
        " had done everything required by the Law of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord, they returned to Galilee, to their ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "own"
          ]
        },
        " town of Nazareth."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "40",
          "sid": "LUK 2:40"
        },
        "And the Child grew and became strong.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:40 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "BYZ and TR "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "became strong in spirit"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " He was filled with wisdom, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " grace of God was upon Him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Boy Jesus at the Temple"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "41",
          "sid": "LUK 2:41"
        },
        "Every year His parents went to Jerusalem for the Feast of the Passover. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "42",
          "sid": "LUK 2:42"
        },
        "And when He was twelve years ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "old"
          ]
        },
        ", they went up according to the custom of the Feast."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "43",
          "sid": "LUK 2:43"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " those days were over ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " they were returning ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "home"
          ]
        },
        ", the boy Jesus remained behind in Jerusalem, but His parents were unaware ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He had stayed"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "44",
          "sid": "LUK 2:44"
        },
        "Assuming He was in their company, they traveled on for a day ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "before"
          ]
        },
        " they began to look for Him among ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " relatives and friends."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "45",
          "sid": "LUK 2:45"
        },
        "When they could not find ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        ", they returned to Jerusalem to search for Him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "46",
          "sid": "LUK 2:46"
        },
        "Finally, after three days they found Him in the temple ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "courts"
          ]
        },
        ", sitting among the teachers, listening to them and asking them questions. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "47",
          "sid": "LUK 2:47"
        },
        "And all who heard Him were astounded at His understanding and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His"
          ]
        },
        " answers."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "48",
          "sid": "LUK 2:48"
        },
        "When ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His parents"
          ]
        },
        " saw Him, they were astonished. “Child, why have You done this to us?” His mother asked. “Your father and I have been anxiously searching for You.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "49",
              "sid": "LUK 2:49"
            },
            "“Why were you looking for Me?”"
          ]
        },
        " He asked. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Did you not know that I had to be in My Father’s ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "house "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "2:49 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "Or "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "I had to be about My Father’s business"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "?”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "50",
          "sid": "LUK 2:50"
        },
        "But they did not understand the statement He was making to them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "51",
          "sid": "LUK 2:51"
        },
        "Then He went down to Nazareth with them and was obedient to them. But His mother treasured up all these things in her heart."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "52",
          "sid": "LUK 2:52"
        },
        "And Jesus grew in wisdom and stature, and in favor with God and man."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "3",
      "sid": "LUK 3"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Mission of John the Baptist"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ISA 40:1-5",
          "content": [
            "Isaiah 40:1–5"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 3:1-12",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 3:1–12"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 1:1-8",
          "content": [
            "Mark 1:1–8"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JHN 1:19-28",
          "content": [
            "John 1:19–28"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "LUK 3:1"
        },
        "In ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " fifteenth year of the reign of Tiberius Caesar, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "while"
          ]
        },
        " Pontius Pilate was governor of Judea, Herod tetrarch of Galilee, his brother Philip tetrarch of Ituraea and Trachonitis, and Lysanias tetrarch of Abilene, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "LUK 3:2"
        },
        "during ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " high priesthood of Annas and Caiaphas, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " word of God came to John son of Zechariah in the wilderness."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "LUK 3:3"
        },
        "He went into all the region around the Jordan, preaching a baptism of repentance for ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " forgiveness of sins, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "LUK 3:4"
        },
        "as it is written in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " book of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " words of Isaiah ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " prophet:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "A"
          ]
        },
        " voice of one calling in the wilderness,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "‘Prepare the way for ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "make straight paths for Him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "LUK 3:5"
        },
        "Every valley shall be filled in,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and every mountain and hill made low."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "The crooked ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "ways"
          ]
        },
        " shall be made straight,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and the rough ways smooth."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "LUK 3:6"
        },
        "And all humanity will see God’s salvation.’”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "3:6 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "And all flesh will see God’s salvation"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "ISA 40:3-5",
                  "content": [
                    "Isaiah 40:3–5"
                  ]
                },
                " (see also LXX)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "LUK 3:7"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "John"
          ]
        },
        " said to the crowds coming out to be baptized by him, “You brood of vipers, who warned you to flee from the coming wrath? ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "LUK 3:8"
        },
        "Produce fruit, then, in keeping with repentance. And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "do"
          ]
        },
        " not begin to say to yourselves, ‘We have Abraham ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "as our"
          ]
        },
        " father.’ For I tell you that out of these stones God can raise up children for Abraham. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "LUK 3:9"
        },
        "The axe lies ready at the root of the trees, and every tree that does not produce good fruit will be cut down and thrown into ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " fire.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "LUK 3:10"
        },
        "The crowds asked him, “What then should we do?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "LUK 3:11"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "John"
          ]
        },
        " replied, “Whoever has two tunics should share with him who has none, and whoever has food should do the same.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "LUK 3:12"
        },
        "Even tax collectors came to be baptized. “Teacher,” they asked, “what should we do?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "LUK 3:13"
        },
        "“Collect no more than you are authorized,” he answered."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "LUK 3:14"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "some"
          ]
        },
        " soldiers asked him, “And what should we do?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "“Do not take money by force or false accusation,” he said. “Be content with your wages.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "LUK 3:15"
        },
        "The people were waiting expectantly and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "were"
          ]
        },
        " all wondering in their hearts if John could be the Christ. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "LUK 3:16"
        },
        "John answered all of them: “I baptize you with water,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "3:16 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "in water"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " but ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "One"
          ]
        },
        " more powerful than I will come, the straps of whose sandals I am not worthy to untie.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "3:16 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Cited in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "ACT 13:25",
                  "content": [
                    "Acts 13:25"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " He will baptize you with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Holy Spirit and with fire.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "3:16 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "in the Holy Spirit and in fire"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "LUK 3:17"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His"
          ]
        },
        " winnowing fork ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " in His hand to clear His threshing floor and to gather the wheat into His barn; but He will burn up the chaff with unquenchable fire.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "LUK 3:18"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "With these and"
          ]
        },
        " many other exhortations, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "John"
          ]
        },
        " proclaimed the good news to the people. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "LUK 3:19"
        },
        "But when he rebuked Herod the tetrarch regarding his brother’s wife Herodias and all ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " evils ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "he"
          ]
        },
        " had done, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "LUK 3:20"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Herod"
          ]
        },
        " added this to them all: He locked John ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "up"
          ]
        },
        " in prison."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Baptism of Jesus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 3:13-17",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 3:13–17"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 1:9-11",
          "content": [
            "Mark 1:9–11"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JHN 1:29-34",
          "content": [
            "John 1:29–34"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "LUK 3:21"
        },
        "When all the people were being baptized, Jesus was baptized too. And as He was praying, heaven was opened, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "LUK 3:22"
        },
        "and the Holy Spirit descended on Him in a bodily form like a dove. And a voice came from heaven: “You are My beloved Son; in You I am well pleased.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Genealogy of Jesus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "RUT 4:18-22",
          "content": [
            "Ruth 4:18–22"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 1:1-17",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 1:1–17"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "LUK 3:23"
        },
