        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "LUK 4:2"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "where for"
          ]
        },
        " forty days He was tempted by the devil. He ate nothing during those days, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " they had ended, He was hungry."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "LUK 4:3"
        },
        "The devil said to Him, “If You are ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Son of God, tell this stone to become bread.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "LUK 4:4"
        },
        "But Jesus answered, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“It is written: ‘Man shall not live on bread alone.’",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "4:4 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "ref",
                      "loc": "DEU 8:3",
                      "content": [
                        "Deuteronomy 8:3"
                      ]
                    },
                    "; BYZ and TR "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "on bread alone, but on every word of God"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "."
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "LUK 4:5"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the devil"
          ]
        },
        " led Him up to a high place ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " showed Him in an instant all the kingdoms of the world. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "LUK 4:6"
        },
        "“I will give You authority over all ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "these kingdoms"
          ]
        },
        " and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "all"
          ]
        },
        " their glory,” ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "he"
          ]
        },
        " said. “For it has been relinquished to me, and I can give it to anyone I wish. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "LUK 4:7"
        },
        "So if You worship me, it will all be Yours.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "LUK 4:8"
        },
        "But Jesus answered, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“It is written: ‘Worship ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " Lord your God and serve Him only.’",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "4:8 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "ref",
                      "loc": "DEU 6:13",
                      "content": [
                        "Deuteronomy 6:13"
                      ]
                    },
                    "; BYZ and TR "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "“Get behind Me, Satan! For it is written..."
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "LUK 4:9"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the devil"
          ]
        },
        " led Him to Jerusalem and set ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        " on the pinnacle of the temple. “If You are ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Son of God,” he said, “throw Yourself down from here. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "LUK 4:10"
        },
        "For it is written:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "‘He will command His angels concerning You"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "to guard You carefully,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "LUK 4:11"
        },
        "and they will lift You ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "up"
          ]
        },
        " in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " hands,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "so that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "You will"
          ]
        },
        " not strike Your foot against a stone.’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "4:11 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PSA 91:11-12",
                  "content": [
                    "Psalm 91:11–12"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "LUK 4:12"
        },
        "But Jesus answered, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“It ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "also"
              ]
            },
            " says, ‘Do not put ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " Lord your God ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "to the test"
              ]
            },
            ".’",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "4:12 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "ref",
                      "loc": "DEU 6:16",
                      "content": [
                        "Deuteronomy 6:16"
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "LUK 4:13"
        },
        "When the devil had finished every temptation, he left Him until an opportune time."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Jesus Begins His Ministry"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ISA 9:1-7",
          "content": [
            "Isaiah 9:1–7"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 4:12-17",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 4:12–17"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 1:14-15",
          "content": [
            "Mark 1:14–15"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "LUK 4:14"
        },
        "Jesus returned to Galilee in the power of the Spirit, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " news about Him spread throughout the surrounding region. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "LUK 4:15"
        },
        "He taught in their synagogues and was glorified by everyone."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Rejection at Nazareth"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ISA 61:1-11",
          "content": [
            "Isaiah 61:1–11"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 13:53-58",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 13:53–58"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 6:1-6",
          "content": [
            "Mark 6:1–6"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "LUK 4:16"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " came to Nazareth, where He had been brought up. As was His custom, He entered the synagogue on the Sabbath. And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " He stood up to read, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "LUK 4:17"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " scroll of the prophet Isaiah was handed to Him. Unrolling ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        ", He found the place where it was written:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "LUK 4:18"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "The"
              ]
            },
            " Spirit of ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " Lord ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "is"
              ]
            },
            " on Me,"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "because He has anointed Me"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "to preach good news to ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " poor."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "He has sent Me to proclaim liberty to ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " captives",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "4:18 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "BYZ and TR "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "He has sent Me to heal the brokenhearted, to proclaim liberty to the captives"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "and recovery of sight to ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " blind,"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "to release ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " oppressed,"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "LUK 4:19"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "to proclaim ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " year of ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " Lord’s favor.”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "4:19 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "to proclaim the acceptable year of the Lord"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "ISA 61:1-2",
                  "content": [
                    "Isaiah 61:1–2"
                  ]
                },
                " (see also LXX)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "LUK 4:20"
        },
        "Then He rolled up the scroll, returned ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        " to the attendant, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " sat down. The eyes of everyone in the synagogue were fixed on Him, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "LUK 4:21"
        },
        "and He began by saying, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Today this Scripture is fulfilled in your hearing.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "LUK 4:22"
        },
        "All spoke well of Him and marveled at the gracious words that came from His lips. “Isn’t this the son of Joseph?” they asked."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "LUK 4:23"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " said to them, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Surely you will quote this proverb to Me: ‘Physician, heal yourself! Do here in Your hometown what we have heard ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "that"
              ]
            },
            " You did in Capernaum.’”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "LUK 4:24"
        },
        "Then He added, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Truly I tell you, no prophet is accepted in his hometown. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "25",
              "sid": "LUK 4:25"
            },
            "But I tell you truthfully ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "that"
              ]
            },
            " there were many widows in Israel in the time of Elijah, when the sky was shut for three and a half years ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " great famine swept over all the land. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "26",
              "sid": "LUK 4:26"
            },
            "Yet Elijah was ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "not"
              ]
            },
            " sent to ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "any"
              ]
            },
            " of them, but to ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " widow of Zarephath in Sidon. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "27",
              "sid": "LUK 4:27"
            },
            "And there were many lepers",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "4:27 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "A "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "leper "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "was one afflicted with a skin disease. See Leviticus 13."
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            " in Israel in the time of Elisha the prophet. Yet not one of them was cleansed— only Naaman the Syrian.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "LUK 4:28"
        },
        "On hearing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        ", all ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the people"
          ]
        },
        " in the synagogue were enraged. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "LUK 4:29"
        },
        "They got up, drove Him out of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " town, and led Him to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " brow of the hill on which the town was built, in order to throw Him over the cliff. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "LUK 4:30"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " passed through ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the crowd"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " went on His way."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Jesus Expels an Unclean Spirit"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 1:21-28",
          "content": [
            "Mark 1:21–28"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "LUK 4:31"
        },
        "Then He went down to Capernaum, a town in Galilee, and on the Sabbath He began to teach ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the people"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "LUK 4:32"
        },
        "They were astonished at His teaching, because His message had authority."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "LUK 4:33"
        },
        "In the synagogue there was a man possessed by ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " spirit of an unclean demon. He cried out in a loud voice, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "LUK 4:34"
        },
        "“Ha! What do You ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "want"
          ]
        },
        " with us, Jesus of Nazareth? Have You come to destroy us? I know who You are — the Holy ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "One"
          ]
        },
        " of God!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "LUK 4:35"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "But"
          ]
        },
        " Jesus rebuked ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the demon"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Be silent!”"
          ]
        },
        " He said. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Come out of him!”"
          ]
        },
        " At this, the demon threw ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the man"
          ]
        },
        " down before them all ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " came out without harming him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "36",
          "sid": "LUK 4:36"
        },
        "All ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the people"
          ]
        },
        " were overcome with amazement and asked one another, “What ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " this message? With authority and power He commands the unclean spirits, and they come out!” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "LUK 4:37"
        },
        "And the news about ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " spread throughout the surrounding region."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Jesus Heals at Peter’s House"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 8:14-17",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 8:14–17"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 1:29-34",
          "content": [
            "Mark 1:29–34"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "38",
          "sid": "LUK 4:38"
        },
        "After ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " had left the synagogue, He went to the home of Simon, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "whose"
          ]
        },
        " mother-in-law was suffering from a high fever. So they appealed to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " on her ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "behalf"
          ]
        },
        ", ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "39",
          "sid": "LUK 4:39"
        },
        "and He stood over her ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " rebuked the fever, and it left her. And she got up at once ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " began to serve them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "40",
          "sid": "LUK 4:40"
        },
        "At sunset, all who were ill with various diseases were brought to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        ", and laying ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His"
          ]
        },
        " hands on each one, He healed them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "41",
          "sid": "LUK 4:41"
        },
        "Demons also came out of many ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "people"
          ]
        },
        ", shouting, “You are the Son of God!” But He rebuked ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the demons "
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " would not allow them to speak, because they knew He was the Christ."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Jesus Preaches in Judea"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 1:35-39",
          "content": [
            "Mark 1:35–39"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "42",
          "sid": "LUK 4:42"
        },
        "At daybreak, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " went out to a solitary place, and the crowds were looking for Him. They came to Him and tried to keep Him ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "from"
          ]
        },
        " leaving. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "43",
          "sid": "LUK 4:43"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " told them, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“I must preach ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " good news of the kingdom of God to the other towns as well, because that is why I was sent.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "44",
          "sid": "LUK 4:44"
        },
        "And He continued to preach in the synagogues of Judea.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "4:44 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "BYZ and TR "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Galilee"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; see ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "MRK 1:39",
                  "content": [
                    "Mark 1:39"
                  ]
                },
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "5",
      "sid": "LUK 5"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The First Disciples"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 4:18-22",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 4:18–22"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 1:16-20",
          "content": [
            "Mark 1:16–20"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JHN 1:35-42",
          "content": [
            "John 1:35–42"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "LUK 5:1"
        },
        "On one occasion, while ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " was standing by the Lake of Gennesaret",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "5:1 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "That is, the Sea of Galilee"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "with"
          ]
        },
        " the crowd pressing in on Him to hear the word of God, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "LUK 5:2"
        },
        "He saw two boats at the edge of the lake. The fishermen had left them and were washing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " nets. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "LUK 5:3"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " got into the boat belonging to Simon ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " asked him to put out a little from shore. And sitting down, He taught the people from the boat."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "LUK 5:4"
        },
        "When ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " had finished speaking, He said to Simon, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Put out into deep ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "water"
              ]
            },
            " and let down your nets for a catch.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "LUK 5:5"
        },
        "“Master,” Simon replied, “we have worked hard all night ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "without"
          ]
        },
        " catching ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "anything"
          ]
        },
        ". But because You say so, I will let down the nets.” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "LUK 5:6"
        },
        "When they had done so, they caught ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "such"
          ]
        },
        " a large number of fish ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " their nets began to tear. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "LUK 5:7"
        },
        "So they signaled to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " partners in the other boat to come ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " help them, and they came and filled both boats so ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "full"
          ]
        },
        " that they began to sink."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "LUK 5:8"
        },
        "When Simon Peter saw ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        ", he fell at Jesus’ knees. “Go away from me, Lord,” he said, “for I am a sinful man.” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "LUK 5:9"
        },
        "For he and his companions were astonished at the catch of fish they had taken, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "LUK 5:10"
        },
        "and so ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "were"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " partners James and John, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " sons of Zebedee."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "Do"
              ]
            },
            " not be afraid,”"
          ]
        },
        " Jesus said to Simon. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“From now on you will catch men.”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "LUK 5:11"
        },
        "And when they had brought ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " boats ashore, they left everything ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " followed Him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Leper’s Prayer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "LEV 14:1-32",
          "content": [
            "Leviticus 14:1–32"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 8:1-4",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 8:1–4"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 1:40-45",
          "content": [
            "Mark 1:40–45"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "LUK 5:12"
        },
        "While ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " was in one of the towns, a man ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "came along"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who was"
          ]
        },
        " covered with leprosy.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "5:12 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Leprosy was a term used for various skin diseases. See Leviticus 13."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " When he saw Jesus, he fell facedown ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " begged Him, “Lord, if You are willing, You can make me clean.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "LUK 5:13"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " reached out ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His"
          ]
        },
        " hand ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " touched ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the man"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“I am willing,”"
          ]
        },
        " He said. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Be clean!”"
          ]
        },
        " And immediately the leprosy left him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "14",
              "sid": "LUK 5:14"
            },
            "“",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "Do not"
              ]
            },
            " tell ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "anyone"
              ]
            },
            ",”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " instructed him. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“But go, show yourself to the priest and present the offering Moses prescribed for your cleansing, as a testimony to them.”",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "5:14 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "See ",
                    {
                      "type": "ref",
                      "loc": "LEV 14:1-32",
                      "content": [
                        "Leviticus 14:1–32"
                      ]
                    },
                    "."
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "LUK 5:15"
        },
        "But the news about ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " spread all the more, and great crowds came to hear ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        " and to be healed of their sicknesses. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "LUK 5:16"
        },
        "Yet He frequently withdrew to the wilderness to pray."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Jesus Heals a Paralytic"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 9:1-8",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 9:1–8"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 2:1-12",
          "content": [
            "Mark 2:1–12"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "LUK 5:17"
        },
        "One day ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " was teaching, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Pharisees and teachers of the law were sitting ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "People"
          ]
        },
        " had come from Jerusalem and from every village of Galilee and Judea, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " power of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord was ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "present"
          ]
        },
        " for Him to heal ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the sick"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "LUK 5:18"
        },
        "Just then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "some"
          ]
        },
        " men ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "came"
          ]
        },
        " carrying a paralyzed man on a mat. They tried to bring him inside to set him before ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        ", ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "LUK 5:19"
        },
        "but they could not find a way through the crowd. So they went up on the roof and lowered him on ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " mat through the tiles into the middle ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of the crowd"
          ]
        },
        ", right in front of Jesus."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "LUK 5:20"
        },
        "When ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " saw their faith, He said, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Friend, your sins are forgiven.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "LUK 5:21"
        },
        "But the scribes and Pharisees began thinking to themselves, “Who is this ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "man"
          ]
        },
        " who speaks blasphemy? Who can forgive sins but God alone?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "LUK 5:22"
        },
        "Knowing what they were thinking, Jesus replied, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Why are you thinking ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "these things"
              ]
            },
            " in your hearts? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "23",
              "sid": "LUK 5:23"
            },
            "Which is easier: to say, ‘Your sins are forgiven,’ or to say, ‘Get up and walk’? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "24",
              "sid": "LUK 5:24"
            },
            "But so that you may know that the Son of Man has authority on the earth to forgive sins…”"
          ]
        },
        " He said to the paralytic, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“I tell you, get up, pick up your mat, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " go home.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "LUK 5:25"
        },
        "And immediately ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the man"
          ]
        },
        " stood up before them, took what he had been lying on, and went home glorifying God. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "LUK 5:26"
        },
        "Everyone was taken with amazement and glorified God. They were filled with awe ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, “We have seen remarkable things today.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Jesus Calls Levi"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 9:9-13",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 9:9–13"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 2:13-17",
          "content": [
            "Mark 2:13–17"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "LUK 5:27"
        },
        "After ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        ", ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " went out and saw a tax collector named Levi sitting at the tax booth. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Follow Me,”"
          ]
        },
        " He told him, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "LUK 5:28"
        },
        "and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Levi"
          ]
        },
        " got up, left everything, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " followed Him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "LUK 5:29"
        },
        "Then Levi hosted a great banquet for ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " at his house. A large crowd of tax collectors was there, along with others who were eating with them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "LUK 5:30"
        },
        "But the Pharisees and their scribes complained to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus’"
          ]
        },
        " disciples, “Why do you eat and drink with tax collectors and sinners?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "LUK 5:31"
        },
        "Jesus answered, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "It is"
              ]
            },
            " not the healthy ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "who"
              ]
            },
            " need a doctor, but the sick. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "32",
              "sid": "LUK 5:32"
            },
            "I have not come to call ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " righteous, but sinners, to repentance.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Questions about Fasting"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 9:14-15",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 9:14–15"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 2:18-20",
          "content": [
            "Mark 2:18–20"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "LUK 5:33"
        },
        "Then they said to Him, “John’s disciples and those of the Pharisees frequently fast and pray, but Yours keep on eating and drinking.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "LUK 5:34"
        },
        "Jesus replied, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Can you make the guests of the bridegroom fast while ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "He"
              ]
            },
            " is with them? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "35",
              "sid": "LUK 5:35"
            },
            "But ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " time will come when the bridegroom will be taken from them; then they will fast.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Patches and the Wineskins"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 9:16-17",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 9:16–17"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 2:21-22",
          "content": [
            "Mark 2:21–22"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "36",
          "sid": "LUK 5:36"
        },
        "He also told them a parable: ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“No one tears a piece of cloth from a new garment ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " sews ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "it"
              ]
            },
            " on an old ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "one"
              ]
            },
            ". If he does, he will tear the new ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "garment"
              ]
            },
            " as well, and ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " patch from the new will not match the old."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "LUK 5:37"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "And no one pours new wine into old wineskins. If he does, the new wine will burst the skins, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the wine"
              ]
            },
            " will spill, and the wineskins will be ruined. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "38",
              "sid": "LUK 5:38"
            },
            "Instead, new wine is poured into new wineskins. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "39",
              "sid": "LUK 5:39"
            },
            "And no one after drinking old ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "wine "
              ]
            },
            " wants new, for he says, ‘The old is better.’”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "6",
      "sid": "LUK 6"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Lord of the Sabbath"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "1SA 21:1-7",
          "content": [
            "1 Samuel 21:1–7"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 12:1-8",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 12:1–8"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 2:23-28",
          "content": [
            "Mark 2:23–28"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "LUK 6:1"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "One"
          ]
        },
        " Sabbath",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "6:1 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "BYZ and TR "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "On the second Sabbath after the first"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " was passing through ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " grainfields, and His disciples began to pick the heads of grain, rub ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " hands, and eat ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "LUK 6:2"
        },
        "But some of the Pharisees asked, “Why are you doing what is unlawful ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "on"
          ]
        },
        " the Sabbath?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "LUK 6:3"
        },
        "Jesus replied, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Have you not read what David did when he and his companions were hungry? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "4",
              "sid": "LUK 6:4"
            },
            "He entered the house of God, took the consecrated bread",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "6:4 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "Or "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "the Bread of the Presence"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            " and gave ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "it"
              ]
            },
            " to his companions, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " ate what is lawful only for the priests to eat.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "LUK 6:5"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " declared, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“The Son of Man is Lord of the Sabbath.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Jesus Heals on the Sabbath"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 12:9-14",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 12:9–14"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 3:1-6",
          "content": [
            "Mark 3:1–6"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "LUK 6:6"
        },
        "On another Sabbath ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " entered the synagogue and was teaching, and a man was there ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "whose"
          ]
        },
        " right hand was withered. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "LUK 6:7"
        },
        "Looking for a reason to accuse ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        ", the scribes and Pharisees were watching Him closely ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to see"
          ]
        },
        " if He would heal on the Sabbath."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "LUK 6:8"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " knew their thoughts and said to the man with the withered hand, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Get up and stand among ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "us"
              ]
            },
            ".”"
          ]
        },
        " So he got up ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " stood ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "LUK 6:9"
        },
        "Then Jesus said to them, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“I ask you, which is lawful on the Sabbath: to do good or to do evil, to save life or to destroy ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "it"
              ]
            },
            "?”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "LUK 6:10"
        },
        "And after looking around at all of them, He said to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the man"
          ]
        },
        ", ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Stretch out your hand.”"
          ]
        },
        " He did ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "so"
          ]
        },
        ", and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        " was restored."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "LUK 6:11"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the scribes and Pharisees"
          ]
        },
        " were filled with rage and began to discuss with one another what they might do to Jesus."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Twelve Apostles"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 10:1-4",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 10:1–4"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 3:13-19",
          "content": [
            "Mark 3:13–19"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "LUK 6:12"
        },
        "In those days ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " went out to the mountain to pray, and He spent the night in prayer to God. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "LUK 6:13"
        },
        "When daylight came, He called His disciples ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to Him"
          ]
        },
        " and chose twelve of them, whom He also designated as apostles: ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "LUK 6:14"
        },
        "Simon, whom He named Peter, and his brother Andrew; James and John; Philip and Bartholomew; ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "LUK 6:15"
        },
        "Matthew and Thomas; James ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "son of"
          ]
        },
        " Alphaeus and Simon called ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Zealot; ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "LUK 6:16"
        },
        "Judas ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "son"
          ]
        },
        " of James, and Judas Iscariot, who became ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "a"
          ]
        },
        " traitor."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Jesus Heals the Multitudes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 4:23-25",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 4:23–25"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 3:7-12",
          "content": [
            "Mark 3:7–12"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "LUK 6:17"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " came down with them ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " stood on a level place. A large crowd of His disciples ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "was there"
          ]
        },
        ", along with a great number of people from all over Judea, Jerusalem, and the seacoast of Tyre and Sidon. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "LUK 6:18"
        },
        "They had come to hear Him and to be healed of their diseases, and those troubled by unclean spirits were healed. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "LUK 6:19"
        },
        "The entire crowd was trying to touch Him, because power was coming from Him and healing them all."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Beatitudes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "PSA 1:1-6",
          "content": [
            "Psalm 1:1–6"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 5:3-12",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 5:3–12"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "LUK 6:20"
        },
        "Looking up at His disciples, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " said:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Blessed ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "are"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "you"
              ]
            },
            " who are poor,"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "for yours is the kingdom of God."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "LUK 6:21"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Blessed ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "are"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "you"
              ]
            },
            " who hunger now,"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "for you will be filled."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Blessed ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "are"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "you"
              ]
            },
            " who weep now,"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "for you will laugh."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "LUK 6:22"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Blessed are you when people hate you, and when they exclude ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "you"
              ]
            },
            " and insult you and reject your name as evil because of the Son of Man. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "23",
              "sid": "LUK 6:23"
            },
            "Rejoice in that day and leap for joy, because great ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "is"
              ]
            },
            " your reward in heaven. For their fathers treated the prophets in the same way."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Woes to the Satisfied"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "AMO 6:1-7",
          "content": [
            "Amos 6:1–7"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "LUK 6:24"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "But woe to you who are rich,"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "for you have already received your comfort."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "LUK 6:25"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Woe to you who are well fed now,"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "for you will hunger."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Woe to ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "you"
              ]
            },
            " who laugh now,"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "for you will mourn and weep."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "LUK 6:26"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Woe to you when all men speak well of you,"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "for their fathers treated the false prophets in the same way."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Love Your Enemies"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 5:38-48",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 5:38–48"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "LUK 6:27"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "But to those of you who will listen, I say: Love your enemies, do good to those who hate you, ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "28",
              "sid": "LUK 6:28"
            },
            "bless those who curse you, pray for those who mistreat you. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "29",
              "sid": "LUK 6:29"
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "If someone"
              ]
            },
            " strikes you on ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "one"
              ]
            },
            " cheek, turn to him the other also. And ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "if someone"
              ]
            },
            " takes your cloak, do not withhold ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "your"
              ]
            },
            " tunic as well. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "30",
              "sid": "LUK 6:30"
            },
            "Give to everyone who asks you, and ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "if anyone"
              ]
            },
            " takes what ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "is"
              ]
            },
            " yours, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "do"
              ]
            },
            " not demand ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "it"
              ]
            },
            " back. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "31",
              "sid": "LUK 6:31"
            },
            "Do to ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "others"
              ]
            },
            " as you would have ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "them"
              ]
            },
            " do to you."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "LUK 6:32"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "If you love those who love you, what credit is that to you? Even sinners love those who love them. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "33",
              "sid": "LUK 6:33"
            },
            "If you do good to those who do good to you, what credit is that to you? Even sinners do the same. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "34",
              "sid": "LUK 6:34"
            },
            "And if you lend ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "to those"
              ]
            },
            " from whom you expect repayment, what credit is that to you? Even sinners lend to sinners, expecting to be repaid in full."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "LUK 6:35"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "But love your enemies, do good ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "to them"
              ]
            },
            ", and lend ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "to them"
              ]
            },
            ", expecting nothing in return. Then your reward will be great, and you will be sons of the Most High; for He is kind to the ungrateful and wicked. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "36",
              "sid": "LUK 6:36"
            },
            "Be merciful, just as your Father is merciful."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Judging Others"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 7:1-6",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 7:1–6"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ROM 14:1-12",
          "content": [
            "Romans 14:1–12"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "LUK 6:37"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "Do"
              ]
            },
            " not judge, and you will not be judged. ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "Do"
              ]
            },
            " not condemn, and you will not be condemned. Forgive, and you will be forgiven. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "38",
              "sid": "LUK 6:38"
            },
            "Give, and it will be given to you. A good measure, pressed down, shaken together, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " running over will be poured into your lap. For with the measure you ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "use"
              ]
            },
            ", it will be measured back to you.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "39",
          "sid": "LUK 6:39"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " also told them a parable: ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Can a blind ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "man"
              ]
            },
            " lead a blind ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "man"
              ]
            },
            "? ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "Will they"
              ]
            },
            " not both fall into a pit? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "40",
              "sid": "LUK 6:40"
            },
            "A disciple is not above ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "his"
              ]
            },
            " teacher, but everyone ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "who is"
              ]
            },
            " fully trained will be like his teacher."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "41",
          "sid": "LUK 6:41"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Why do you look at the speck in your brother’s eye but fail to notice ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " beam in ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "your"
              ]
            },
            " own eye? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "42",
              "sid": "LUK 6:42"
            },
            "How can you say, ‘Brother,",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "6:42 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "Literally "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "How can you say to your brother, ‘Brother"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            " let me take the speck ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "out"
              ]
            },
            " of your eye,’ ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "while"
              ]
            },
            " you yourself fail to see ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " beam in your own eye? ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "You"
              ]
            },
            " hypocrite! First take the beam out of your own eye, and then you will see clearly to remove the speck from your brother’s eye."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "A Tree and Its Fruit"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 7:15-23",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 7:15–23"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 12:33-37",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 12:33–37"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "43",
          "sid": "LUK 6:43"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "No good tree bears bad fruit, nor ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "does"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "a"
              ]
            },
            " bad tree bear good fruit. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "44",
              "sid": "LUK 6:44"
            },
            "For each tree is known by its own fruit. Indeed, figs are not gathered from thornbushes, nor grapes from brambles. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "45",
              "sid": "LUK 6:45"
            },
            "The good man brings good things out of the good treasure of his heart, and the evil ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "man"
              ]
            },
            " brings evil ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "things"
              ]
            },
            " out of the evil ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "treasure of his heart"
              ]
            },
            ". For out of the overflow of the heart the mouth speaks."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The House on the Rock"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 7:24-27",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 7:24–27"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "46",
          "sid": "LUK 6:46"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Why do you call Me ‘Lord, Lord,’ ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "but"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "do"
              ]
            },
            " not do what I say? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "47",
              "sid": "LUK 6:47"
            },
            "I will show you what he is like who comes to Me and hears My words and acts on them: ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "48",
              "sid": "LUK 6:48"
            },
            "He is like a man building a house, who dug down deep and laid ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "his"
              ]
            },
            " foundation on the rock. When ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " flood came, the torrent crashed against that house but could not shake it, because it was well built.",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "6:48 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "BYZ and TR "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "because its foundation was on the rock"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "; see ",
                    {
                      "type": "ref",
                      "loc": "MAT 7:25",
                      "content": [
                        "Matthew 7:25"
                      ]
                    },
                    "."
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "49",
          "sid": "LUK 6:49"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "But the ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "one who"
              ]
            },
            " hears ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "My words"
              ]
            },
            " and ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "does"
              ]
            },
            " not act on them is like a man who built ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "his"
              ]
            },
            " house on ground without ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "a"
              ]
            },
            " foundation. The torrent crashed against ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "that house"
              ]
            },
            ", and immediately it fell — and great was ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "its"
              ]
            },
            " destruction!”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "7",
      "sid": "LUK 7"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Faith of the Centurion"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 8:5-13",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 8:5–13"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JHN 4:43-54",
          "content": [
            "John 4:43–54"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "LUK 7:1"
        },
        "When ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " had concluded His discourse in the hearing of the people, He went to Capernaum. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "LUK 7:2"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "There"
          ]
        },
        " a highly valued servant of a centurion was sick ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " about to die. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "LUK 7:3"
        },
        "When ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the centurion"
          ]
        },
        " heard about Jesus, he sent ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "some"
          ]
        },
        " Jewish elders to ask Him to come ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " heal his servant. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "LUK 7:4"
        },
        "They came to Jesus ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " pleaded with Him earnestly, “",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "This man"
          ]
        },
        " is worthy to have You grant this, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "LUK 7:5"
        },
        "for he loves our nation and has built our synagogue.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "LUK 7:6"
        },
        "So Jesus went with them. But when He was not far from the house, the centurion sent friends with the message: “Lord, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "do"
          ]
        },
        " not trouble Yourself, for I am not worthy to have You come under my roof. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "LUK 7:7"
        },
        "That is why I did not consider myself worthy to come to You. But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "just"
          ]
        },
        " say ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " word, and my servant will be healed. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "LUK 7:8"
        },
        "For I ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "myself"
          ]
        },
        " am a man under authority, with soldiers under me. I tell ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "one"
          ]
        },
        " to go, and he goes, and another to come, and he comes. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "I tell"
          ]
        },
        " my servant to do ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "something"
          ]
        },
        ", and he does ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        ".”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "LUK 7:9"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " heard ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        ", ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He"
          ]
        },
        " marveled at ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the centurion"
          ]
        },
        ". Turning to the crowd following Him, He said, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“I tell you, not even in Israel have I found such great faith.”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "LUK 7:10"
        },
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " the messengers returned to the house, they found the servant in good health."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Jesus Raises a Widow’s Son"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "LUK 7:11"
        },
        "Soon afterward, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " went to a town called Nain. His disciples went with Him, accompanied by a large crowd. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "LUK 7:12"
        },
        "As He approached the town gate, He saw a dead man being carried out, the only son of his mother, and she was a widow. And a large crowd from the town was with her."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "LUK 7:13"
        },
        "When the Lord saw her, He had compassion on her and said, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "Do"
              ]
            },
            " not weep.”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "LUK 7:14"
        },
        "Then He went up ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " touched the coffin,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "7:14 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "bier"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                ", probably a wooden plank or open coffin"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " and those carrying it stood still. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Young man,”"
          ]
        },
        " He said, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“I tell you, get up!”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "LUK 7:15"
        },
        "And the dead ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "man"
          ]
        },
        " sat up and began to speak! Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " gave him ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "back"
          ]
        },
        " to his mother."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "LUK 7:16"
        },
        "A sense of awe swept over all ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of them"
          ]
        },
        ", and they glorified God. “A great prophet has appeared among us!” they said. “God has visited His people!” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "LUK 7:17"
        },
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " news about ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " spread throughout Judea and all the surrounding region."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "John’s Inquiry"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 11:1-6",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 11:1–6"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "LUK 7:18"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "John’s"
          ]
        },
        " disciples informed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " about all these things. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "LUK 7:19"
        },
        "So John called two of his disciples ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " sent ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " to ask the Lord, “Are You the One who was to come, or should we look for someone else?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "LUK 7:20"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " the men came to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        ", they said, “John the Baptist sent us to ask, ‘Are You the One who was to come, or should we look for someone else?’”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "LUK 7:21"
        },
        "At that very hour ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " healed many ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "people"
          ]
        },
        " of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " diseases, afflictions, and evil spirits, and He gave sight to many ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who were"
          ]
        },
        " blind. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "LUK 7:22"
        },
        "So He replied, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Go ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "back"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " report to John what you have seen and heard: ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "The"
              ]
            },
            " blind receive sight, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " lame walk, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " lepers",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "7:22 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "A "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "leper "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "was one afflicted with a skin disease. See Leviticus 13."
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            " are cleansed, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " deaf hear, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " dead are raised, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and the"
              ]
            },
            " good news is preached ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "to the"
              ]
            },
            " poor. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "23",
              "sid": "LUK 7:23"
            },
            "Blessed is the ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "one who"
              ]
            },
            " does not fall away on account of Me.",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "7:23 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "Or "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "who is not offended by Me"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Jesus Testifies about John"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAL 3:1-5",
          "content": [
            "Malachi 3:1–5"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 11:7-19",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 11:7–19"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "LUK 7:24"
        },
        "After John’s messengers had left, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " began to speak to the crowds about John: ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“What did you go out into the wilderness to see? A reed swaying in ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " wind? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "25",
              "sid": "LUK 7:25"
            },
            "Otherwise, what did you go out to see? A man dressed in fine clothes? Look, those who ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "wear"
              ]
            },
            " elegant clothing and live in luxury are found in palaces."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "LUK 7:26"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "What then did you go out to see? A prophet? Yes, I tell you, and more than a prophet. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "27",
              "sid": "LUK 7:27"
            },
            "This is the one about whom it is written:"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "‘Behold, I will send My messenger ahead of You,"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "who will prepare Your way before You.’",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "7:27 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "ref",
                      "loc": "MAL 3:1",
                      "content": [
                        "Malachi 3:1"
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "LUK 7:28"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "I tell you, among ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "those"
              ]
            },
            " born of women there is no one greater than John, yet even the least in the kingdom of God is greater than he.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "LUK 7:29"
        },
        "All the people ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who"
          ]
        },
        " heard ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        ", even the tax collectors, acknowledged God’s justice. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "For"
          ]
        },
        " they had received the baptism of John. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "LUK 7:30"
        },
        "But the Pharisees and experts in the law rejected God’s purpose for themselves, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "because"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "they had"
          ]
        },
        " not been baptized by ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "John"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "LUK 7:31"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“To what, then, can I compare the men of this generation? What are they like? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "32",
              "sid": "LUK 7:32"
            },
            "They are like children sitting in ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " marketplace and calling out to one another:"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "‘We played the flute for you,"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "and you did not dance;"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "we sang a dirge,"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "and you did not weep.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "LUK 7:33"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "For John the Baptist came neither eating bread nor drinking wine, and you say, ‘He has a demon!’ ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "34",
              "sid": "LUK 7:34"
            },
            "The Son of Man came eating and drinking, and you say, ‘Look ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "at this"
              ]
            },
            " glutton and drunkard, a friend of tax collectors and sinners!’ ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "35",
              "sid": "LUK 7:35"
            },
            "But wisdom is vindicated by all her children.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "A Sinful Woman Anoints Jesus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 26:6-13",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 26:6–13"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 14:3-9",
          "content": [
            "Mark 14:3–9"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JHN 12:1-8",
          "content": [
            "John 12:1–8"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "36",
          "sid": "LUK 7:36"
        },
        "Then one of the Pharisees invited ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " to eat with him, and He entered the Pharisee’s house ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " reclined at the table. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "LUK 7:37"
        },
        "When a sinful woman from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " town learned that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " was dining ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there"
          ]
        },
        ", she brought an alabaster jar of perfume. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "38",
          "sid": "LUK 7:38"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "As"
          ]
        },
        " she stood behind Him at His feet weeping, she began to wet His feet with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "her"
          ]
        },
        " tears and wipe ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " with her hair. Then she kissed His feet and anointed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " with the perfume."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "39",
          "sid": "LUK 7:39"
        },
        "When the Pharisee who had invited ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " saw ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        ", he said to himself, “If this ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "man"
          ]
        },
        " were a prophet, He would know who ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this is"
          ]
        },
        " and what kind of woman is touching Him — for she is a sinner!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "40",
          "sid": "LUK 7:40"
        },
        "But Jesus answered him, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Simon, I have something to tell you.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "“Tell ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "me"
          ]
        },
        ", Teacher,” he said."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "41",
              "sid": "LUK 7:41"
            },
            "“Two ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "men"
              ]
            },
            " were debtors to a certain moneylender. One owed ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "him"
              ]
            },
            " five hundred denarii,",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "7:41 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "A denarius was customarily a day’s wage for a laborer; see ",
                    {
                      "type": "ref",
                      "loc": "MAT 20:2",
                      "content": [
                        "Matthew 20:2"
                      ]
                    },
                    "."
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            " and the other fifty. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "42",
              "sid": "LUK 7:42"
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "When"
              ]
            },
            " they were unable to repay ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "him"
              ]
            },
            ", he forgave both ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "of them"
              ]
            },
            ". Which ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "one"
              ]
            },
            ", then, will love him more?”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "43",
          "sid": "LUK 7:43"
        },
        "“I suppose the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "one who"
          ]
        },
        " was forgiven more,” Simon replied."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“You have judged correctly,”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " said."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "44",
          "sid": "LUK 7:44"
        },
        "And turning toward the woman, He said to Simon, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Do you see this woman? ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "When"
              ]
            },
            " I entered your house, you did not give ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "Me"
              ]
            },
            " water for My feet, but she wet My feet with her tears and wiped ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "them"
              ]
            },
            " with her hair. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "45",
              "sid": "LUK 7:45"
            },
            "You did not greet Me with a kiss, but she has not stopped kissing My feet since I arrived. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "46",
              "sid": "LUK 7:46"
            },
            "You did not anoint My head with oil, but she has anointed My feet with perfume. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "47",
              "sid": "LUK 7:47"
            },
            "Therefore I tell you, her many sins have been forgiven, for she has loved much. But he who has been forgiven little loves little.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "48",
          "sid": "LUK 7:48"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " said to her, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Your sins are forgiven.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "49",
          "sid": "LUK 7:49"
        },
        "But those at the table began to say to themselves, “Who is this who even forgives sins?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "50",
          "sid": "LUK 7:50"
        },
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " told the woman, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Your faith has saved you; go in peace.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "8",
      "sid": "LUK 8"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Women Minister to Jesus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "LUK 8:1"
        },
        "Soon afterward, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " traveled from one town and village ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to another"
          ]
        },
        ", preaching and proclaiming the good news of the kingdom of God. The Twelve ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "were"
          ]
        },
        " with Him, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "LUK 8:2"
        },
        "as well as some women who had been healed of evil spirits and infirmities: Mary called Magdalene, from whom seven demons had gone out, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "LUK 8:3"
        },
        "Joanna ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " wife of Herod’s household manager Chuza, Susanna, and many others. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "These women"
          ]
        },
        " were ministering to them",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "8:3 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "TR "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "to Him"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " out of their own means."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Parable of the Sower"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 13:1-23",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 13:1–23"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 4:1-20",
          "content": [
            "Mark 4:1–20"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "LUK 8:4"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "While"
          ]
        },
        " a large crowd was gathering and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "people"
          ]
        },
        " were coming to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " from town after town, He told ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        " parable: ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "5",
              "sid": "LUK 8:5"
            },
            "“A farmer went out to sow his seed. And as he was sowing, some ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "seed"
              ]
            },
            " fell along the path, where it was trampled, and the birds of the air devoured it."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "LUK 8:6"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Some fell on rocky ground, and when it came up, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the seedlings"
              ]
            },
            " withered because they had no moisture."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "LUK 8:7"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Other ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "seed"
              ]
            },
            " fell among thorns, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "which"
              ]
            },
            " grew up with ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "it"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " choked ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the seedlings"
              ]
            },
            "."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "LUK 8:8"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Still other ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "seed"
              ]
            },
            " fell on good soil, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "where"
              ]
            },
            " it sprang up ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " produced a crop — a hundredfold.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "As ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " said ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        ", He called out, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“He who has ears to hear, let him hear.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "LUK 8:9"
        },
        "Then His disciples asked Him what this parable meant."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "LUK 8:10"
        },
        "He replied, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“The knowledge of the mysteries of the kingdom of God has been given to you, but to others ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "I speak"
              ]
            },
            " in parables, so that,"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "‘",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "though"
              ]
            },
            " seeing, they may not see;"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "though"
              ]
            },
            " hearing, they may not understand.’",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "8:10 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "ref",
                      "loc": "ISA 6:9",
                      "content": [
                        "Isaiah 6:9"
                      ]
                    },
                    " (See also LXX)"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "LUK 8:11"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Now this is the meaning of the parable: The seed is the word of God. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "12",
              "sid": "LUK 8:12"
            },
            "The  ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "seeds "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "8:12 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "Literally "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "the ones"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "; also in verses 13, 14, and 15"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            " along the path are those who hear, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "but"
              ]
            },
            " the devil comes and takes away the word from their hearts, so that they may not believe ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " be saved."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "LUK 8:13"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "The ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "seeds "
              ]
            },
            " on rocky ground ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "are"
              ]
            },
            " those who hear the word ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " receive it with joy, but ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "they"
              ]
            },
            " have no root. ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "They"
              ]
            },
            " believe for a season, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "but"
              ]
            },
            " in ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " time of testing, they fall away."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "LUK 8:14"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "The ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "seeds that "
              ]
            },
            " fell among the thorns are those who hear, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "but"
              ]
            },
            " as they go on their way, they are choked by ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " worries, riches, and pleasures of ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "this"
              ]
            },
            " life, and their fruit does not mature."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "LUK 8:15"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "But the ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "seeds"
              ]
            },
            " on good soil are those with a noble and good heart, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "who"
              ]
            },
            " hear the word, cling to ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "it"
              ]
            },
            ", and by persevering produce a crop."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Lesson of the Lamp"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 4:21-25",
          "content": [
            "Mark 4:21–25"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "LUK 8:16"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "No one lights a lamp ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " covers it with a jar or puts ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "it"
              ]
            },
            " under a bed. Instead, he sets ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "it"
              ]
            },
            " on a stand, so those who enter can see the light. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "17",
              "sid": "LUK 8:17"
            },
            "For there is nothing hidden that will not be disclosed, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " nothing concealed that will not be made known and brought to light."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "LUK 8:18"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Pay attention, therefore, to how you listen. Whoever has will be given ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "more"
              ]
            },
            ", ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "but"
              ]
            },
            " whoever does not have, even what he thinks he has will be taken away from him.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Jesus’ Mother and Brothers"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 12:46-50",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 12:46–50"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 3:31-35",
          "content": [
            "Mark 3:31–35"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "LUK 8:19"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus’"
          ]
        },
        " mother and brothers came to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "see"
          ]
        },
        " Him, but they were unable to reach Him because of the crowd. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "LUK 8:20"
        },
        "He was told, “Your mother and brothers are standing outside, wanting to see You.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "LUK 8:21"
        },
        "But He replied, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“My mother and brothers are those who hear the word of God and carry it out.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Jesus Calms the Storm"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "PSA 107:1-43",
          "content": [
            "Psalm 107:1–43"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 8:23-27",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 8:23–27"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 4:35-41",
          "content": [
            "Mark 4:35–41"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "LUK 8:22"
        },
        "One day ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " said to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His disciples"
          ]
        },
        ", ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Let us cross to the other side of the lake.”"
          ]
        },
        " So He got into a boat ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "with"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " and set out."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "LUK 8:23"
        },
        "As they sailed, He fell asleep, and a windstorm came down on the lake, so that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the boat"
          ]
        },
        " was being swamped, and they were in great danger. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "LUK 8:24"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "The disciples"
          ]
        },
        " went ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " woke Him, saying, “Master, Master, we are perishing!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " got up ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " rebuked the wind and the raging waters, and they subsided, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "all"
          ]
        },
        " was calm. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "25",
              "sid": "LUK 8:25"
            },
            "“Where is your faith?”"
          ]
        },
        " He asked."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "Frightened ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " amazed, they asked one another, “Who is this? He commands even the winds and the water, and they obey Him!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Demons and the Pigs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 8:28-34",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 8:28–34"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 5:1-20",
          "content": [
            "Mark 5:1–20"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "LUK 8:26"
        },
        "Then they sailed to the region of the Gerasenes,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "8:26 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "BYZ and TR "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Gadarenes"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; Tischendorf "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Gergesenes"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; also in verse 37"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " across ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the lake"
          ]
        },
        " from Galilee. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "LUK 8:27"
        },
        "When ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " stepped ashore, He was met by a demon-possessed man from the town. For a long time ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this man"
          ]
        },
        " had not worn clothing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " lived in a house, but ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "he stayed"
          ]
        },
        " in the tombs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "LUK 8:28"
        },
        "When ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the man"
          ]
        },
        " saw Jesus, he cried out ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " fell down before Him, shouting in a loud voice, “What do You ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "want"
          ]
        },
        " with me, Jesus, Son of the Most High God? I beg You not to torture me!” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "LUK 8:29"
        },
        "For ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " had commanded the unclean spirit to come out of the man. Many times it had seized him, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "though"
          ]
        },
        " he was bound with chains and shackles, he had broken the chains ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " been driven by the demon into solitary places."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "30",
              "sid": "LUK 8:30"
            },
            "“What is your name?”"
          ]
        },
        " Jesus asked."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "“Legion,” he replied, because many demons had gone into him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "LUK 8:31"
        },
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the demons"
          ]
        },
        " kept begging ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " not to order them to go into the Abyss."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "LUK 8:32"
        },
        "There on the hillside a large herd of pigs was feeding. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the demons"
          ]
        },
        " begged ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " to let them enter ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the pigs"
          ]
        },
        ", and He gave them permission."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "LUK 8:33"
        },
        "Then the demons came out of the man ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " went into the pigs, and the herd rushed down the steep bank into the lake and was drowned."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "LUK 8:34"
        },
        "When those tending ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the pigs"
          ]
        },
        " saw what had happened, they ran off and reported ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        " in the town and countryside. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "LUK 8:35"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the people"
          ]
        },
        " went out to see what had happened. They came to Jesus and found the man whom the demons had left, sitting at Jesus’ feet, clothed and in his right mind; and they were afraid. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "36",
          "sid": "LUK 8:36"
        },
        "Meanwhile, those who had seen ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        " reported how the demon-possessed man had been healed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "LUK 8:37"
        },
        "Then all the people of the region of the Gerasenes asked ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " to depart from them, because great fear had taken hold of them. So He got into the boat ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " started back."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "38",
          "sid": "LUK 8:38"
        },
        "The man whom the demons had left begged to go with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        ". But He sent him away, saying, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "39",
              "sid": "LUK 8:39"
            },
            "“Return home and describe how much God has done for you.”"
          ]
        },
        " So ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the man"
          ]
        },
        " went away ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " proclaimed all over the town how much Jesus had done for him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Healing Touch of Jesus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 9:18-26",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 9:18–26"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 5:21-43",
          "content": [
            "Mark 5:21–43"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "40",
          "sid": "LUK 8:40"
        },
        "When Jesus returned, the crowd welcomed Him, for they had all been waiting for Him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "41",
          "sid": "LUK 8:41"
        },
        "Just then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "a"
          ]
        },
        " synagogue leader named Jairus came and fell at Jesus’ feet. He begged Him to come to his house, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "42",
          "sid": "LUK 8:42"
        },
        "because his only daughter, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who was"
          ]
        },
        " about twelve, was dying."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "As ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " went ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "with him"
          ]
        },
        ", the crowds pressed around Him, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "43",
          "sid": "LUK 8:43"
        },
        "including a woman who had suffered from bleeding for twelve years. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "She"
          ]
        },
        " had spent all her money on physicians,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "8:43 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "NE and WH do not include "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "She had spent all her money on physicians"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "but"
          ]
        },
        " no one was able to heal ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "her"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "44",
          "sid": "LUK 8:44"
        },
        "She came up behind ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " touched the fringe of His cloak, and immediately her bleeding stopped."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "45",
              "sid": "LUK 8:45"
            },
            "“Who touched Me?”"
          ]
        },
        " Jesus asked."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "But they all denied ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        ". “Master,” said Peter,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "8:45 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "BYZ and TR include "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "and those who were with him"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " “the people are crowding and pressing against You.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "46",
          "sid": "LUK 8:46"
        },
        "But Jesus declared, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Someone touched Me, for I know that power has gone out from Me.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "47",
          "sid": "LUK 8:47"
        },
        "Then the woman, seeing that she could not escape notice, came trembling and fell down before Him. In the presence of all the people, she explained why she had touched Him and how she had immediately been healed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "48",
              "sid": "LUK 8:48"
            },
            "“Daughter,”"
          ]
        },
        " said ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        ", ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“your faith has healed you. Go in peace.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "49",
          "sid": "LUK 8:49"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "While"
          ]
        },
        " He ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "was"
          ]
        },
        " still speaking, someone arrived from the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "house of"
          ]
        },
        " the synagogue leader. “Your daughter is dead,” he told ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jairus"
          ]
        },
        ". “",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Do not"
          ]
        },
        " bother the Teacher ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "anymore"
          ]
        },
        ".”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "50",
          "sid": "LUK 8:50"
        },
        "But Jesus overheard ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jairus"
          ]
        },
        ", ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "Do"
              ]
            },
            " not be afraid; just believe, and she will be healed.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "51",
          "sid": "LUK 8:51"
        },
        "When He entered the house, He did not allow anyone to go in with Him except Peter, John, James, and the child’s father and mother. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "52",
          "sid": "LUK 8:52"
        },
        "Meanwhile, everyone was weeping and mourning for her. But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " said, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Stop weeping; she is not dead but asleep.”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "53",
          "sid": "LUK 8:53"
        },
        "And they laughed at Him, knowing that she was dead."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "54",
          "sid": "LUK 8:54"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " took her by the hand ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " called out, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Child, get up!”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "55",
          "sid": "LUK 8:55"
        },
        "Her spirit returned, and at once she got up. And He directed that she be given ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "something"
          ]
        },
        " to eat. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "56",
          "sid": "LUK 8:56"
        },
        "Her parents were astounded, but ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " ordered them ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "not"
          ]
        },
        " to tell ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "anyone"
          ]
        },
        " what had happened."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "9",
      "sid": "LUK 9"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Ministry of the Twelve"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 10:5-15",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 10:5–15"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 6:7-13",
          "content": [
            "Mark 6:7–13"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "LUK 9:1"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " called the Twelve",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "9:1 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "TR "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "His twelve disciples"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "together"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " gave them power and authority over all demons, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "power "
          ]
        },
        " to cure diseases. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "LUK 9:2"
        },
        "And He sent them out to proclaim the kingdom of God and to heal the sick. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "3",
              "sid": "LUK 9:3"
            },
            "“Take nothing for the journey,”"
          ]
        },
        " He told them, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“no staff, no bag, no bread, no money,",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "9:3 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "Or "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "silver coins"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            " no second tunic. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "4",
              "sid": "LUK 9:4"
            },
            "Whatever house you enter, stay there ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "until"
              ]
            },
            " you leave that area. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "5",
              "sid": "LUK 9:5"
            },
            "If anyone does not welcome you, shake the dust off your feet when you leave that town, as a testimony against them.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "LUK 9:6"
        },
        "So they set out and went from village to village, preaching the gospel and healing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "people"
          ]
        },
        " everywhere."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Herod Tries to See Jesus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 14:1-12",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 14:1–12"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 6:14-29",
          "content": [
            "Mark 6:14–29"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "LUK 9:7"
        },
        "When Herod the tetrarch heard about all that was happening, he was perplexed. For some were saying that John had risen from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " dead, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "LUK 9:8"
        },
        "others that Elijah had appeared, and still others that a prophet of old had arisen."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "LUK 9:9"
        },
        "“I beheaded John,” Herod said, “but who is this ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "man"
          ]
        },
        " I hear such things about?” And he kept trying to see ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Feeding of the Five Thousand"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 14:13-21",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 14:13–21"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 6:30-44",
          "content": [
            "Mark 6:30–44"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JHN 6:1-15",
          "content": [
            "John 6:1–15"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "LUK 9:10"
        },
        "Then the apostles returned ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " reported to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " all that they had done. Taking them ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "away"
          ]
        },
        " privately, He withdrew to a town called Bethsaida. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "LUK 9:11"
        },
        "But the crowds found out ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " followed Him. He welcomed them ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " spoke to them about the kingdom of God, and He healed those who needed healing."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "LUK 9:12"
        },
        "As the day neared its end, the Twelve came to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, “Dismiss the crowd so they can go to the surrounding villages and countryside for lodging and provisions. For we are in a desolate place here.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "LUK 9:13"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " told them, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“You give them something to eat.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "“We have only five loaves of bread and two fish,” they answered, “unless we go ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " buy food for all these people.” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "LUK 9:14"
        },
        "(There were about five thousand men.)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "He told His disciples, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Have them sit down in groups of about fifty ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "each"
              ]
            },
            ".”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "LUK 9:15"
        },
        "They did so, and everyone was seated."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "LUK 9:16"
        },
        "Taking the five loaves and the two fish ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " looking up to heaven, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " spoke a blessing and broke them. Then He gave ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " to the disciples to set before the people."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "LUK 9:17"
        },
        "They all ate and were satisfied, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the disciples"
          ]
        },
        " picked up twelve basketfuls of broken pieces that were left over."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Peter’s Confession of Christ"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 16:13-20",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 16:13–20"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 8:27-30",
          "content": [
            "Mark 8:27–30"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JHN 6:67-71",
          "content": [
            "John 6:67–71"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "LUK 9:18"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "One day"
          ]
        },
        " as ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " was praying in private ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " the disciples were with Him, He questioned them: ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Who ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "do"
              ]
            },
            " the crowds say I am?”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "LUK 9:19"
        },
        "They replied, “",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Some say"
          ]
        },
        " John the Baptist; others ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "say"
          ]
        },
        " Elijah; and still others, that a prophet of old has arisen.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "20",
              "sid": "LUK 9:20"
            },
            "“But ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "what about"
              ]
            },
            " you?”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " asked. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Who do you say I am?”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "Peter answered, “The Christ of God.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Christ’s Passion Foretold"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 16:21-23",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 16:21–23"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 8:31-33",
          "content": [
            "Mark 8:31–33"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "LUK 9:21"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " strictly warned them ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "not"
          ]
        },
        " to tell this to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "anyone"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "22",
              "sid": "LUK 9:22"
            },
            "“The Son of Man must suffer many things,”"
          ]
        },
        " He said. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“He must be rejected by the elders, chief priests, and scribes, and He must be killed and on the third day be raised to life.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Take Up Your Cross"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 16:24-28",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 16:24–28"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 8:34-38",
          "content": [
            "Mark 8:34–38"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "LUK 9:23"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " said to all of them, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“If anyone wants to come after Me, he must deny himself and take up his cross daily and follow Me. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "24",
              "sid": "LUK 9:24"
            },
            "For whoever wants to save his life will lose it, but whoever loses his life for My sake will save it."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "LUK 9:25"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "What does it profit a man to gain the whole world, yet lose or forfeit his very self? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "26",
              "sid": "LUK 9:26"
            },
            "If anyone is ashamed of Me and My words, the Son of Man will be ashamed of him when He comes in His glory and ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "in the glory"
              ]
            },
            " of the Father and of the holy angels. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "27",
              "sid": "LUK 9:27"
            },
            "But I tell you truly, some who are standing here will not taste death before they see the kingdom of God.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Transfiguration"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 17:1-13",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 17:1–13"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 9:1-13",
          "content": [
            "Mark 9:1–13"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "2PE 1:16-21",
          "content": [
            "2 Peter 1:16–21"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "LUK 9:28"
        },
        "About eight days after ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " had said these things, He took with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        " Peter, John, and James, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " went up on a mountain to pray. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "LUK 9:29"
        },
        "And as He was praying, the appearance of His face changed, and His clothes became radiantly white. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "LUK 9:30"
        },
        "Suddenly two men, Moses and Elijah, began talking with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "LUK 9:31"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "They"
          ]
        },
        " appeared in glory ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " spoke about His departure, which He was about to accomplish at Jerusalem."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "LUK 9:32"
        },
        "Meanwhile Peter and his companions were overcome by sleep, but when they awoke, they saw ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus’"
          ]
        },
        " glory and the two men standing with Him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "LUK 9:33"
        },
        "As ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Moses and Elijah"
          ]
        },
        " were leaving, Peter said to Jesus, “Master, it is good for us to be here. Let us put up three shelters",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "9:33 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "three tabernacles"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "— one for You, one for Moses, and one for Elijah.” (He did not know what he was saying.)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "LUK 9:34"
        },
        "While ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Peter"
          ]
        },
        " was speaking, a cloud appeared and enveloped them, and they were afraid as they entered the cloud. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "LUK 9:35"
        },
        "And a voice came from the cloud, saying, “This is My Son, whom I have chosen.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "9:35 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "BYZ and TR "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "This is My beloved Son"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; see ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "MAT 17:5",
                  "content": [
                    "Matthew 17:5"
                  ]
                },
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " Listen to Him!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "36",
          "sid": "LUK 9:36"
        },
        "After the voice had spoken, only Jesus was present ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "with them"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "The disciples"
          ]
        },
        " kept this to themselves, and in those days they did not tell anyone what they had seen."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Boy with an Evil Spirit"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 17:14-18",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 17:14–18"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 9:14-29",
          "content": [
            "Mark 9:14–29"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "LUK 9:37"
        },
        "The next day, when they came down from the mountain, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " was met by a large crowd. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "38",
          "sid": "LUK 9:38"
        },
        "Suddenly a man in the crowd cried out, “Teacher, I beg You to look at my son, for he is my only child. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "39",
          "sid": "LUK 9:39"
        },
        "A spirit keeps seizing him, and he screams abruptly. It throws him into convulsions ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "so that"
          ]
        },
        " he foams at the mouth. It keeps mauling him ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " rarely departs from him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "40",
          "sid": "LUK 9:40"
        },
        "I begged Your disciples to drive it out, but they were unable.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "41",
              "sid": "LUK 9:41"
            },
            "“O unbelieving and perverse generation!”"
          ]
        },
        " Jesus replied. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“How long must I remain with you and put up with you? Bring your son here.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "42",
          "sid": "LUK 9:42"
        },
        "Even while ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the boy"
          ]
        },
        " was approaching, the demon slammed him to the ground in a convulsion. But Jesus rebuked the unclean spirit, healed the boy, and gave him back to his father."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Second Prediction of the Passion"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 17:22-23",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 17:22–23"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 9:30-32",
          "content": [
            "Mark 9:30–32"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "43",
          "sid": "LUK 9:43"
        },
        "And they were all astonished at the greatness of God."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "While everyone was marveling at all that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " was doing, He said to His disciples, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "44",
              "sid": "LUK 9:44"
            },
            "“",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "Let"
              ]
            },
            " these words sink into your ears: The Son of Man is about to be delivered into ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " hands of men.”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "45",
          "sid": "LUK 9:45"
        },
        "But they did not understand this statement. It was veiled from them so that they could not comprehend it, and they were afraid to ask Him about ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Greatest in the Kingdom"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 18:1-5",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 18:1–5"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 9:33-41",
          "content": [
            "Mark 9:33–41"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "46",
          "sid": "LUK 9:46"
        },
        "Then an argument started among ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the disciples"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "as to"
          ]
        },
        " which of them would be ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " greatest. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "47",
          "sid": "LUK 9:47"
        },
        "But Jesus, knowing the thoughts of their hearts, had a little child ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "stand"
          ]
        },
        " beside Him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "48",
          "sid": "LUK 9:48"
        },
        "And He said to them, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Whoever welcomes this little child in My name welcomes Me, and whoever welcomes Me welcomes the ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "One who"
              ]
            },
            " sent Me. For whoever is ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " least among all of you, he is ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " greatest.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "49",
          "sid": "LUK 9:49"
        },
        "“Master,” said John, “we saw someone driving out demons in Your name, and we tried to stop him, because he does not accompany us.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "50",
              "sid": "LUK 9:50"
            },
            "“",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "Do"
              ]
            },
            " not stop ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "him"
              ]
            },
            ",”"
          ]
        },
        " Jesus replied, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“for whoever is not against you is for you.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Samaritans Reject Jesus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "51",
          "sid": "LUK 9:51"
        },
        "As the day of His ascension approached, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " resolutely set out for Jerusalem. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "52",
          "sid": "LUK 9:52"
        },
        "He sent messengers on ahead, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who"
          ]
        },
        " went into a village of the Samaritans to make arrangements for Him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "53",
          "sid": "LUK 9:53"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the people there"
          ]
        },
        " refused to welcome Him, because He was heading for Jerusalem."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "54",
          "sid": "LUK 9:54"
        },
        "When the disciples James and John saw ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        ", they asked, “Lord, do You want us to call down fire from heaven",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "9:54 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "BYZ and TR "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "from heaven, just as Elijah did"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; see ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "2KI 1:10-12",
                  "content": [
                    "2 Kings 1:10–12"
                  ]
                },
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " to consume them?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "55",
          "sid": "LUK 9:55"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " turned ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " rebuked them.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "9:55 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "BYZ and TR include "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "and He said, “You do not know what kind of spirit you are of. ",
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fv",
                  "content": [
                    "56"
                  ]
                },
                "For the Son of Man did not come to destroy the lives of men, but to save them.”"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "56",
          "sid": "LUK 9:56"
        },
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He and His disciples"
          ]
        },
        " went on to another village."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Cost of Discipleship"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 8:18-22",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 8:18–22"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "LUK 14:25-33",
          "content": [
            "Luke 14:25–33"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JHN 6:59-66",
          "content": [
            "John 6:59–66"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "57",
          "sid": "LUK 9:57"
        },
        "As they were walking along the road, someone said to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        ", “I will follow You wherever You go.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "58",
          "sid": "LUK 9:58"
        },
        "Jesus replied, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Foxes have dens and birds of the air ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "have"
              ]
            },
            " nests, but the Son of Man has no place to lay ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "His"
              ]
            },
            " head.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "59",
          "sid": "LUK 9:59"
        },
        "Then He said to another ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "man"
          ]
        },
        ", ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Follow Me.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "The man"
          ]
        },
        " replied, “Lord, first let me go ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " bury my father.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "60",
          "sid": "LUK 9:60"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " told him, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Let the dead bury their own dead. You, however, go ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " proclaim the kingdom of God.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "61",
          "sid": "LUK 9:61"
        },
        "Still another said, “I will follow You, Lord; but first let me bid farewell to my family.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "62",
          "sid": "LUK 9:62"
        },
        "Then Jesus declared, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“No one who puts ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "his"
              ]
            },
            " hand to ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " plow and then looks back is fit for the kingdom of God.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "10",
      "sid": "LUK 10"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Jesus Sends the Seventy-Two"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 9:35-38",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 9:35–38"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "LUK 10:1"
        },
        "After this, the Lord appointed seventy-two",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "10:1 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "NE, BYZ, and TR "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "seventy"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; also in verse 17"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " others and sent them two by two ahead of Him to every town and place He was about to visit. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "LUK 10:2"
        },
        "And He told them, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“The harvest ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "is"
              ]
            },
            " plentiful, but the workers ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "are"
              ]
            },
            " few. Ask the Lord of the harvest, therefore, to send out workers into His harvest."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "LUK 10:3"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Go! I am sending you out like lambs among wolves. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "4",
              "sid": "LUK 10:4"
            },
            "Carry no purse ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "or"
              ]
            },
            " bag ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "or"
              ]
            },
            " sandals. Do not greet ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "anyone"
              ]
            },
            " along the road."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "LUK 10:5"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Whatever house you enter, begin by saying, ‘Peace to this house.’ ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "6",
              "sid": "LUK 10:6"
            },
            "If a man of peace is there, your peace will rest on him; if not, it will return to you. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "7",
              "sid": "LUK 10:7"
            },
            "Stay at the same house, eating and drinking whatever you are ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "offered"
              ]
            },
            ". For the worker ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "is"
              ]
            },
            " worthy of his wages.",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "10:7 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "See ",
                    {
                      "type": "ref",
                      "loc": "LEV 19:13",
                      "content": [
                        "Leviticus 19:13"
                      ]
                    },
                    " and Deuteronomy 24:14–15; cited in 1 Timothy 5:18."
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "Do"
              ]
            },
            " not move around from house to house."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "LUK 10:8"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "If you enter a town and they welcome you, eat whatever is set before you. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "9",
              "sid": "LUK 10:9"
            },
            "Heal the sick ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "who are there"
              ]
            },
            " and tell them, ‘The kingdom of God is near you.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "LUK 10:10"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "But if you enter a town and they do not welcome you, go into the streets ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " declare, ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "11",
              "sid": "LUK 10:11"
            },
            "‘Even the dust of your town that clings to our feet, we wipe off as a testimony against you. Yet be sure of this: The kingdom of God is near.’ ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "12",
              "sid": "LUK 10:12"
            },
            "I tell you, it will be more bearable on that day for Sodom than for that town."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Woe to the Unrepentant"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 11:20-24",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 11:20–24"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "LUK 10:13"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Woe to you, Chorazin! Woe to you, Bethsaida! For if the miracles ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "that"
              ]
            },
            " were performed in you had been performed in Tyre and Sidon, they would have repented long ago, sitting in sackcloth and ashes. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "14",
              "sid": "LUK 10:14"
            },
            "But it will be more bearable for Tyre and Sidon at the judgment than for you."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "LUK 10:15"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "And you, Capernaum, will you be lifted up to heaven? No, you will be brought down to Hades!"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "LUK 10:16"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Whoever listens to you listens to Me; whoever rejects you rejects Me; and whoever rejects Me rejects the ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "One who"
              ]
            },
            " sent Me.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Joyful Return"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "LUK 10:17"
        },
        "The seventy-two returned with joy ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, “Lord, even the demons submit to us in Your name.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "LUK 10:18"
        },
        "So He told them, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“I saw Satan fall like lightning from heaven. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "19",
              "sid": "LUK 10:19"
            },
            "Behold, I have given you authority to tread on snakes and scorpions, and over all the power of the enemy. Nothing will harm you. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "20",
              "sid": "LUK 10:20"
            },
            "Nevertheless, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "do"
              ]
            },
            " not rejoice that the spirits submit to you, but rejoice that your names are written in heaven.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Jesus’ Prayer of Thanksgiving"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 11:25-30",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 11:25–30"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "LUK 10:21"
        },
        "At that time ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " rejoiced in the Holy Spirit and declared, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“I praise You, Father, Lord of heaven and earth, because You have hidden these things from ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " wise and learned, and revealed them to little children. Yes, Father, for this was well-pleasing in Your sight."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "LUK 10:22"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "All things have been entrusted to Me by My Father. No one knows who the Son is except the Father, and ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "no one knows"
              ]
            },
            " who the Father is except the Son and those to whom the Son chooses to reveal ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "Him"
              ]
            },
            ".”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "LUK 10:23"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " turned to the disciples ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said privately, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Blessed ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "are"
              ]
            },
            " the eyes that see what you see. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "24",
              "sid": "LUK 10:24"
            },
            "For I tell you that many prophets and kings desired to see what you see ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "but"
              ]
            },
            " did not see ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "it"
              ]
            },
            ", and to hear what you hear ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "but"
              ]
            },
            " did not hear ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "it"
              ]
            },
            ".”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Parable of the Good Samaritan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "LUK 10:25"
        },
        "One day an expert in the law stood up to test Him. “Teacher,” he asked, “what must I do to inherit eternal life?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "26",
              "sid": "LUK 10:26"
            },
            "“What is written in the Law?”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " replied. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“How do you read ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "it"
              ]
            },
            "?”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "LUK 10:27"
        },
        "He answered, “‘Love ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord your God with all your heart and with all your soul and with all your strength and with all your mind’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "10:27 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "DEU 6:5",
                  "content": [
                    "Deuteronomy 6:5"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " and ‘",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Love"
          ]
        },
        " your neighbor as yourself.’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "10:27 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "LEV 19:18",
                  "content": [
                    "Leviticus 19:18"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "28",
              "sid": "LUK 10:28"
            },
            "“You have answered correctly,”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " said. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Do this and you will live.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "LUK 10:29"
        },
        "But wanting to justify himself, he asked Jesus, “And who is my neighbor?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "LUK 10:30"
        },
        "Jesus took up ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this question"
          ]
        },
        " and said, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“A man was going down from Jerusalem to Jericho when he fell into the hands of robbers. ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "They"
              ]
            },
            " stripped ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "him"
              ]
            },
            ", beat him, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " went away, leaving ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "him"
              ]
            },
            " half dead."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "LUK 10:31"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Now by chance a priest was going down the same road, but when he saw him, he passed by on the other side."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "LUK 10:32"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "So too, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "when"
              ]
            },
            " a Levite came to that spot and saw ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "him"
              ]
            },
            ", he passed by on the other side."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "LUK 10:33"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "But a Samaritan on a journey came upon him, and when he saw ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "him"
              ]
            },
            ", he had compassion. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "34",
              "sid": "LUK 10:34"
            },
            "He went to ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "him"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " bandaged his wounds, pouring on oil and wine. Then he put him on his own animal, brought him to an inn, and took care of him."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "LUK 10:35"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "The next day he took out two denarii",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "10:35 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "A denarius was customarily a day’s wage for a laborer; see ",
                    {
                      "type": "ref",
                      "loc": "MAT 20:2",
                      "content": [
                        "Matthew 20:2"
                      ]
                    },
                    "."
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " gave ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "them"
              ]
            },
            " to the innkeeper. ‘Take care of him,’ he said, ‘and on my return I will repay you for any additional expense.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "36",
          "sid": "LUK 10:36"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Which of these three ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "do"
              ]
            },
            " you think was a neighbor to the ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "man"
              ]
            },
            " who fell into the hands of robbers?”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "LUK 10:37"
        },
        "“The ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "one"
          ]
        },
        " who showed him mercy,” replied ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the expert in the law"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "Then Jesus told him, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Go and do likewise.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Martha and Mary"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "38",
          "sid": "LUK 10:38"
        },
        "As they traveled along, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " entered a village ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "where"
          ]
        },
        " a woman named Martha welcomed Him into ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "her"
          ]
        },
        " home. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "39",
          "sid": "LUK 10:39"
        },
        "She had a sister named Mary, who sat at the Lord’s feet listening to His message. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "40",
          "sid": "LUK 10:40"
        },
        "But Martha was distracted by all the preparations ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to be made"
          ]
        },
        ". She came to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, “Lord, do You not care that my sister has left me to serve alone? Tell her to help me!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "41",
              "sid": "LUK 10:41"
            },
            "“Martha, Martha,”"
          ]
        },
        " the Lord replied, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“you are worried and upset about many things. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "42",
              "sid": "LUK 10:42"
            },
            "But only one thing is necessary. Mary has chosen the good portion, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and it"
              ]
            },
            " will not be taken away from her.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "11",
      "sid": "LUK 11"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Lord’s Prayer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 6:5-15",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 6:5–15"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "LUK 11:1"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "One day"
          ]
        },
        " in a place where ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " had just finished praying, one of His disciples requested, “Lord, teach us to pray, just as John taught his disciples.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "LUK 11:2"
        },
        "So ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " told them, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“When you pray, say:"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "‘Father,",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "11:2 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "BYZ and TR "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "Our Father in heaven"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "; see ",
                    {
                      "type": "ref",
                      "loc": "MAT 6:9",
                      "content": [
                        "Matthew 6:9"
                      ]
                    },
                    "."
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            " hallowed be Your name."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Your kingdom come.",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "11:2 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "BYZ and TR include "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "Your will be done, on earth as it is in heaven"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "; see ",
                    {
                      "type": "ref",
                      "loc": "MAT 6:10",
                      "content": [
                        "Matthew 6:10"
                      ]
                    },
                    "."
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "LUK 11:3"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Give us each day our daily bread."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "LUK 11:4"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "And forgive us our sins,"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "for we also forgive everyone who sins against us."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "And lead us not into temptation.",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "11:4 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "BYZ and TR include "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "but deliver us from the evil one"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "; see ",
                    {
                      "type": "ref",
                      "loc": "MAT 6:13",
                      "content": [
                        "Matthew 6:13"
                      ]
                    },
                    "."
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "’”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Ask, Seek, Knock"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 7:7-12",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 7:7–12"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "LUK 11:5"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " said to them, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "Suppose one"
              ]
            },
            " of you goes to ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "his"
              ]
            },
            " friend at midnight and says, ‘Friend, lend me three loaves ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "of bread"
              ]
            },
            ", ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "6",
              "sid": "LUK 11:6"
            },
            "because ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "a"
              ]
            },
            " friend of mine has come to me on a journey, and I have nothing to set before him.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "LUK 11:7"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "And ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "suppose the one"
              ]
            },
            " inside answers, ‘",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "Do"
              ]
            },
            " not bother me. ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "My"
              ]
            },
            " door ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "is"
              ]
            },
            " already shut, and my children and I are in bed. I cannot get up to give you ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "anything"
              ]
            },
            ".’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "LUK 11:8"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "I tell you, even though he will not get up to provide for him because of his friendship, yet because of ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the man’s"
              ]
            },
            " persistence, he will get up ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " give him as much as he needs."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "LUK 11:9"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "So I tell you: Ask, and it will be given to you; seek, and you will find; knock, and ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the door"
              ]
            },
            " will be opened to you. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "10",
              "sid": "LUK 11:10"
            },
            "For everyone who asks receives; he who seeks finds; and to him who knocks, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the door"
              ]
            },
            " will be opened."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "LUK 11:11"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "What father among you, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "if his"
              ]
            },
            " son asks for a fish,",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "11:11 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "BYZ and TR "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "if his son asks for bread, will give him a stone, or for a fish"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "; see ",
                    {
                      "type": "ref",
                      "loc": "MAT 7:9-10",
                      "content": [
                        "Matthew 7:9–10"
                      ]
                    },
                    "."
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            " will give him a snake instead? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "12",
              "sid": "LUK 11:12"
            },
            "Or ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "if"
              ]
            },
            " he asks for an egg, will give him a scorpion? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "13",
              "sid": "LUK 11:13"
            },
            "So if you who are evil know how to give good gifts to your children, how much more ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "will"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "your"
              ]
            },
            " Father in heaven give ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " Holy Spirit to those who ask Him!”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "A House Divided"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 12:22-30",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 12:22–30"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 3:20-27",
          "content": [
            "Mark 3:20–27"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "LUK 11:14"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "One day"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " was driving out a demon that was mute. And when the demon was gone, the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "man who had been"
          ]
        },
        " mute spoke. The crowds were amazed, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "LUK 11:15"
        },
        "but some of them said, “",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "It is"
          ]
        },
        " by Beelzebul,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "11:15 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "WH "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Beezeboul"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; Vulgate "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Beelzebub"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; also in verses 18 and 19"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " the prince of the demons, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " He drives out demons.” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "LUK 11:16"
        },
        "And others tested Him by demanding a sign from heaven."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "LUK 11:17"
        },
        "Knowing their thoughts, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " said to them, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Every kingdom divided against itself will be laid waste, and a house divided against a house will fall. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "18",
              "sid": "LUK 11:18"
            },
            "If Satan is divided against himself, how ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "can"
              ]
            },
            " his kingdom stand? After all, you say that I drive out demons by Beelzebul. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "19",
              "sid": "LUK 11:19"
            },
            "And if I drive out demons by Beelzebul, by whom ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "do"
              ]
            },
            " your sons drive ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "them"
              ]
            },
            " out? So then, they will be your judges. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "20",
              "sid": "LUK 11:20"
            },
            "But if I drive out demons by ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " finger of God, then the kingdom of God has come upon you."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "LUK 11:21"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "When a strong ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "man"
              ]
            },
            ", fully armed, guards his house, his possessions are secure. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "22",
              "sid": "LUK 11:22"
            },
            "But when ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "someone"
              ]
            },
            " stronger attacks ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " overpowers him, he takes away ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " armor in which ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the man"
              ]
            },
            " trusted, and ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "then"
              ]
            },
            " he divides up his plunder."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "LUK 11:23"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "He who is not with Me is against Me, and he who does not gather with Me scatters."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "An Unclean Spirit Returns"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 12:43-45",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 12:43–45"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "LUK 11:24"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "When an unclean spirit comes out of a man, it passes through arid places seeking rest and does not find ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "it"
              ]
            },
            ". Then it says, ‘I will return to ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " house I left.’ ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "25",
              "sid": "LUK 11:25"
            },
            "On its return, it finds ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the house"
              ]
            },
            " swept clean and put in order. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "26",
              "sid": "LUK 11:26"
            },
            "Then it goes and brings seven other spirits more wicked than itself, and they go in ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " dwell there. And the final ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "plight"
              ]
            },
            " of that man is worse than the first.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "True Blessedness"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "LUK 11:27"
        },
        "As ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " was saying these things, a woman in the crowd raised ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "her"
          ]
        },
        " voice ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, “Blessed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " the womb that bore You, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "blessed are"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " breasts that nursed You!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "LUK 11:28"
        },
        "But He replied, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Blessed rather ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "are"
              ]
            },
            " those who hear the word of God and obey it.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Sign of Jonah"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JON 3:1-10",
          "content": [
            "Jonah 3:1–10"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 12:38-42",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 12:38–42"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "LUK 11:29"
        },
        "As the crowds were increasing, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " said, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“This is a wicked generation. It demands a sign, but none will be given it except the sign of Jonah. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "30",
              "sid": "LUK 11:30"
            },
            "For as Jonah was a sign to the Ninevites, so the Son of Man will be ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "a sign"
              ]
            },
            " to this generation."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "LUK 11:31"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "The Queen of ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " South will rise at the judgment with the men of this generation and condemn them; for she came from the ends of the earth to hear the wisdom of Solomon, and now ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "One"
              ]
            },
            " greater than Solomon ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "is"
              ]
            },
            " here. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "32",
              "sid": "LUK 11:32"
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "The"
              ]
            },
            " men of Nineveh will stand at the judgment with this generation and condemn it; for they repented at the preaching of Jonah, and now ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "One"
              ]
            },
            " greater than Jonah ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "is"
              ]
            },
            " here."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Lamp of the Body"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 6:22-24",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 6:22–24"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "LUK 11:33"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "No one lights a lamp ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " puts it in a cellar ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "or"
              ]
            },
            " under a basket. Instead, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "he sets it"
              ]
            },
            " on a stand, so those who enter can see the light."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "LUK 11:34"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Your eye is the lamp of your body. When your eyes are good,",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "11:34 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "Literally "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "When your eye is sound"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "; see ",
                    {
                      "type": "ref",
                      "loc": "PRO 22:9",
                      "content": [
                        "Proverbs 22:9"
                      ]
                    },
                    "."
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            " your whole body also is full of light. But when they are bad,",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "11:34 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "Literally "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "when it is evil"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "; see ",
                    {
                      "type": "ref",
                      "loc": "PRO 23:6",
                      "content": [
                        "Proverbs 23:6"
                      ]
                    },
                    " and Proverbs 28:22."
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            " your body ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "is"
              ]
            },
            " full of darkness. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "35",
              "sid": "LUK 11:35"
            },
            "Be careful, then, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "that"
              ]
            },
            " the light within you is not darkness. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "36",
              "sid": "LUK 11:36"
            },
            "So if your ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "whole"
              ]
            },
            " body ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "is"
              ]
            },
            " full of light, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "with"
              ]
            },
            " no part ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "of it"
              ]
            },
            " in darkness, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "you"
              ]
            },
            " will be radiant, as though a lamp were shining on you.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Woes to Pharisees and Experts in the Law"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 23:1-36",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 23:1–36"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "LUK 11:37"
        },
        "As ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " was speaking, a Pharisee invited Him to dine with him; ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "so"
          ]
        },
        " He went in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " reclined at the table. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "38",
          "sid": "LUK 11:38"
        },
        "But the Pharisee was surprised to see that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " did not first wash before the meal."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "39",
          "sid": "LUK 11:39"
        },
        "Then the Lord said, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Now you Pharisees clean the outside of the cup and dish, but inside you are full of greed and wickedness. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "40",
              "sid": "LUK 11:40"
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "You"
              ]
            },
            " fools! ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "Did"
              ]
            },
            " not the ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "One who"
              ]
            },
            " made the outside make the inside as well? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "41",
              "sid": "LUK 11:41"
            },
            "But give ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "as"
              ]
            },
            " alms the things that are within ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "you"
              ]
            },
            ", and behold, everything will be clean for you."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "42",
          "sid": "LUK 11:42"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Woe to you Pharisees! For you pay tithes of mint, rue, and every herb, but you disregard justice and the love of God. You should have practiced ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the latter"
              ]
            },
            " without neglecting ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the former"
              ]
            },
            "."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "43",
          "sid": "LUK 11:43"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Woe to you Pharisees! For you love the chief seats in the synagogues and the greetings in the marketplaces. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "44",
              "sid": "LUK 11:44"
            },
            "Woe to you! For you are like unmarked graves, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "which"
              ]
            },
            " men walk over without ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "even"
              ]
            },
            " noticing.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "45",
          "sid": "LUK 11:45"
        },
        "One of the experts in the law told Him, “Teacher, when You say these things, You insult us as well.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "46",
              "sid": "LUK 11:46"
            },
            "“Woe to you as well, experts in the law!”"
          ]
        },
        " He replied. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“For you weigh men down ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "with"
              ]
            },
            " heavy burdens, but you yourselves will not lift a finger ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "to lighten"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "their"
              ]
            },
            " load."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "47",
          "sid": "LUK 11:47"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Woe to you! For you build tombs for the prophets, but ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "it was"
              ]
            },
            " your fathers ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "who"
              ]
            },
            " killed them. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "48",
              "sid": "LUK 11:48"
            },
            "So you are witnesses consenting to the deeds of your fathers: They killed ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the prophets"
              ]
            },
            ", and you build ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "their tombs"
              ]
            },
            ". ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "49",
              "sid": "LUK 11:49"
            },
            "Because of this, the wisdom of God said, ‘I will send them prophets and apostles; ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "some"
              ]
            },
            " of them they will kill and ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "others"
              ]
            },
            " they will persecute.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "50",
          "sid": "LUK 11:50"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "As a result, this generation will be charged with the blood of all the prophets that has been shed since ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " foundation of ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " world, ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "51",
              "sid": "LUK 11:51"
            },
            "from the blood of Abel to the blood of Zechariah, who was killed between the altar and the sanctuary.",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "11:51 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "Literally "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "the house"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            " Yes, I tell you,  ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "all of "
              ]
            },
            " it will be charged to this generation."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "52",
          "sid": "LUK 11:52"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Woe to you experts in the law! For you have taken away the key to knowledge. You yourselves have not entered, and you have hindered those who were entering.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "53",
          "sid": "LUK 11:53"
        },
        "As ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " went on from there, the scribes and Pharisees began to oppose ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        " bitterly and to ply Him with questions about many things, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "54",
          "sid": "LUK 11:54"
        },
        "waiting to catch Him in something He might say."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "12",
      "sid": "LUK 12"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Leaven of the Pharisees"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 16:5-12",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 16:5–12"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 8:14-21",
          "content": [
            "Mark 8:14–21"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "LUK 12:1"
        },
        "In the meantime, a crowd of many thousands had gathered, so that they were trampling one another. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " began to speak first to His disciples: ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Beware of the leaven of the Pharisees, which is hypocrisy. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "2",
              "sid": "LUK 12:2"
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "There"
              ]
            },
            " is nothing concealed that will not be disclosed, and ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "nothing"
              ]
            },
            " hidden that will not be made known. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "3",
              "sid": "LUK 12:3"
            },
            "What you have spoken in the dark will be heard in the daylight, and what you have whispered in the inner rooms will be proclaimed from the housetops."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Fear God Alone"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 10:26-31",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 10:26–31"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "LUK 12:4"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "I tell you, My friends, do not be afraid of those who kill the body and after that can do no more. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "5",
              "sid": "LUK 12:5"
            },
            "But I will show you whom you should fear: Fear the ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "One who"
              ]
            },
            ", after ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "you"
              ]
            },
            " have been killed, has authority to throw ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "you"
              ]
            },
            " into hell.",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "12:5 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "Greek "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "Gehenna"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            " Yes, I tell you, fear Him!"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "LUK 12:6"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "Are"
              ]
            },
            " not five sparrows sold for two pennies?",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "12:6 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "Greek "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "two assaria"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "; an assarion was a Roman copper coin worth about 1/16 of a denarius."
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            " Yet not one of them is forgotten by God. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "7",
              "sid": "LUK 12:7"
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "And even"
              ]
            },
            " the very hairs of your head are all numbered. ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "So"
              ]
            },
            " do not be afraid; you are worth more than many sparrows."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Confessing Christ"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 10:32-33",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 10:32–33"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "LUK 12:8"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "I tell you, everyone who confesses Me before men, the Son of Man will also confess him before the angels of God. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "9",
              "sid": "LUK 12:9"
            },
            "But whoever denies Me before men will be denied before the angels of God. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "10",
              "sid": "LUK 12:10"
            },
            "And everyone who speaks a word against the Son of Man will be forgiven, but whoever blasphemes against the Holy Spirit will not be forgiven."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "LUK 12:11"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "When you are brought before synagogues, rulers, and authorities, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "do"
              ]
            },
            " not worry about how to defend yourselves or what to say. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "12",
              "sid": "LUK 12:12"
            },
            "For at that time the Holy Spirit will teach you what you should say.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Parable of the Rich Fool"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "LUK 12:13"
        },
        "Someone in the crowd said to Him, “Teacher, tell my brother to divide the inheritance with me.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "LUK 12:14"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " replied, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Man, who appointed Me judge or executor between you?”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "LUK 12:15"
        },
        "And He said to them, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Watch out! Guard yourselves against every ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "form of"
              ]
            },
            " greed, for one’s life does not consist in the abundance of his possessions.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "LUK 12:16"
        },
        "Then He told them a parable: ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“The ground of a certain rich man produced an abundance. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "17",
              "sid": "LUK 12:17"
            },
            "So he thought to himself, ‘What shall I do, since I have nowhere to store my crops?’ ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "18",
              "sid": "LUK 12:18"
            },
            "Then he said, ‘This ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "is what"
              ]
            },
            " I will do: I will tear down my barns and will build bigger ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "ones"
              ]
            },
            ", and there I will store up all my grain and ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "my"
              ]
            },
            " goods. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "19",
              "sid": "LUK 12:19"
            },
            "Then I will say to myself, “You have plenty of good things laid up for many years. Take it easy. Eat, drink, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " be merry!”’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "LUK 12:20"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "But God said to him, ‘",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "You"
              ]
            },
            " fool! This very night your life will be required of you. Then who will own what you have accumulated?’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "LUK 12:21"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "This is how ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "it will be for"
              ]
            },
            " anyone who stores up treasure for himself but is not rich toward God.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Do Not Worry"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 6:25-34",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 6:25–34"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "LUK 12:22"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " said to His disciples, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Therefore I tell you, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "do"
              ]
            },
            " not worry about your life, what you will eat, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "or"
              ]
            },
            " about your body, what you will wear. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "23",
              "sid": "LUK 12:23"
            },
            "For life is more than food, and the body ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "more"
              ]
            },
            " than clothes. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "24",
              "sid": "LUK 12:24"
            },
            "Consider the ravens: They do not sow ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "or"
              ]
            },
            " reap, they have no storehouse ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "or"
              ]
            },
            " barn; yet God feeds them. How much more valuable you are than the birds!"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "LUK 12:25"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Who of you by worrying can add a single hour to his life?",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "12:25 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "Or "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "a single cubit to his height"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "; a cubit was approximately 18 inches or 45 centimeters."
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "26",
              "sid": "LUK 12:26"
            },
            "So if you cannot ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "do"
              ]
            },
            " such a small thing, why do you worry about the rest?"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "LUK 12:27"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Consider how the lilies grow: They do not labor ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "or"
              ]
            },
            " spin.",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "12:27 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "NE and Tischendorf "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "Consider the lilies: They do not spin or weave."
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            " Yet I tell you, not even Solomon in all his glory was adorned like one of these. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "28",
              "sid": "LUK 12:28"
            },
            "If that is how God clothes the grass of ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " field, which is ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "here"
              ]
            },
            " today and tomorrow is thrown into the furnace, how much ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "more will He clothe"
              ]
            },
            " you, O ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "you"
              ]
            },
            " of little faith!"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "LUK 12:29"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "And ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "do"
              ]
            },
            " not be concerned about what you will eat ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "or"
              ]
            },
            " drink. ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "Do"
              ]
            },
            " not worry about ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "it"
              ]
            },
            ". ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "30",
              "sid": "LUK 12:30"
            },
            "For the Gentiles of the world strive after all these things, and your Father knows that you need them. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "31",
              "sid": "LUK 12:31"
            },
            "But seek His",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "12:31 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "BYZ and TR "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "God’s"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "; see ",
                    {
                      "type": "ref",
                      "loc": "MAT 6:33",
                      "content": [
                        "Matthew 6:33"
                      ]
                    },
                    "."
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            " kingdom, and these things will be added unto you."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Treasures in Heaven"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 6:19-21",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 6:19–21"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "LUK 12:32"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "Do"
              ]
            },
            " not be afraid, little flock, for your Father is pleased to give you the kingdom. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "33",
              "sid": "LUK 12:33"
            },
            "Sell your possessions and give to the poor. Provide yourselves ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "with"
              ]
            },
            " purses ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "that will"
              ]
            },
            " not wear out, an inexhaustible treasure in heaven, where no thief approaches ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " no moth destroys. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "34",
              "sid": "LUK 12:34"
            },
            "For where your treasure is, there your heart will be also."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Readiness at Any Hour"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 24:36-51",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 24:36–51"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 13:32-37",
          "content": [
            "Mark 13:32–37"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "LUK 12:35"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Be dressed for service and ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "keep"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "your"
              ]
            },
            " lamps burning. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "36",
              "sid": "LUK 12:36"
            },
            "Then you  ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "will be "
              ]
            },
            " like ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "servants"
              ]
            },
            " waiting for their master to return from the wedding banquet, so that when he comes and knocks, they can open ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the door"
              ]
            },
            " for him at once. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "37",
              "sid": "LUK 12:37"
            },
            "Blessed ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "are"
              ]
            },
            " those servants whom the master finds on watch when he returns. Truly I tell you, he will dress himself to serve and will have them recline at the table, and he ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "himself"
              ]
            },
            " will come ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " wait on them. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "38",
              "sid": "LUK 12:38"
            },
            "Even if he comes in the second or third watch of the night",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "12:38 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "That is, between nine at night and three in the morning"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            " and finds ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "them"
              ]
            },
            " alert, those ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "servants"
              ]
            },
            " will be blessed."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "39",
          "sid": "LUK 12:39"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "But understand this: If the homeowner had known at what hour the thief was coming,",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "12:39 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "BYZ and TR include "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "he would have stayed awake, and"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            " he would not have let his house be broken into. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "40",
              "sid": "LUK 12:40"
            },
            "You also must be ready, because the Son of Man will come at an hour you do not expect.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "41",
          "sid": "LUK 12:41"
        },
        "“Lord,” said Peter, “are You addressing this parable to us, or to everyone else as well?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "42",
          "sid": "LUK 12:42"
        },
        "And the Lord answered, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Who then is the faithful ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " wise manager, whom the master puts in charge of his ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "servants"
              ]
            },
            " to give ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "them"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "their"
              ]
            },
            " portion at the proper time? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "43",
              "sid": "LUK 12:43"
            },
            "Blessed ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "is"
              ]
            },
            " that servant whose master finds him doing so when he returns. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "44",
              "sid": "LUK 12:44"
            },
            "Truly I tell you, he will put him in charge of all his possessions."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "45",
          "sid": "LUK 12:45"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "But suppose that servant says in his heart, ‘My master will be a long time in coming,’ and he begins to beat the menservants and maidservants, and to eat and drink and get drunk. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "46",
              "sid": "LUK 12:46"
            },
            "The master of that servant will come on a day he does not expect and at an hour he does not anticipate. Then he will cut him to pieces and assign him a place with the unbelievers."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "47",
          "sid": "LUK 12:47"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "That servant who knows his master’s will ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "but"
              ]
            },
            " does not get ready ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "or"
              ]
            },
            " follow his instructions will be beaten with many ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "blows"
              ]
            },
            ". ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "48",
              "sid": "LUK 12:48"
            },
            "But the ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "one who"
              ]
            },
            " unknowingly does ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "things"
              ]
            },
            " worthy of punishment will be beaten with few ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "blows"
              ]
            },
            ". ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "From"
              ]
            },
            " everyone who has been given much, much will be required; and from him who has been entrusted with much, even more will be demanded."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Not Peace but Division"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MIC 7:1-6",
          "content": [
            "Micah 7:1–6"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 10:34-39",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 10:34–39"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "49",
          "sid": "LUK 12:49"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "I have come to ignite a fire on the earth, and how I wish it were already kindled! ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "50",
              "sid": "LUK 12:50"
            },
            "But I have a baptism to undergo, and how distressed I am until it is accomplished!"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "51",
          "sid": "LUK 12:51"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Do you think that I have come to bring peace to the earth? No, I tell you, but division. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "52",
              "sid": "LUK 12:52"
            },
            "From now on, five in one household will be divided, three against two and two against three. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "53",
              "sid": "LUK 12:53"
            },
            "They will be divided, father against son and son against father, mother against daughter and daughter against mother, mother-in-law against daughter-in-law and daughter-in-law against mother-in-law.",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "12:53 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "See ",
                    {
                      "type": "ref",
                      "loc": "MIC 7:6",
                      "content": [
                        "Micah 7:6"
                      ]
                    },
                    "."
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Interpreting the Present Time"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 16:1-4",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 16:1–4"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 8:11-13",
          "content": [
            "Mark 8:11–13"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "54",
          "sid": "LUK 12:54"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " said to the crowds, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“As soon as you see a cloud rising in ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " west, you say, ‘A shower is coming,’ and that is what happens. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "55",
              "sid": "LUK 12:55"
            },
            "And when ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " south wind blows, you say, ‘It will be hot,’ and it is. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "56",
              "sid": "LUK 12:56"
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "You"
              ]
            },
            " hypocrites! You know how to interpret the appearance of the earth and sky. Why don’t you know how to interpret ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " present time?"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Reconciling with an Adversary"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 5:21-26",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 5:21–26"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "57",
          "sid": "LUK 12:57"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "And why don’t you judge for yourselves what ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "is"
              ]
            },
            " right? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "58",
              "sid": "LUK 12:58"
            },
            "Make every effort to reconcile with your adversary while you are on your way to ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " magistrate. Otherwise, he may drag you off to the judge, and the judge may hand you over to the officer, and the officer may throw you into prison. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "59",
              "sid": "LUK 12:59"
            },
            "I tell you, you will not get out until you have paid the very last penny.",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "12:59 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "Greek "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "lepton"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "; that is, a Jewish coin of bronze or copper worth about 1/128 of a denarius"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "13",
      "sid": "LUK 13"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "A Call to Repentance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JOL 1:13-20",
          "content": [
            "Joel 1:13–20"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "AMO 5:4-15",
          "content": [
            "Amos 5:4–15"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ZEP 2:1-3",
          "content": [
            "Zephaniah 2:1–3"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "LUK 13:1"
        },
        "At that time some ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of those"
          ]
        },
        " present told ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " about the Galileans whose blood Pilate had mixed with their sacrifices. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "LUK 13:2"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "To this"
          ]
        },
        " He replied, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Do you think that these Galileans were ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "worse"
              ]
            },
            " sinners than all the ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "other"
              ]
            },
            " Galileans, because they suffered this way? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "3",
              "sid": "LUK 13:3"
            },
            "No, I tell you. But unless you repent, you too will all perish. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "4",
              "sid": "LUK 13:4"
            },
            "Or those eighteen who were killed ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "when"
              ]
            },
            " the tower of Siloam collapsed on them: Do you think that they were more sinful ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "than"
              ]
            },
            " all the ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "others"
              ]
            },
            " living in Jerusalem? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "5",
              "sid": "LUK 13:5"
            },
            "No, I tell you. But unless you repent, you too will all perish.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Parable of the Barren Fig Tree"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ISA 5:1-7",
          "content": [
            "Isaiah 5:1–7"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "LUK 13:6"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " told this parable: ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“A ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "man"
              ]
            },
            " had a fig tree that was planted in his vineyard. He went to look for fruit on it ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "but"
              ]
            },
            " did not find ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "any"
              ]
            },
            ". ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "7",
              "sid": "LUK 13:7"
            },
            "So he said to the keeper of the vineyard, ‘Look, for the past three years I have come to search for fruit on this fig tree and haven’t found ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "any"
              ]
            },
            ". Therefore cut it down!",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "13:7 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "SBL, NE, WH "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "Cut it down!"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            " Why should it use up the soil?’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "LUK 13:8"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "‘Sir,’ ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the man"
              ]
            },
            " replied, ‘leave it alone again this year, until I dig around it and fertilize ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "it"
              ]
            },
            ". ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "9",
              "sid": "LUK 13:9"
            },
            "If it bears fruit ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "next year"
              ]
            },
            ", fine. But if not, you can cut it down.’”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Jesus Heals a Disabled Woman"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "LUK 13:10"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "One"
          ]
        },
        " Sabbath ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " was teaching in one of the synagogues, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "LUK 13:11"
        },
        "and a woman there had been disabled ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "by a"
          ]
        },
        " spirit ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "for"
          ]
        },
        " eighteen years. She was hunched over and could not stand up straight. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "LUK 13:12"
        },
        "When Jesus saw her, He called ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "her"
          ]
        },
        " over and said, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Woman, you are set free from your disability.”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "LUK 13:13"
        },
        "Then He placed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His"
          ]
        },
        " hands on her, and immediately she straightened up and began to glorify God."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "LUK 13:14"
        },
        "But the synagogue leader was indignant that Jesus had healed on the Sabbath. “There are six days for work,” he told the crowd. “So come ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " be healed on those ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "days"
          ]
        },
        " and not on the Sabbath.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "15",
              "sid": "LUK 13:15"
            },
            "“You hypocrites!”"
          ]
        },
        " the Lord replied. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "Does"
              ]
            },
            " not each of you on the Sabbath untie his ox or donkey from the stall and lead it to water? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "16",
              "sid": "LUK 13:16"
            },
            "Then should not this daughter of Abraham, whom Satan has kept bound ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "for"
              ]
            },
            " eighteen ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "long"
              ]
            },
            " years, be released from ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "her"
              ]
            },
            " bondage on the Sabbath day?”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "LUK 13:17"
        },
        "When ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " said this, all ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His"
          ]
        },
        " adversaries were humiliated. And the whole crowd rejoiced at all the glorious things He was doing."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Parable of the Mustard Seed"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 13:31-32",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 13:31–32"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 4:30-34",
          "content": [
            "Mark 4:30–34"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "LUK 13:18"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " asked, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“What is the kingdom of God like? To what can I compare it? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "19",
              "sid": "LUK 13:19"
            },
            "It is like a mustard seed that a man tossed into his garden. It grew and became a tree, and the birds of the air nested in its branches.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Parable of the Leaven"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 13:33",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 13:33"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "LUK 13:20"
        },
        "Again He asked, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“To what can I compare the kingdom of God? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "21",
              "sid": "LUK 13:21"
            },
            "It is like leaven that a woman took ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " mixed into three measures of flour, until all of it was leavened.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Narrow Door"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 7:13-14",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 7:13–14"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "LUK 13:22"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " traveled throughout ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " towns and villages, teaching as He made His way toward Jerusalem. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "LUK 13:23"
        },
        "“Lord,” someone asked Him, “",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "will"
          ]
        },
        " only a few ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "people"
          ]
        },
        " be saved?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " answered, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "24",
              "sid": "LUK 13:24"
            },
            "“Make every effort to enter through the narrow door. For many, I tell you, will try to enter and will not be able. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "25",
              "sid": "LUK 13:25"
            },
            "After the master of the house gets up and shuts the door, you will stand outside knocking ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " saying, ‘Lord, open the door for us.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "But he will reply, ‘I do not know where you are ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "from"
              ]
            },
            ".’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "LUK 13:26"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Then you will say, ‘We ate and drank with you, and you taught in our streets.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "LUK 13:27"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "And he will answer, ‘I tell you, I do not know where you are ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "from"
              ]
            },
            ". Depart from me, all ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "you"
              ]
            },
            " evildoers.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "LUK 13:28"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "There will be weeping and gnashing of teeth when you see Abraham, Isaac, Jacob, and all the prophets in the kingdom of God, but you yourselves are thrown out. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "29",
              "sid": "LUK 13:29"
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "People"
              ]
            },
            " will come from east and west and north and south, and will recline at the table in the kingdom of God. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "30",
              "sid": "LUK 13:30"
            },
            "And indeed, some who are last will be first, and some who are first will be last.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Lament over Jerusalem"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 23:37-39",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 23:37–39"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "LUK 13:31"
        },
        "At that very hour, some Pharisees came to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " told Him, “Leave this place and get away, because Herod wants to kill You.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "LUK 13:32"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " replied, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Go tell that fox, ‘Look, I will keep driving out demons and healing ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "people"
              ]
            },
            " today and tomorrow, and on the third ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "day"
              ]
            },
            " I will reach My goal.’ ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "33",
              "sid": "LUK 13:33"
            },
            "Nevertheless, I must keep going today and tomorrow and the next ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "day"
              ]
            },
            ", for it is not admissible ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "for"
              ]
            },
            " a prophet to perish outside of Jerusalem."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "LUK 13:34"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "O Jerusalem, Jerusalem, who kills the prophets and stones those sent to her, how often I have longed to gather your children ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "together"
              ]
            },
            " as a hen ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "gathers"
              ]
            },
            " her chicks under ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "her"
              ]
            },
            " wings, but you were unwilling! ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "35",
              "sid": "LUK 13:35"
            },
            "Look, your house is left to you desolate. And I tell you ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "that"
              ]
            },
            " you will not see Me ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "again"
              ]
            },
            " until you say, ‘Blessed is He who comes in ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " name of ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " Lord.’",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "13:35 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "ref",
                      "loc": "PSA 118:26",
                      "content": [
                        "Psalm 118:26"
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "14",
      "sid": "LUK 14"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Jesus Heals a Man with Dropsy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "LUK 14:1"
        },
        "One Sabbath, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " went to eat in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " home of a leading Pharisee, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "those in attendance"
          ]
        },
        " were watching Him closely. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "LUK 14:2"
        },
        "Right there before Him was a man with dropsy. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "LUK 14:3"
        },
        "So Jesus asked the experts in the law and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Pharisees, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Is it lawful to heal on the Sabbath or not?”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "LUK 14:4"
        },
        "But they remained silent."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " took hold ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of the man"
          ]
        },
        ", healed him, and sent him on his way. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "LUK 14:5"
        },
        "And He asked them, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Which of you ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "whose"
              ]
            },
            " son",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "14:5 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "TR "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "donkey"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            " or ox falls into a pit on the Sabbath day ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "will"
              ]
            },
            " not immediately pull him out?”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "LUK 14:6"
        },
        "And they were unable to answer these  ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "questions "
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Parable of the Guests"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "LUK 14:7"
        },
        "When ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " noticed how the guests chose the places of honor, He told them a parable: ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "8",
              "sid": "LUK 14:8"
            },
            "“When you are invited to a wedding banquet, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "do"
              ]
            },
            " not sit in the place of honor, in case ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "someone"
              ]
            },
            " more distinguished than you has been invited. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "9",
              "sid": "LUK 14:9"
            },
            "Then the host who invited both of you will come ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " tell you, ‘Give this man ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "your"
              ]
            },
            " seat.’ And in humiliation, you will have to take the last place."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "LUK 14:10"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "But when you are invited, go ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " sit in the last place, so that your host will come ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " tell you, ‘Friend, move up to a better place.’",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "14:10 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "See ",
                    {
                      "type": "ref",
                      "loc": "PRO 25:7",
                      "content": [
                        "Proverbs 25:7"
                      ]
                    },
                    "."
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            " Then you will be honored in front of everyone at the table ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "with"
              ]
            },
            " you. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "11",
              "sid": "LUK 14:11"
            },
            "For everyone who exalts himself will be humbled, and the ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "one who"
              ]
            },
            " humbles himself will be exalted.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "LUK 14:12"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " said to the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "man who"
          ]
        },
        " had invited Him, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“When you host a dinner or a banquet, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "do"
              ]
            },
            " not invite your friends ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "or"
              ]
            },
            " brothers ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "or"
              ]
            },
            " relatives ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "or"
              ]
            },
            " rich neighbors. Otherwise, they may invite you ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "in return"
              ]
            },
            ", and you will be repaid. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "13",
              "sid": "LUK 14:13"
            },
            "But when you host a banquet, invite the poor, the crippled, the lame, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " the blind, ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "14",
              "sid": "LUK 14:14"
            },
            "and you will be blessed. Since they cannot repay you, you will be repaid at the resurrection of the righteous.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Parable of the Banquet"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 22:1-14",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 22:1–14"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "LUK 14:15"
        },
        "When one of those reclining with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        " heard ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        ", he said to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        ", “Blessed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is everyone"
          ]
        },
        " who will eat at the feast",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "14:15 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "who will eat bread "
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " in the kingdom of God.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "LUK 14:16"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " replied, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“A certain man prepared a great banquet and invited many ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "guests"
              ]
            },
            ". ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "17",
              "sid": "LUK 14:17"
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "When it was"
              ]
            },
            " time for the banquet, he sent his servant to tell those who had been invited, ‘Come, for ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "everything"
              ]
            },
            " is now ready.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "LUK 14:18"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "But one after another they all began to make excuses. The first ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "one"
              ]
            },
            " said, ‘I have bought a field, and I need to go see it. Please excuse me.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "LUK 14:19"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Another said, ‘I have bought five yoke of oxen, and I am going to try them ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "out"
              ]
            },
            ". Please excuse me.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "LUK 14:20"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Still another said, ‘I have married a wife, so I cannot come.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "LUK 14:21"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "The servant returned ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " reported all this to his master. Then the owner of the house became angry ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " said to his servant, ‘Go out quickly into the streets and alleys of the city, and bring in the poor, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " crippled, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " blind, and ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " lame.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "LUK 14:22"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "‘Sir,’ the servant replied, ‘what you ordered has been done, and there is still room.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "LUK 14:23"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "So"
              ]
            },
            " the master told ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "his"
              ]
            },
            " servant, ‘Go out to the highways and hedges and compel ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "them"
              ]
            },
            " to come in, so that my house will be full. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "24",
              "sid": "LUK 14:24"
            },
            "For I tell you, not one of those men who were invited will taste my banquet.’”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Cost of Discipleship"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 8:18-22",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 8:18–22"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "LUK 9:57-62",
          "content": [
            "Luke 9:57–62"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JHN 6:59-66",
          "content": [
            "John 6:59–66"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "LUK 14:25"
        },
        "Now large crowds were traveling with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        ", and He turned ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said to them, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "26",
              "sid": "LUK 14:26"
            },
            "“If anyone comes to Me and ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "does"
              ]
            },
            " not hate his father and mother and wife and children and brothers and sisters — yes, even his ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "own"
              ]
            },
            " life — he cannot be My disciple. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "27",
              "sid": "LUK 14:27"
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "And"
              ]
            },
            " whoever ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "does"
              ]
            },
            " not carry his cross and follow Me cannot be My disciple."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "LUK 14:28"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Which of you, wishing to build a tower, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "does"
              ]
            },
            " not first sit down ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " count the cost to see if he has ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the resources "
              ]
            },
            " to complete ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "it"
              ]
            },
            "? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "29",
              "sid": "LUK 14:29"
            },
            "Otherwise, if he lays ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " foundation and is unable to finish ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the work"
              ]
            },
            ", everyone who sees ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "it"
              ]
            },
            " will ridicule him, ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "30",
              "sid": "LUK 14:30"
            },
            "saying, ‘This man could not finish what he started to build.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "LUK 14:31"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Or what king on his way to war with another king will not first sit down ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " consider whether he can engage with ten thousand ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "men"
              ]
            },
            " the ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "one"
              ]
            },
            " coming against him with twenty thousand? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "32",
              "sid": "LUK 14:32"
            },
            "And if ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "he is unable"
              ]
            },
            ", he will send a delegation ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "while the other king"
              ]
            },
            " is still far off, to ask for terms of peace."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "LUK 14:33"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "In the same way, any one of you who does not give up everything he has cannot be My disciple."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Good Salt"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 5:13-16",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 5:13–16"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 9:49-50",
          "content": [
            "Mark 9:49–50"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "LUK 14:34"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Salt ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "is"
              ]
            },
            " good, but if the salt loses its savor, with what will it be seasoned? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "35",
              "sid": "LUK 14:35"
            },
            "It is fit neither for ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " soil nor for ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " manure pile, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " it is thrown out."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "He who has ears to hear, let him hear.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "15",
      "sid": "LUK 15"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Parable of the Lost Sheep"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 18:10-14",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 18:10–14"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "LUK 15:1"
        },
        "Now all the tax collectors and sinners were gathering around to listen to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "LUK 15:2"
        },
        "So the Pharisees and scribes began to grumble: “This ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "man"
          ]
        },
        " welcomes sinners and eats with them.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "LUK 15:3"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " told them this parable: ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "4",
              "sid": "LUK 15:4"
            },
            "“What man among you, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "if"
              ]
            },
            " he has a hundred sheep and loses one of them, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "does"
              ]
            },
            " not leave the ninety-nine in the pasture and go after the ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "one"
              ]
            },
            " that is lost, until he finds it? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "5",
              "sid": "LUK 15:5"
            },
            "And when he finds ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "it"
              ]
            },
            ", he joyfully puts ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "it"
              ]
            },
            " on his shoulders, ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "6",
              "sid": "LUK 15:6"
            },
            "comes home, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " calls together ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "his"
              ]
            },
            " friends and neighbors to tell them, ‘Rejoice with me, for I have found my lost sheep!’ ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "7",
              "sid": "LUK 15:7"
            },
            "I tell you that in the same way there will be ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "more"
              ]
            },
            " joy in heaven over one sinner who repents than over ninety-nine righteous ones who do not need to repent."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Parable of the Lost Coin"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "LUK 15:8"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Or what woman who has ten silver coins",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "15:8 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "Greek "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "ten drachmas"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    ", each worth about a day’s wages"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " loses one ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "of them"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "does"
              ]
            },
            " not light a lamp, sweep ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "her"
              ]
            },
            " house, and search carefully until she finds it? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "9",
              "sid": "LUK 15:9"
            },
            "And when she finds ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "it"
              ]
            },
            ", she calls together ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "her"
              ]
            },
            " friends and neighbors to say, ‘Rejoice with me, for I have found ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "my"
              ]
            },
            " lost coin.’ ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "10",
              "sid": "LUK 15:10"
            },
            "In the same way, I tell you, there is joy in the presence of God’s angels over one sinner who repents.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Parable of the Prodigal Son"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "DEU 21:18-21",
          "content": [
            "Deuteronomy 21:18–21"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "LUK 15:11"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " said, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "There was"
              ]
            },
            " a man who had two sons. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "12",
              "sid": "LUK 15:12"
            },
            "The younger ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "son"
              ]
            },
            " said to ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "him"
              ]
            },
            ", ‘Father, give me my share of the estate.’ So he divided ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "his"
              ]
            },
            " property between them."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "LUK 15:13"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "After a few days, the younger son got everything together ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " journeyed to a distant country, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "where"
              ]
            },
            " he squandered his wealth in wild living."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "LUK 15:14"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "After he had spent all ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "he had"
              ]
            },
            ", a severe famine swept through that country, and he began to be in need. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "15",
              "sid": "LUK 15:15"
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "So"
              ]
            },
            " he went ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " hired himself out to a citizen of that country, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "who"
              ]
            },
            " sent him into his fields to feed ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " pigs. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "16",
              "sid": "LUK 15:16"
            },
            "He longed to fill his belly with the pods the pigs were eating, but no one would give him  ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "a thing "
              ]
            },
            "."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "LUK 15:17"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Finally he came to his senses ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " said, ‘How many of my father’s hired servants have plenty of food, but here I ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "am"
              ]
            },
            ", starving to death! ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "18",
              "sid": "LUK 15:18"
            },
            "I will get up ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " go back to my father and say to him, “Father, I have sinned against heaven and against you. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "19",
              "sid": "LUK 15:19"
            },
            "I am no longer worthy to be called your son. Make me like one of your hired servants.”’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "LUK 15:20"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "So he got up ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " went to his father. But while he ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "was"
              ]
            },
            " still in the distance, his father saw him and was filled with compassion. He ran ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "to his son"
              ]
            },
            ", embraced him, and kissed him."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "LUK 15:21"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "The son declared, ‘Father, I have sinned against heaven and against you. I am no longer worthy to be called your son.",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "15:21 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "WH includes "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "Make me like one of your hired servants"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "; see verse 19."
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "LUK 15:22"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "But the father said to his servants, ‘Quick! Bring the best robe and put it on him. Put a ring on his finger and sandals on his feet. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "23",
              "sid": "LUK 15:23"
            },
            "Bring the fattened calf ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " kill ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "it"
              ]
            },
            ". Let us feast ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " celebrate. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "24",
              "sid": "LUK 15:24"
            },
            "For this son of mine was dead and is alive again! He was lost and is found!’ So they began to celebrate."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "LUK 15:25"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Meanwhile the older son was in ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " field, and as he approached the house, he heard music and dancing. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "26",
              "sid": "LUK 15:26"
            },
            "So he called one of the servants ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " asked what was going on."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "LUK 15:27"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "‘Your brother has returned,’ he said, ‘and your father has killed the fattened calf, because he has him back safe and sound.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "LUK 15:28"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "The older son"
              ]
            },
            " became angry and refused to go in. So his father came out ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " pleaded with him."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "LUK 15:29"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "But he answered his father, ‘Look, all these years I have served you and never disobeyed a commandment of yours. Yet you never gave me ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "even"
              ]
            },
            " a young goat so I could celebrate with my friends. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "30",
              "sid": "LUK 15:30"
            },
            "But when this son of yours returns from squandering your wealth with prostitutes, you kill the fattened calf for him!’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "LUK 15:31"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "‘Son, you are always with me,’ ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the father"
              ]
            },
            " said, ‘and all that ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "is"
              ]
            },
            " mine is yours. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "32",
              "sid": "LUK 15:32"
            },
            "But it was fitting to celebrate and be glad, because this brother of yours was dead and is alive again; he was lost and is found.’”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "16",
      "sid": "LUK 16"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Parable of the Shrewd Manager"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "LUK 16:1"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " also said to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His"
          ]
        },
        " disciples, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“There was a rich man whose manager was accused of wasting his possessions. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "2",
              "sid": "LUK 16:2"
            },
            "So he called him in to ask, ‘What ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "is"
              ]
            },
            " this I hear about you? Turn in an account of your management, for you cannot be manager any longer.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "LUK 16:3"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "The manager said to himself, ‘What shall I do, now that my master is taking away my ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "position"
              ]
            },
            "? I am too weak to dig ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " too ashamed to beg. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "4",
              "sid": "LUK 16:4"
            },
            "I know what I will do so that after my removal from management, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "people"
              ]
            },
            " will welcome me into their homes.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "LUK 16:5"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "And he called in each one of his master’s debtors. ‘How much do you owe my master?’ he asked the first."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "LUK 16:6"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "‘A hundred ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "measures"
              ]
            },
            " of olive oil,’",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "16:6 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "Greek "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "‘A hundred baths of oil’"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "; that is, approximately 870 gallons or 3,300 liters"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            " he answered."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "‘Take your bill,’ said ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the manager"
              ]
            },
            ", ‘sit down quickly, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " write fifty.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "LUK 16:7"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Then he asked another, ‘And how much ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "do"
              ]
            },
            " you owe?’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "‘A hundred ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "measures"
              ]
            },
            " of wheat,’",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "16:7 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "Greek "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "‘A hundred cors of wheat’"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "; that is, approximately 1,000 bushels or 35,000 liters (probably about 30 tons or 27 metric tons of wheat)"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            " he replied."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "‘Take your bill and write eighty,’ he told him."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "LUK 16:8"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "The master commended the dishonest manager because he had acted shrewdly. For the sons of this age are more shrewd in dealing with their own kind than ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "are"
              ]
            },
            " the sons of light. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "9",
              "sid": "LUK 16:9"
            },
            "I tell you, use worldly wealth to make friends for yourselves so that when it is gone, they will welcome you into eternal dwellings."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "LUK 16:10"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Whoever ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "is"
              ]
            },
            " faithful with very little will also ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "be"
              ]
            },
            " faithful with much, and whoever ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "is"
              ]
            },
            " dishonest with very little will also ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "be"
              ]
            },
            " dishonest with much. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "11",
              "sid": "LUK 16:11"
            },
            "So if you have not been faithful with worldly wealth, who will entrust you ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "with"
              ]
            },
            " true ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "riches"
              ]
            },
            "? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "12",
              "sid": "LUK 16:12"
            },
            "And if you have not been faithful with the ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "belongings"
              ]
            },
            " of another, who will give you belongings of your own?"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "LUK 16:13"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "No servant can serve two masters. Either he will hate the one and love the other, or he will be devoted to ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " one and despise the other. You cannot serve ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "both"
              ]
            },
            " God and money.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Law and the Prophets"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "LUK 16:14"
        },
        "The Pharisees, who were lovers of money, heard all ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of this"
          ]
        },
        " and were scoffing at ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "LUK 16:15"
        },
        "So He said to them, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“You are the ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "ones who"
              ]
            },
            " justify ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "yourselves"
              ]
            },
            " before men, but God knows your hearts. For what ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "is"
              ]
            },
            " prized among men ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "is"
              ]
            },
            " detestable before God."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "LUK 16:16"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "The Law and the Prophets ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "were proclaimed"
              ]
            },
            " until John. Since that time, the ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "gospel"
              ]
            },
            " of the kingdom of God is being preached, and everyone is forcing his way into it.",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "16:16 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "Or "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "everyone is urged to enter into it"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "17",
              "sid": "LUK 16:17"
            },
            "But it is easier for heaven and earth to pass away than for a single stroke of a pen to drop out of the Law."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "LUK 16:18"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Anyone who divorces his wife and marries another ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "woman"
              ]
            },
            " commits adultery, and he who marries a divorced woman commits adultery."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Rich Man and Lazarus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JHN 5:39-47",
          "content": [
            "John 5:39–47"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "LUK 16:19"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Now there was a rich man dressed in purple and fine linen, who lived each day in joyous splendor. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "20",
              "sid": "LUK 16:20"
            },
            "And a beggar named Lazarus lay at his gate, covered with sores ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "21",
              "sid": "LUK 16:21"
            },
            "and longing to be fed with the crumbs that fell from the rich man’s table. Even the dogs came ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " licked his sores."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "LUK 16:22"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "One day the beggar died and was carried by the angels to Abraham’s side.",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "16:22 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "Greek "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "into Abraham’s bosom"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "; similarly in verse 23"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            " And the rich man also died and was buried. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "23",
              "sid": "LUK 16:23"
            },
            "In Hades, where he was in torment, he looked up ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " saw Abraham from afar, with Lazarus by his side."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "LUK 16:24"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "So he cried out, ‘Father Abraham, have mercy on me and send Lazarus to dip the tip of his finger in water and cool my tongue. For I am in agony in this fire.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "LUK 16:25"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "But Abraham answered, ‘Child, remember that during your lifetime you received your good ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "things"
              ]
            },
            ", ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "while"
              ]
            },
            " Lazarus ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "received"
              ]
            },
            " bad ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "things"
              ]
            },
            ". But now he is comforted here, while you are in agony. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "26",
              "sid": "LUK 16:26"
            },
            "And besides all this, a great chasm has been fixed between us and you, so that ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "even"
              ]
            },
            " those who wish cannot cross from here to you, nor can ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "anyone"
              ]
            },
            " cross from there to us.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "LUK 16:27"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "‘Then I beg you, father,’ he said, ‘send ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "Lazarus"
              ]
            },
            " to my father’s house, ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "28",
              "sid": "LUK 16:28"
            },
            "for I have five brothers. Let him warn them, so that they will not also end up in this place of torment.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "LUK 16:29"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "But Abraham replied, ‘They have Moses and the Prophets; let ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "your brothers"
              ]
            },
            " listen to them.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "LUK 16:30"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "‘No, father Abraham,’ he said, ‘but if someone is sent to them from ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " dead, they will repent.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "LUK 16:31"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Then ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "Abraham"
              ]
            },
            " said to him, ‘If they do not listen to Moses and the Prophets, they will not be persuaded even if someone rises from ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " dead.’”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "17",
      "sid": "LUK 17"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Temptations and Trespasses"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 18:6-9",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 18:6–9"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 9:42-48",
          "content": [
            "Mark 9:42–48"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "LUK 17:1"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " said to His disciples, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“It is inevitable that stumbling blocks will come, but woe ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "to the one "
              ]
            },
            " through whom they come! ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "2",
              "sid": "LUK 17:2"
            },
            "It would be better for him to have a millstone hung around his neck and to be thrown into the sea than ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "to cause"
              ]
            },
            " one of these little ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "ones"
              ]
            },
            " to stumble."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "LUK 17:3"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Watch yourselves. If your brother sins, rebuke him; and if he repents, forgive him. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "4",
              "sid": "LUK 17:4"
            },
            "Even if he sins against you seven times in a day, and seven times returns to say, ‘I repent,’ you must forgive him.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Power of Faith"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 17:19-20",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 17:19–20"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "LUK 17:5"
        },
        "The apostles said to the Lord, “Increase our faith!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "LUK 17:6"
        },
        "And the Lord answered, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“If you have faith the size of a mustard seed, you can say to this mulberry tree, ‘Be uprooted and planted in the sea,’ and it will obey you."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "LUK 17:7"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Which of you ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "whose"
              ]
            },
            " servant comes in from plowing or shepherding in the field will say to him, ‘Come at once ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " sit down to eat’? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "8",
              "sid": "LUK 17:8"
            },
            "Instead, won’t he tell him, ‘Prepare my meal and dress yourself to serve me while I eat and drink, and afterward you may eat and drink’? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "9",
              "sid": "LUK 17:9"
            },
            "Does he thank the servant because he did what he was told? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "10",
              "sid": "LUK 17:10"
            },
            "So you also, when you have done everything commanded of you, should say, ‘We are unworthy servants; we have only done our duty.’”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Ten Lepers"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "2KI 5:1-14",
          "content": [
            "2 Kings 5:1–14"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "LUK 17:11"
        },
        "While ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " was on His way to Jerusalem, He was passing between Samaria and Galilee. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "LUK 17:12"
        },
        "As He entered one of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " villages, He was met by ten lepers.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "17:12 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "A "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "leper "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "was one afflicted with a skin disease. See Leviticus 13."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "They"
          ]
        },
        " stood at a distance ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "LUK 17:13"
        },
        "and raised ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " voices, shouting, “Jesus, Master, have mercy on us!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "LUK 17:14"
        },
        "When ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " saw ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        ", He said, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Go, show yourselves to the priests.”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "17:14 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "See ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "LEV 14:1-32",
                  "content": [
                    "Leviticus 14:1–32"
                  ]
                },
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " And as they were on their way, they were cleansed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "LUK 17:15"
        },
        "When one of them saw that he was healed, he came back, praising God in a loud voice. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "LUK 17:16"
        },
        "He fell facedown at ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus’"
          ]
        },
        " feet in thanksgiving to Him — and he was a Samaritan."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "17",
              "sid": "LUK 17:17"
            },
            "“",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "Were"
              ]
            },
            " not ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "all"
              ]
            },
            " ten cleansed?”"
          ]
        },
        " Jesus asked. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Where then are the ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "other"
              ]
            },
            " nine? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "18",
              "sid": "LUK 17:18"
            },
            "Was no one found except this foreigner to return ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " give glory to God?”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "LUK 17:19"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " said to him, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Rise ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " go; your faith has made you well!",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "17:19 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "Or "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "has saved you"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Coming of the Kingdom"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "GEN 19:24-29",
          "content": [
            "Genesis 19:24–29"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "LUK 17:20"
        },
        "When asked by the Pharisees when the kingdom of God would come, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " replied, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“The kingdom of God ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "will"
              ]
            },
            " not come with observable signs. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "21",
              "sid": "LUK 17:21"
            },
            "Nor will ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "people"
              ]
            },
            " say, ‘Look, here ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "it is"
              ]
            },
            ",’ or ‘There ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "it is"
              ]
            },
            ".’ For you see, the kingdom of God is in your midst.",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "17:21 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "Or "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "within you "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "or "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "within your grasp"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "LUK 17:22"
        },
        "Then He said to the disciples, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "The"
              ]
            },
            " time is coming when you will long to see one of the days of the Son of Man, but you will not see ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "it"
              ]
            },
            ". ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "23",
              "sid": "LUK 17:23"
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "People"
              ]
            },
            " will tell you, ‘Look, there ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "He is"
              ]
            },
            "!’ or ‘Look, here ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "He is"
              ]
            },
            "!’ ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "Do"
              ]
            },
            " not go out ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "or"
              ]
            },
            " chase after ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "them"
              ]
            },
            ". ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "24",
              "sid": "LUK 17:24"
            },
            "For just as the lightning flashes ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " lights up the sky from ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "one end"
              ]
            },
            " to the ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "other"
              ]
            },
            ", so will be the Son of Man in His day. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "25",
              "sid": "LUK 17:25"
            },
            "But first He must suffer many things and be rejected by this generation."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "LUK 17:26"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Just as it was in the days of Noah, so also will it be in the days of the Son of Man: ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "27",
              "sid": "LUK 17:27"
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "People"
              ]
            },
            " were eating ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " drinking, marrying ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " being given in marriage, up to ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " day Noah entered the ark. Then the flood came and destroyed them all."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "LUK 17:28"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "It was the same in the days of Lot: ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "People"
              ]
            },
            " were eating ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " drinking, buying ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " selling, planting ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " building. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "29",
              "sid": "LUK 17:29"
            },
            "But on the day Lot left Sodom, fire and sulfur rained down from heaven and destroyed them all."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "LUK 17:30"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "It will be just like that on the day the Son of Man is revealed. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "31",
              "sid": "LUK 17:31"
            },
            "On that day, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "let"
              ]
            },
            " no one on the housetop come down to retrieve his possessions. Likewise, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "let"
              ]
            },
            " no one in ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " field return for anything ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "he has"
              ]
            },
            " left behind. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "32",
              "sid": "LUK 17:32"
            },
            "Remember Lot’s wife! ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "33",
              "sid": "LUK 17:33"
            },
            "Whoever tries to save his life will lose it, but whoever loses ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "his life"
              ]
            },
            " will preserve it. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "34",
              "sid": "LUK 17:34"
            },
            "I tell you, on that night two ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "people"
              ]
            },
            " will be in one bed: one will be taken and the other left. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "35",
              "sid": "LUK 17:35"
            },
            "Two ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "women"
              ]
            },
            " will be grinding grain together: one will be taken and the other left.”",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "17:35 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "TR includes "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "char",
                      "marker": "fv",
                      "content": [
                        "36"
                      ]
                    },
                    "Two men will be in the field. One will be taken and the other left"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "; see ",
                    {
                      "type": "ref",
                      "loc": "MAT 24:40",
                      "content": [
                        "Matthew 24:40"
                      ]
                    },
                    "."
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "LUK 17:37"
        },
        "“Where, Lord?” they asked."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " answered, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Wherever ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "there is"
              ]
            },
            " a carcass, there the vultures will gather.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "18",
      "sid": "LUK 18"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Parable of the Persistent Widow"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "LUK 18:1"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " told them a parable about their need to pray at all times and not lose heart: ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "2",
              "sid": "LUK 18:2"
            },
            "“In a certain town there was a judge ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "who"
              ]
            },
            " neither feared God ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "nor"
              ]
            },
            " respected men. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "3",
              "sid": "LUK 18:3"
            },
            "And there was a widow in that town who kept appealing to him, ‘Give me justice ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "against"
              ]
            },
            " my adversary.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "LUK 18:4"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "For a while he refused, but later he said to himself, ‘Though I neither fear God nor respect men, ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "5",
              "sid": "LUK 18:5"
            },
            "yet because this widow keeps pestering me, I will give her justice. Otherwise, she will wear me out with her perpetual requests.’”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "LUK 18:6"
        },
        "And the Lord said, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Listen to ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " words of the unjust judge. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "7",
              "sid": "LUK 18:7"
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "Will"
              ]
            },
            " not God bring about justice for His elect who cry out to Him day and night? Will He delay in helping them? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "8",
              "sid": "LUK 18:8"
            },
            "I tell you, He will promptly carry out justice on their behalf. Nevertheless, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "when"
              ]
            },
            " the Son of Man comes, will He find faith on earth?”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Pharisee and the Tax Collector"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "LUK 18:9"
        },
        "To some who trusted in their own righteousness and viewed others ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "with contempt"
          ]
        },
        ", He also told this parable: ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "10",
              "sid": "LUK 18:10"
            },
            "“Two men went up to the temple to pray. One ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "was"
              ]
            },
            " a Pharisee and the other a tax collector. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "11",
              "sid": "LUK 18:11"
            },
            "The Pharisee stood by himself ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " prayed,",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "18:11 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "Or "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "stood and prayed to himself"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            " ‘God, I thank You that I am not like other men — swindlers, evildoers, adulterers — or even like this tax collector. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "12",
              "sid": "LUK 18:12"
            },
            "I fast twice a week ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " pay tithes of all that I acquire.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "LUK 18:13"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "But the tax collector stood at a distance, unwilling even to lift up ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "his"
              ]
            },
            " eyes to heaven. Instead, he beat his breast ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " said, ‘God, have mercy on me, a sinner!’ ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "14",
              "sid": "LUK 18:14"
            },
            "I tell you, this ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "man"
              ]
            },
            ", rather than ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the Pharisee"
              ]
            },
            ", went home justified. For everyone who exalts himself will be humbled, but the ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "one who"
              ]
            },
            " humbles himself will be exalted.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Jesus Blesses the Children"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 19:13-15",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 19:13–15"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 10:13-16",
          "content": [
            "Mark 10:13–16"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "LUK 18:15"
        },
        "Now ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "people"
          ]
        },
        " were even bringing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " babies to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " for Him to place His hands on them. And when the disciples saw ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        ", they rebuked ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "those who brought them"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "LUK 18:16"
        },
        "But Jesus called ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the children"
          ]
        },
        " to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Let the little children come to Me, and ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "do"
              ]
            },
            " not hinder them! For the kingdom of God belongs to such as these. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "17",
              "sid": "LUK 18:17"
            },
            "Truly I tell you, anyone who does not receive the kingdom of God like a little child will never enter it.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Rich Young Ruler"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 19:16-30",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 19:16–30"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 10:17-31",
          "content": [
            "Mark 10:17–31"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "LUK 18:18"
        },
        "Then a certain ruler asked Him, “Good Teacher, what must I do to inherit eternal life?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "19",
              "sid": "LUK 18:19"
            },
            "“Why do you call Me good?”"
          ]
        },
        " Jesus replied. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“No one ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "is"
              ]
            },
            " good except God alone. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "20",
              "sid": "LUK 18:20"
            },
            "You know the commandments: ‘Do not commit adultery, do not murder, do not steal, do not bear false witness, honor your father and mother.’",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "18:20 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "ref",
                      "loc": "EXO 20:12-16",
                      "content": [
                        "Exodus 20:12–16"
                      ]
                    },
                    "; Deuteronomy 5:16–20"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "LUK 18:21"
        },
        "“All these I have kept from my youth,” he said."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "LUK 18:22"
        },
        "On hearing this, Jesus told him, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“You still lack one thing: Sell everything you own and give to ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " poor, and you will have treasure in heaven. Then come, follow Me.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "LUK 18:23"
        },
        "But when ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the ruler"
          ]
        },
        " heard this, he became very sad, because he was extremely wealthy."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "LUK 18:24"
        },
        "Seeing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the man’s"
          ]
        },
        " sadness,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "18:24 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Seeing that he had become sorrowful"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; SBL, NE, and WH "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Seeing him"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " Jesus said, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“How hard ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "it is"
              ]
            },
            " for the rich to enter the kingdom of God! ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "25",
              "sid": "LUK 18:25"
            },
            "Indeed, it is easier for a camel to pass through the eye of a needle than for a rich man to enter the kingdom of God.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "LUK 18:26"
        },
        "Those who heard ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        " asked, “Who then can be saved?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "LUK 18:27"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " said, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“What ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "is"
              ]
            },
            " impossible with man is possible with God.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "LUK 18:28"
        },
        "“Look,” said Peter, “we have left all we had",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "18:28 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "left our own"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; BYZ and TR "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "left all"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " to follow You.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "29",
              "sid": "LUK 18:29"
            },
            "“Truly I tell you,”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " replied, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“no one who has left home or wife or brothers or parents or children for the sake of the kingdom of God ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "30",
              "sid": "LUK 18:30"
            },
            "will fail to receive many times more in this age — and in the age to come, eternal life.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Third Prediction of the Passion"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 20:17-19",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 20:17–19"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 10:32-34",
          "content": [
            "Mark 10:32–34"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "LUK 18:31"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " took the Twelve ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "aside"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said to them, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Look, we are going up to Jerusalem, and everything the prophets have written about the Son of Man will be fulfilled. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "32",
              "sid": "LUK 18:32"
            },
            "He will be delivered over to the Gentiles and will be mocked and insulted and spit upon. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "33",
              "sid": "LUK 18:33"
            },
            "They will flog ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "Him"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " kill Him, and on the third day He will rise again.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "LUK 18:34"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the disciples"
          ]
        },
        " did not understand any of these things. The meaning was hidden from them, and they did not comprehend what He was saying."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Jesus Heals a Blind Beggar"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 20:29-34",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 20:29–34"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 10:46-52",
          "content": [
            "Mark 10:46–52"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "LUK 18:35"
        },
        "As ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " drew near to Jericho, a blind ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "man"
          ]
        },
        " was sitting beside the road, begging. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "36",
          "sid": "LUK 18:36"
        },
        "When he heard the crowd going by, he asked what was ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "happening"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "LUK 18:37"
        },
        "“Jesus of Nazareth is passing by,” they told him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "38",
          "sid": "LUK 18:38"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        " he called out, “Jesus, Son of David, have mercy on me!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "39",
          "sid": "LUK 18:39"
        },
        "Those who led the way admonished him to be silent, but he cried out all the louder, “Son of David, have mercy on me!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "40",
          "sid": "LUK 18:40"
        },
        "Jesus stopped ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " directed that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the man"
          ]
        },
        " be brought to Him. When he had come near, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " asked him, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "41",
              "sid": "LUK 18:41"
            },
            "“What do you want Me to do for you?”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "“Lord,” he said, “let me see again.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "42",
              "sid": "LUK 18:42"
            },
            "“Receive your sight!”"
          ]
        },
        " Jesus replied. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Your faith has healed you.”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "43",
          "sid": "LUK 18:43"
        },
        "Immediately he received his sight and followed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        ", glorifying God. And all the people, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " they saw ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        ", gave praise to God."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "19",
      "sid": "LUK 19"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Jesus and Zacchaeus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "NUM 5:5-10",
          "content": [
            "Numbers 5:5–10"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "LUK 19:1"
        },
        "Then Jesus entered Jericho ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " was passing through. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "LUK 19:2"
        },
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there was"
          ]
        },
        " a man named Zacchaeus, a chief tax collector, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who was"
          ]
        },
        " very wealthy. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "LUK 19:3"
        },
        "He was trying to see who Jesus was, but could not ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "see"
          ]
        },
        " over the crowd because he was small in stature. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "LUK 19:4"
        },
        "So he ran on ahead ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " climbed a sycamore tree to see Him, since ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " was about to pass that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "way"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "LUK 19:5"
        },
        "When ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " came to that place, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He"
          ]
        },
        " looked up ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Zacchaeus, hurry down, for I must stay at your house today.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "LUK 19:6"
        },
        "So ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Zacchaeus"
          ]
        },
        " hurried down and welcomed Him joyfully. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "LUK 19:7"
        },
        "And all ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who"
          ]
        },
        " saw ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        " began to grumble, saying, “He has gone to be the guest of a sinful man!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "LUK 19:8"
        },
        "But Zacchaeus stood up ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said to the Lord, “Look, Lord, half of my possessions I give to the poor, and if I have cheated anyone, I will repay ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        " fourfold.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "LUK 19:9"
        },
        "Jesus said to him, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Today salvation has come to this house, because ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "this man"
              ]
            },
            " too is a son of Abraham. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "10",
              "sid": "LUK 19:10"
            },
            "For the Son of Man came to seek and to save the lost.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Parable of the Ten Minas"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 25:14-30",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 25:14–30"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "LUK 19:11"
        },
        "While ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the people"
          ]
        },
        " were listening to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        ", ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " proceeded to tell ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " a parable, because He was near Jerusalem and they thought the kingdom of God would appear imminently. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "LUK 19:12"
        },
        "So He said, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“A man of noble birth went to a distant country to lay claim to his kingship and then return. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "13",
              "sid": "LUK 19:13"
            },
            "Beforehand, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "he"
              ]
            },
            " called ten of his servants ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " gave them ten minas.",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "19:13 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "That is, he gave each servant one mina. A mina was most likely a silver coin worth a hundred drachmas, that is, about a hundred days’ wages."
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            " ‘Conduct business ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "with this"
              ]
            },
            " until I return,’ he said."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "LUK 19:14"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "But his subjects hated him and sent a delegation after him to say, ‘We do not want this ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "man"
              ]
            },
            " to rule over us.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "LUK 19:15"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "When he returned from procuring ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "his"
              ]
            },
            " kingship, he summoned ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " servants to whom he had given the money, to find out what each one had earned."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "LUK 19:16"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "The first ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "servant"
              ]
            },
            " came forward ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " said, ‘Master, your mina has produced ten ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "more"
              ]
            },
            " minas.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "LUK 19:17"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "His master"
              ]
            },
            " replied, ‘Well done, good servant! Because you have been faithful in a very small matter, you shall have authority over ten cities.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "LUK 19:18"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "The second ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "servant"
              ]
            },
            " came ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " said, ‘Master, your mina has made five minas.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "LUK 19:19"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "And to this one he said, ‘You shall ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "have authority"
              ]
            },
            " over five cities.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "LUK 19:20"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Then another ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "servant"
              ]
            },
            " came ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " said, ‘Master, here is your mina, which I have laid away in a piece of cloth.",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "19:20 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "Greek "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "soudariō"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "21",
              "sid": "LUK 19:21"
            },
            "For I was afraid of you, because you are a harsh man. You withdraw what you did not deposit and reap what you did not sow.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "LUK 19:22"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "His master"
              ]
            },
            " replied, ‘",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "You"
              ]
            },
            " wicked servant, I will judge you by your ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "own words"
              ]
            },
            ". ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "So"
              ]
            },
            " you knew that I am a harsh man, withdrawing what I did not deposit and reaping what I did not sow? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "23",
              "sid": "LUK 19:23"
            },
            "Why then did you not deposit my money in ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " bank, and upon my return I could have collected it with interest?’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "LUK 19:24"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Then he told those standing by, ‘Take the mina from him and give ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "it"
              ]
            },
            " to the ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "one who"
              ]
            },
            " has ten minas.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "LUK 19:25"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "‘Master,’ they said, ‘he ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "already"
              ]
            },
            " has ten!’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "LUK 19:26"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "He replied,"
              ]
            },
            " ‘ I tell you that everyone who has will be given ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "more"
              ]
            },
            "; but the ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "one who"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "does"
              ]
            },
            " not have, even what he has will be taken away from ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "him"
              ]
            },
            ". ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "27",
              "sid": "LUK 19:27"
            },
            "And these enemies of mine who were unwilling ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "for"
              ]
            },
            " me to rule over them, bring ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "them"
              ]
            },
            " here and slay them in front of me.’”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Triumphal Entry"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ZEC 9:9-13",
          "content": [
            "Zechariah 9:9–13"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 21:1-11",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 21:1–11"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 11:1-11",
          "content": [
            "Mark 11:1–11"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JHN 12:12-19",
          "content": [
            "John 12:12–19"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "LUK 19:28"
        },
        "After ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " had said this, He went on ahead, going up to Jerusalem."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "LUK 19:29"
        },
        "As He approached Bethphage and Bethany at the Mount of Olives, He sent out two of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His"
          ]
        },
        " disciples, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "LUK 19:30"
        },
        "saying, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Go into the village ahead ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "of you"
              ]
            },
            ", ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " as you enter ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "it"
              ]
            },
            ", you will find a colt tied ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "there"
              ]
            },
            ", on which no one ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "has"
              ]
            },
            " ever sat. Untie it ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " bring ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "it here"
              ]
            },
            ". ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "31",
              "sid": "LUK 19:31"
            },
            "If anyone asks, ‘Why are you untying ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "it"
              ]
            },
            "?’ tell ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "him"
              ]
            },
            ", ‘The Lord needs it.’”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "LUK 19:32"
        },
        "So those who were sent went out ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " found ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        " just as ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " had told them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "LUK 19:33"
        },
        "As they were untying the colt, its owners asked, “Why are you untying the colt?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "LUK 19:34"
        },
        "“The Lord needs it,” they answered. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "LUK 19:35"
        },
        "Then they led ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the colt"
          ]
        },
        " to Jesus, threw their cloaks over ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        ", ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " put ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " on ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "36",
          "sid": "LUK 19:36"
        },
        "As He rode along,  ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the people "
          ]
        },
        " spread their cloaks on the road. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "LUK 19:37"
        },
        "And as He approached the descent from the Mount of Olives, the whole multitude of disciples began to praise God joyfully in a loud voice for all ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " miracles they had seen:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "38",
          "sid": "LUK 19:38"
        },
        "“Blessed is the King who comes in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " name of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord!”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "19:38 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PSA 118:26",
                  "content": [
                    "Psalm 118:26"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“Peace in heaven and glory in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " highest!”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "19:38 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "See ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PSA 148:1",
                  "content": [
                    "Psalm 148:1"
                  ]
                },
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "39",
          "sid": "LUK 19:39"
        },
        "But some of the Pharisees in the crowd said to Him, “Teacher, rebuke Your disciples!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "40",
              "sid": "LUK 19:40"
            },
            "“I tell you,”"
          ]
        },
        " He answered, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“if they remain silent, the very stones will cry out.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Jesus Weeps over Jerusalem"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ISA 29:1-16",
          "content": [
            "Isaiah 29:1–16"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "41",
          "sid": "LUK 19:41"
        },
        "As ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " approached ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jerusalem"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " saw the city, He wept over it ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "42",
          "sid": "LUK 19:42"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“If only you had known on this day what ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "would bring"
              ]
            },
            " you peace! But now it is hidden from your eyes. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "43",
              "sid": "LUK 19:43"
            },
            "For ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " days will come upon you ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "when"
              ]
            },
            " your enemies will barricade you and surround you and hem you in on every side. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "44",
              "sid": "LUK 19:44"
            },
            "They will level you to the ground — you and ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " children within your ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "walls"
              ]
            },
            ". They will not leave one stone on ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "another"
              ]
            },
            ", because you did not recognize the time of your visitation ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "from God"
              ]
            },
            ".",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "19:44 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "Literally "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "your visitation"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Jesus Cleanses the Temple"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 21:12-17",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 21:12–17"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 11:15-19",
          "content": [
            "Mark 11:15–19"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JHN 2:12-25",
          "content": [
            "John 2:12–25"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "45",
          "sid": "LUK 19:45"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " entered the temple ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "courts"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "19:45 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the temple"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " began to drive out those who were selling ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "46",
          "sid": "LUK 19:46"
        },
        "He declared to them, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“It is written: ‘My house will be a house of prayer.’",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "19:46 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "ref",
                      "loc": "ISA 56:7",
                      "content": [
                        "Isaiah 56:7"
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            " But you have made it ‘a den of robbers.’",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "19:46 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "ref",
                      "loc": "JER 7:11",
                      "content": [
                        "Jeremiah 7:11"
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "47",
          "sid": "LUK 19:47"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " was teaching at the temple every day, but the chief priests, scribes, and leaders of the people were intent on killing Him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "48",
          "sid": "LUK 19:48"
        },
        "Yet they could not find a way to do ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "so"
          ]
        },
        ", because all the people hung on His words."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "20",
      "sid": "LUK 20"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Jesus’ Authority Challenged"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 21:23-27",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 21:23–27"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 11:27-33",
          "content": [
            "Mark 11:27–33"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "LUK 20:1"
        },
        "One day ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "as Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " was teaching the people in the temple ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "courts"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "20:1 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the temple"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " and proclaiming the gospel, the chief priests and scribes, together with the elders, came up ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to Him"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "LUK 20:2"
        },
        "“Tell us,” they said, “by what authority are You doing these things, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " who gave You this authority?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "3",
              "sid": "LUK 20:3"
            },
            "“I will also ask you a question,”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " replied. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Tell Me: ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "4",
              "sid": "LUK 20:4"
            },
            "John’s baptism — was it from heaven, or from men?”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "LUK 20:5"
        },
        "They deliberated among themselves ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, “If we say, ‘From heaven,’ He will ask, ‘Why did you not believe him?’ ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "LUK 20:6"
        },
        "But if we say, ‘From men,’ all the people will stone us, for they are convinced ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " John was a prophet.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "LUK 20:7"
        },
        "So they answered ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " they did not know where ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it was"
          ]
        },
        " from."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "LUK 20:8"
        },
        "And Jesus replied, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Neither ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "will"
              ]
            },
            " I tell you by what authority I am doing these things.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Parable of the Wicked Tenants"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 21:33-46",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 21:33–46"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 12:1-12",
          "content": [
            "Mark 12:1–12"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "LUK 20:9"
        },
        "Then He proceeded to tell the people this parable: ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“A man planted a vineyard, rented it ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "out"
              ]
            },
            " to ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "some"
              ]
            },
            " tenants, and went away for a long time. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "10",
              "sid": "LUK 20:10"
            },
            "At harvest time, he sent a servant to the tenants to collect ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "his share"
              ]
            },
            " of the fruit of the vineyard. But the tenants beat ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the servant"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " sent him away empty-handed."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "LUK 20:11"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "So"
              ]
            },
            " he sent another servant, but they beat ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "him"
              ]
            },
            " and treated him shamefully, sending ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "him"
              ]
            },
            " away empty-handed."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "LUK 20:12"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Then he sent a third, but they wounded him ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " threw ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "him"
              ]
            },
            " out."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "LUK 20:13"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "‘What shall I do?’ asked the owner of the vineyard. ‘I will send my beloved son. Perhaps they will respect him.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "LUK 20:14"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "But when the tenants saw ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the son"
              ]
            },
            ", they discussed it among themselves ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " said, ‘This is the heir. Let us kill him, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " the inheritance will be ours.’ ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "15",
              "sid": "LUK 20:15"
            },
            "So they threw him out of the vineyard ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " killed ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "him"
              ]
            },
            "."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "What then ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "will"
              ]
            },
            " the owner of the vineyard do to them? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "16",
              "sid": "LUK 20:16"
            },
            "He will come and kill those tenants and give the vineyard to others.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when the people"
          ]
        },
        " heard ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        ", they said, “May such a thing never happen!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "LUK 20:17"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " looked directly at them ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Then what is the meaning of that which is written:"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "‘",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "The"
              ]
            },
            " stone the builders rejected"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "has become ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " cornerstone’",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "20:17 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "ref",
                      "loc": "PSA 118:22",
                      "content": [
                        "Psalm 118:22"
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "?"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "LUK 20:18"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Everyone who falls on this stone will be broken to pieces, but he on whom it falls will be crushed.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Paying Taxes to Caesar"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 22:15-22",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 22:15–22"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 12:13-17",
          "content": [
            "Mark 12:13–17"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "LUK 20:19"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " the scribes and chief priests realized that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " had spoken this parable against them, they sought to arrest Him that very hour. But they were afraid of the people."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "LUK 20:20"
        },
        "So they watched ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        " closely ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " sent spies who pretended to be sincere. They were hoping to catch ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        " in His words in order to hand Him over to the rule and authority of the governor. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "LUK 20:21"
        },
        "“Teacher,” they inquired, “we know that You speak and teach correctly. You show no partiality but teach the way of God in accordance with the truth. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "LUK 20:22"
        },
        "Is it lawful for us to pay taxes to Caesar or not?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "LUK 20:23"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " saw through their duplicity ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said to them, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "24",
              "sid": "LUK 20:24"
            },
            "“Show Me a denarius.",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "20:24 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "A denarius was customarily a day’s wage for a laborer; see ",
                    {
                      "type": "ref",
                      "loc": "MAT 20:2",
                      "content": [
                        "Matthew 20:2"
                      ]
                    },
                    "."
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            " Whose image and inscription are on it?”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "“Caesar’s,” they answered."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "LUK 20:25"
        },
        "So ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " told them, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Give to Caesar what ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "is"
              ]
            },
            " Caesar’s, and to God what ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "is"
              ]
            },
            " God’s.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "LUK 20:26"
        },
        "And they were unable to trap Him in His words before the people. And amazed at His answer, they fell silent."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Sadducees and the Resurrection"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 22:23-33",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 22:23–33"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 12:18-27",
          "content": [
            "Mark 12:18–27"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "LUK 20:27"
        },
        "Then some of the Sadducees, who say there is no resurrection, came to question Him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "LUK 20:28"
        },
        "“Teacher,” they said, “Moses wrote for us that if a man’s brother dies ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " leaves a wife but no children, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the man"
          ]
        },
        " is to marry ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his brother’s"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "widow"
          ]
        },
        " and raise up offspring for ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        ".",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "20:28 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "DEU 25:5",
                  "content": [
                    "Deuteronomy 25:5"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "LUK 20:29"
        },
        "Now there were seven brothers. The first ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "one"
          ]
        },
        " married a wife ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "but"
          ]
        },
        " died childless. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "LUK 20:30"
        },
        "Then the second",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "20:30 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "BYZ and TR include "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "married the widow, and he also died,"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "LUK 20:31"
        },
        "and the third married ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the widow"
          ]
        },
        ", and in the same way ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "all"
          ]
        },
        " seven died, leaving no children. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "LUK 20:32"
        },
        "And last of all, the woman died. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "LUK 20:33"
        },
        "So then, in the resurrection, whose wife will she be? For ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "all"
          ]
        },
        " seven were married to her.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "LUK 20:34"
        },
        "Jesus answered, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“The sons of this age marry and are given in marriage. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "35",
              "sid": "LUK 20:35"
            },
            "But those who are considered worthy to share in the age ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "to come"
              ]
            },
            " and in the resurrection from ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " dead ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "will"
              ]
            },
            " neither marry nor be given in marriage. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "36",
              "sid": "LUK 20:36"
            },
            "In fact, they can no longer die, because they are like ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " angels. And since they are sons of the resurrection, they are sons of God."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "LUK 20:37"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Even Moses demonstrates that the dead are raised, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "in the passage "
              ]
            },
            " about the ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "burning "
              ]
            },
            " bush. For he calls ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " Lord ‘the God of Abraham, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " God of Isaac, and ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " God of Jacob.’",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "20:37 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "ref",
                      "loc": "EXO 3:6",
                      "content": [
                        "Exodus 3:6"
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "38",
              "sid": "LUK 20:38"
            },
            "He is not ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " God of ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " dead, but of ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " living, for to Him all are alive.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "39",
          "sid": "LUK 20:39"
        },
        "Some of the scribes answered, “Teacher, You have spoken well!” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "40",
          "sid": "LUK 20:40"
        },
        "And they did not dare to question Him any ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "further"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Whose Son Is the Christ?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 22:41-46",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 22:41–46"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 12:35-37",
          "content": [
            "Mark 12:35–37"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "41",
          "sid": "LUK 20:41"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " declared, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“How can it be said that the Christ is ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " Son of David? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "42",
              "sid": "LUK 20:42"
            },
            "For David himself says in ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " book of Psalms:"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "‘",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "The"
              ]
            },
            " Lord said to my Lord,"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Sit at My right hand"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "43",
          "sid": "LUK 20:43"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "until I make Your enemies"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "a footstool for Your feet.”’",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "20:43 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "ref",
                      "loc": "PSA 110:1",
                      "content": [
                        "Psalm 110:1"
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "44",
          "sid": "LUK 20:44"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Thus David calls Him ‘Lord.’ So how can He be ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "David’s"
              ]
            },
            " son?”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Beware of the Scribes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 12:38-40",
          "content": [
            "Mark 12:38–40"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "45",
          "sid": "LUK 20:45"
        },
        "In the hearing of all the people, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " said to His disciples, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "46",
              "sid": "LUK 20:46"
            },
            "“Beware of the scribes. They like to walk around in long robes, and they love ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " greetings in the marketplaces, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " chief seats in the synagogues, and ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " places of honor at banquets. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "47",
              "sid": "LUK 20:47"
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "They"
              ]
            },
            " defraud widows ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "of their"
              ]
            },
            " houses,",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "20:47 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "Literally "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "They devour widows’ houses"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            " and for a show make lengthy prayers. These ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "men"
              ]
            },
            " will receive greater condemnation.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "21",
      "sid": "LUK 21"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Poor Widow’s Offering"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 12:41-44",
          "content": [
            "Mark 12:41–44"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "LUK 21:1"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " looked up ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " saw the rich putting their gifts into the treasury, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "LUK 21:2"
        },
        "and He saw a poor widow put in two small copper coins.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "21:2 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Greek "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "two lepta"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; a lepton was a Jewish coin of bronze or copper worth about 1/128 of a denarius."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "3",
              "sid": "LUK 21:3"
            },
            "“Truly I tell you,”"
          ]
        },
        " He said, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“this poor widow has put in more than all ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the others"
              ]
            },
            ". ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "4",
              "sid": "LUK 21:4"
            },
            "For they all contributed out of their surplus, but she out of her poverty has put in all she had to live on.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Temple Destruction and Other Signs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 24:1-8",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 24:1–8"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 13:1-8",
          "content": [
            "Mark 13:1–8"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "LUK 21:5"
        },
        "As some ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of the disciples"
          ]
        },
        " were remarking how the temple was adorned with beautiful stones and consecrated gifts, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " said, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "6",
              "sid": "LUK 21:6"
            },
            "“",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "As for"
              ]
            },
            " what you see here, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " time will come ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "when"
              ]
            },
            " not one stone will be left on ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "another"
              ]
            },
            "; ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "every one"
              ]
            },
            " will be thrown down.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "LUK 21:7"
        },
        "“Teacher,” they asked, “when ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "will"
          ]
        },
        " these things happen? And what ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "will be"
          ]
        },
        " the sign ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " they are about to take place?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "LUK 21:8"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " answered, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“See to it that you are not deceived. For many will come in My name, claiming, ‘I am ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "He"
              ]
            },
            ",’ and, ‘The time is near.’ ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "Do"
              ]
            },
            " not follow them. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "9",
              "sid": "LUK 21:9"
            },
            "When you hear of wars and rebellions, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "do"
              ]
            },
            " not be alarmed. These things must happen first, but the end ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "is"
              ]
            },
            " not imminent.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Witnessing to All Nations"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 24:9-14",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 24:9–14"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 13:9-13",
          "content": [
            "Mark 13:9–13"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "LUK 21:10"
        },
        "Then He told them, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Nation will rise against nation, and kingdom against kingdom. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "11",
              "sid": "LUK 21:11"
            },
            "There will be great earthquakes, famines, and pestilences in various places, along with fearful sights and great signs from heaven."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "LUK 21:12"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "But before all ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "this"
              ]
            },
            ", they will seize you and persecute ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "you"
              ]
            },
            ". On account of My name they will deliver you to the synagogues and prisons, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " they will bring ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "you"
              ]
            },
            " before kings and governors. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "13",
              "sid": "LUK 21:13"
            },
            "This will be your opportunity to serve as witnesses. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "14",
              "sid": "LUK 21:14"
            },
            "So make up your mind not to worry beforehand how to defend yourselves. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "15",
              "sid": "LUK 21:15"
            },
            "For I will give you speech and wisdom that none of your adversaries will be able to resist ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "or"
              ]
            },
            " contradict."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "LUK 21:16"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "You will be betrayed even by parents and brothers and relatives and friends, and ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "some"
              ]
            },
            " of you will be put to death. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "17",
              "sid": "LUK 21:17"
            },
            "And you will be hated by everyone because of My name. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "18",
              "sid": "LUK 21:18"
            },
            "Yet not even a hair of your head will perish. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "19",
              "sid": "LUK 21:19"
            },
            "By your patient endurance you will gain your souls."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Destruction of Jerusalem"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 24:15-25",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 24:15–25"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 13:14-23",
          "content": [
            "Mark 13:14–23"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "LUK 21:20"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "But when you see Jerusalem surrounded by armies, you will know that her desolation is near. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "21",
              "sid": "LUK 21:21"
            },
            "Then ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "let"
              ]
            },
            " those who are in Judea flee to the mountains, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "let"
              ]
            },
            " those in ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the city"
              ]
            },
            " get out, and ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "let"
              ]
            },
            " those in the country stay out of ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the city"
              ]
            },
            ". ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "22",
              "sid": "LUK 21:22"
            },
            "For these are ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " days of vengeance, to fulfill all that is written."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "LUK 21:23"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "How miserable those days ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "will be"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "for"
              ]
            },
            " pregnant and nursing ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "mothers"
              ]
            },
            "! For there will be great distress upon the land and wrath against this people. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "24",
              "sid": "LUK 21:24"
            },
            "They will fall by ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " edge of ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " sword and be led captive into all the nations. And Jerusalem will be trodden down by ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " Gentiles, until ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " times of ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " Gentiles are fulfilled."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Return of the Son of Man"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 24:26-31",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 24:26–31"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 13:24-27",
          "content": [
            "Mark 13:24–27"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "LUK 21:25"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "There will be signs in ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " sun and moon and stars, and on the earth dismay among the nations, bewildered by ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " roaring of ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " sea and ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " surging of the waves. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "26",
              "sid": "LUK 21:26"
            },
            "Men will faint from fear and anxiety over what is coming upon the earth, for the powers of the heavens will be shaken. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "27",
              "sid": "LUK 21:27"
            },
            "At that time they will see the Son of Man coming in a cloud with power and great glory.",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "21:27 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "See ",
                    {
                      "type": "ref",
                      "loc": "DAN 7:13-14",
                      "content": [
                        "Daniel 7:13–14"
                      ]
                    },
                    "."
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "28",
              "sid": "LUK 21:28"
            },
            "When these things begin to happen, stand up and lift up your heads, because your redemption is drawing near.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Lesson of the Fig Tree"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 24:32-35",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 24:32–35"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 13:28-31",
          "content": [
            "Mark 13:28–31"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "LUK 21:29"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " told them a parable: ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Look at the fig tree and all the trees. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "30",
              "sid": "LUK 21:30"
            },
            "When they sprout leaves, you can see for yourselves ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " know that summer is near. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "31",
              "sid": "LUK 21:31"
            },
            "So also, when you see these things happening, know that the kingdom of God is near. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "32",
              "sid": "LUK 21:32"
            },
            "Truly I tell you, this generation will not pass away until all ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "these things"
              ]
            },
            " have happened. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "33",
              "sid": "LUK 21:33"
            },
            "Heaven and earth will pass away, but My words will never pass away."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Be Watchful for the Day"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "LUK 21:34"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "But watch yourselves, or your hearts will be weighed down by dissipation, drunkenness, and ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " worries of life — and that day will spring upon you suddenly like a snare. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "35",
              "sid": "LUK 21:35"
            },
            "For it will come upon all who dwell on the face of all the earth. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "36",
              "sid": "LUK 21:36"
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "So"
              ]
            },
            " keep watch at all times, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " pray that you may have the strength to escape all that is about to happen and to stand before the Son of Man.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "LUK 21:37"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Every"
          ]
        },
        " day ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " taught at the temple, but ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "every"
          ]
        },
        " evening He went out to spend the night on the Mount of Olives. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "38",
          "sid": "LUK 21:38"
        },
        "And early in the morning all the people ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "would come"
          ]
        },
        " to hear Him at the temple."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "22",
      "sid": "LUK 22"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Plot to Kill Jesus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 26:1-5",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 26:1–5"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 14:1-2",
          "content": [
            "Mark 14:1–2"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JHN 11:45-57",
          "content": [
            "John 11:45–57"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "LUK 22:1"
        },
        "Now the Feast of Unleavened ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Bread"
          ]
        },
        ",",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "22:1 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the feast of the Unleavened"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; see ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "EXO 12:14-20",
                  "content": [
                    "Exodus 12:14–20"
                  ]
                },
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " called ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Passover, was approaching, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "LUK 22:2"
        },
        "and the chief priests and scribes were looking for a way to put ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " to death, for they feared the people."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Judas Agrees to Betray Jesus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 26:14-16",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 26:14–16"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 14:10-11",
          "content": [
            "Mark 14:10–11"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "LUK 22:3"
        },
        "Then Satan entered Judas Iscariot, who was ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "one"
          ]
        },
        " of the Twelve. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "LUK 22:4"
        },
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Judas"
          ]
        },
        " went to discuss with the chief priests and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "temple"
          ]
        },
        " officers how he might betray ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " to them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "LUK 22:5"
        },
        "They were delighted and agreed to give him money. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "LUK 22:6"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Judas"
          ]
        },
        " consented, and began to look for ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "an"
          ]
        },
        " opportunity to betray ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " to them in the absence of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "a"
          ]
        },
        " crowd."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Preparing the Passover"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 26:17-19",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 26:17–19"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 14:12-16",
          "content": [
            "Mark 14:12–16"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "LUK 22:7"
        },
        "Then came the day of Unleavened ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Bread"
          ]
        },
        " on which the Passover lamb was to be sacrificed. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "LUK 22:8"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " sent Peter and John, saying, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Go ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " make preparations for us to eat the Passover.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "LUK 22:9"
        },
        "“Where do You want us to prepare ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        "?” they asked."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "LUK 22:10"
        },
        "He answered, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“When you enter the city, a man carrying a jug of water will meet you. Follow him to the house he enters, ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "11",
              "sid": "LUK 22:11"
            },
            "and say to the owner of that house, ‘The Teacher asks: Where is the guest room, where I may eat the Passover with My disciples?’ ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "12",
              "sid": "LUK 22:12"
            },
            "And he will show you a large upper room, already furnished. Make preparations there.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "LUK 22:13"
        },
        "So they went ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " found ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        " just as ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " had told them. And they prepared the Passover."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Last Supper"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 26:20-30",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 26:20–30"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 14:17-26",
          "content": [
            "Mark 14:17–26"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "1CO 11:17-34",
          "content": [
            "1 Corinthians 11:17–34"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "LUK 22:14"
        },
        "When the hour had come, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " reclined at the table with His apostles. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "LUK 22:15"
        },
        "And He said to them, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“I have eagerly desired to eat this Passover with you before My suffering. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "16",
              "sid": "LUK 22:16"
            },
            "For I tell you that I will not eat it again until it is fulfilled in the kingdom of God.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "LUK 22:17"
        },
        "After taking ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " cup, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He"
          ]
        },
        " gave thanks ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Take this and divide ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "it"
              ]
            },
            " among yourselves. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "18",
              "sid": "LUK 22:18"
            },
            "For I tell you that I will not drink of the fruit of the vine from now on until the kingdom of God comes.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "LUK 22:19"
        },
        "And He took ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " bread, gave thanks ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " broke ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        ", and gave ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        " to them, saying, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“This is My body, given for you; do this in remembrance of Me.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "LUK 22:20"
        },
        "In the same way, after supper ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He took"
          ]
        },
        " the cup, saying, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“This cup ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "is"
              ]
            },
            " the new covenant in My blood, which is poured out for you.",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "22:20 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "Some manuscripts end verse 19 after "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "This is My body "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "and do not include verse 20."
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "LUK 22:21"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Look! The hand of My betrayer ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "is"
              ]
            },
            " with Mine on the table. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "22",
              "sid": "LUK 22:22"
            },
            "Indeed, the Son of Man will go as it has been determined, but woe to that man who betrays Him.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "LUK 22:23"
        },
        "Then they began to question among themselves which of them was going to do this."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Who Is the Greatest?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "LUK 22:24"
        },
        "A dispute also arose among ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the disciples"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "as to"
          ]
        },
        " which of them should be considered ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " greatest. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "LUK 22:25"
        },
        "So ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " declared, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“The kings of the Gentiles lord it over them, and those in authority over them call themselves benefactors. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "26",
              "sid": "LUK 22:26"
            },
            "But you ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "shall"
              ]
            },
            " not ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "be"
              ]
            },
            " like them. Instead, the greatest among you should be like the youngest, and the ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "one who"
              ]
            },
            " leads like the ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "one who"
              ]
            },
            " serves. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "27",
              "sid": "LUK 22:27"
            },
            "For who ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "is"
              ]
            },
            " greater, the ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "one who"
              ]
            },
            " reclines at the table or the ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "one who"
              ]
            },
            " serves? ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "Is it"
              ]
            },
            " not the ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "one who"
              ]
            },
            " reclines? But I am among you as ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "one who"
              ]
            },
            " serves."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "LUK 22:28"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "You are the ones who have stood by Me in My trials. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "29",
              "sid": "LUK 22:29"
            },
            "And I bestow on you a kingdom, just as My Father has bestowed ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "one"
              ]
            },
            " on Me, ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "30",
              "sid": "LUK 22:30"
            },
            "so that you may eat and drink at My table in My kingdom and sit on thrones, judging the twelve tribes of Israel."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Jesus Predicts Peter’s Denial"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 26:31-35",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 26:31–35"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 14:27-31",
          "content": [
            "Mark 14:27–31"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JHN 13:36-38",
          "content": [
            "John 13:36–38"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "LUK 22:31"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Simon, Simon, Satan has asked to sift all of you like wheat. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "32",
              "sid": "LUK 22:32"
            },
            "But I have prayed for you,  ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "Simon "
              ]
            },
            ", that your faith will not fail. And when you have turned back, strengthen your brothers.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "LUK 22:33"
        },
        "“Lord,” said ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Peter"
          ]
        },
        ", “I am ready to go with You even to prison and to death.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "LUK 22:34"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " replied, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“I tell you, Peter, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " rooster ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "will"
              ]
            },
            " not crow today until you have denied three times that you know Me.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "LUK 22:35"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " asked them, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“When I sent you out without purse ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "or"
              ]
            },
            " bag ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "or"
              ]
            },
            " sandals, did you lack anything?”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "“Nothing,” they answered."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "36",
              "sid": "LUK 22:36"
            },
            "“Now, however,”"
          ]
        },
        " He told them, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“the ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "one"
              ]
            },
            " with a purse should take ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "it"
              ]
            },
            ", and likewise a bag; and the ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "one"
              ]
            },
            " without a sword should sell his cloak and buy ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "one"
              ]
            },
            ". ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "37",
              "sid": "LUK 22:37"
            },
            "For I tell you that this Scripture must be fulfilled in Me: ‘And He was numbered with ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " transgressors.’",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "22:37 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "ref",
                      "loc": "ISA 53:12",
                      "content": [
                        "Isaiah 53:12"
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            " For ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "what is written"
              ]
            },
            " about Me is reaching its fulfillment.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "38",
          "sid": "LUK 22:38"
        },
        "So they said, “Look, Lord, here ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "are"
          ]
        },
        " two swords.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“That is enough,”"
          ]
        },
        " He answered."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Jesus Prays on the Mount of Olives"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 26:36-46",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 26:36–46"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 14:32-42",
          "content": [
            "Mark 14:32–42"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "39",
          "sid": "LUK 22:39"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " went out as usual to the Mount of Olives, and the disciples followed Him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "40",
          "sid": "LUK 22:40"
        },
        "When He came to the place, He told them, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Pray that you will not enter into temptation.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "41",
          "sid": "LUK 22:41"
        },
        "And He withdrew about a stone’s throw beyond them, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "where"
          ]
        },
        " He knelt down ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " prayed, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "42",
              "sid": "LUK 22:42"
            },
            "“Father, if You are willing, take this cup from Me. Yet not My will, but Yours be done.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "43",
          "sid": "LUK 22:43"
        },
        "Then an angel from heaven appeared to Him ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " strengthened Him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "44",
          "sid": "LUK 22:44"
        },
        "And in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His"
          ]
        },
        " anguish, He prayed more earnestly, and His sweat became like drops of blood falling to the ground.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "22:44 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Some manuscripts do not include verses 43 and 44."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "45",
          "sid": "LUK 22:45"
        },
        "When ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " rose from prayer ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " returned to the disciples, He found them asleep, exhausted from sorrow. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "46",
              "sid": "LUK 22:46"
            },
            "“Why are you sleeping?”"
          ]
        },
        " He asked. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Get up ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " pray so that you will not enter into temptation.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Betrayal of Jesus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 26:47-56",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 26:47–56"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 14:43-52",
          "content": [
            "Mark 14:43–52"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JHN 18:1-14",
          "content": [
            "John 18:1–14"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "47",
          "sid": "LUK 22:47"
        },
        "While He was still speaking, a crowd arrived, led by the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "man"
          ]
        },
        " called Judas, one of the Twelve. He approached Jesus to kiss Him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "48",
          "sid": "LUK 22:48"
        },
        "But Jesus asked him, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Judas, are you betraying the Son of Man with a kiss?”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "49",
          "sid": "LUK 22:49"
        },
        "Those around ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " saw what was about to happen ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, “Lord, should we strike with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "our"
          ]
        },
        " swords?” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "50",
          "sid": "LUK 22:50"
        },
        "And one of them struck the servant of the high priest, cutting off his right ear."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "51",
          "sid": "LUK 22:51"
        },
        "But Jesus answered, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“No more of this!”"
          ]
        },
        " And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He"
          ]
        },
        " touched the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "man’s"
          ]
        },
        " ear ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " healed him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "52",
          "sid": "LUK 22:52"
        },
        "Then Jesus said to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " chief priests, temple officers, and elders who had come for Him, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Have you come out with swords and clubs as ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "you would"
              ]
            },
            " against an outlaw? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "53",
              "sid": "LUK 22:53"
            },
            "Every day I was with you in the temple ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "courts"
              ]
            },
            ",",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "22:53 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "Literally "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "the temple"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " you did not lay a hand on Me. But this hour belongs to you and to the power of darkness.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Peter Denies Jesus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 26:69-75",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 26:69–75"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 14:66-72",
          "content": [
            "Mark 14:66–72"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JHN 18:15-18",
          "content": [
            "John 18:15–18"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "54",
          "sid": "LUK 22:54"
        },
        "Then they seized ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        ", led ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        " away, and took ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        " into the house of the high priest. And Peter followed at a distance."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "55",
          "sid": "LUK 22:55"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "those present"
          ]
        },
        " had kindled a fire in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " middle of the courtyard and sat down together, Peter sat down among them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "56",
          "sid": "LUK 22:56"
        },
        "A servant girl saw him seated in the firelight and looked intently at him. “This ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "man"
          ]
        },
        " also was with Him,” she said."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "57",
          "sid": "LUK 22:57"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Peter"
          ]
        },
        " denied ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        ". “Woman, I do not know Him,” he said."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "58",
          "sid": "LUK 22:58"
        },
        "A short time later, someone else saw him ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, “You also are one of them.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "But Peter said, “Man, I am not.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "59",
          "sid": "LUK 22:59"
        },
        "About an hour later, another ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "man"
          ]
        },
        " insisted, “Certainly this ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "man"
          ]
        },
        " was with Him, for he too is a Galilean.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "60",
          "sid": "LUK 22:60"
        },
        "“Man, I do not know what you are talking about,” Peter replied."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "And immediately, while he was still speaking, the rooster crowed. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "61",
          "sid": "LUK 22:61"
        },
        "And the Lord turned ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " looked at Peter."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "Then Peter remembered the word that the Lord had spoken to him: ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Before ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " rooster crows today, you will deny Me three times.”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "62",
          "sid": "LUK 22:62"
        },
        "And he went outside ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " wept bitterly."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Soldiers Mock Jesus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ISA 50:4-11",
          "content": [
            "Isaiah 50:4–11"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 27:27-31",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 27:27–31"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 15:16-20",
          "content": [
            "Mark 15:16–20"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JHN 19:1-15",
          "content": [
            "John 19:1–15"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "63",
          "sid": "LUK 22:63"
        },
        "The men who were holding ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " began to mock Him ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " beat ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "64",
          "sid": "LUK 22:64"
        },
        "They blindfolded Him",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "22:64 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "BYZ and TR include "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "and were striking Him on the face"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " kept demanding, “Prophesy! Who hit You?” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "65",
          "sid": "LUK 22:65"
        },
        "And they said many ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "other"
          ]
        },
        " blasphemous things against Him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Jesus before the Sanhedrin"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 26:57-68",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 26:57–68"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 14:53-65",
          "content": [
            "Mark 14:53–65"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JHN 18:19-24",
          "content": [
            "John 18:19–24"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "66",
          "sid": "LUK 22:66"
        },
        "At daybreak the council of the elders of the people, both ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " chief priests and scribes, met together. They led Jesus into their Sanhedrin",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "22:66 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "their Council"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "67",
          "sid": "LUK 22:67"
        },
        "“If You are the Christ, tell us.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " answered, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“If I tell you, you will not believe. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "68",
              "sid": "LUK 22:68"
            },
            "And if I ask ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "you"
              ]
            },
            " a question, you will not answer. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "69",
              "sid": "LUK 22:69"
            },
            "But from now on the Son of Man will be seated at ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " right hand of the power of God.”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "22:69 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "See ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PSA 110:1",
                  "content": [
                    "Psalm 110:1"
                  ]
                },
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "70",
          "sid": "LUK 22:70"
        },
        "So they all asked, “Are You then the Son of God?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "He replied, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“You say that I am.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "71",
          "sid": "LUK 22:71"
        },
        "“Why do we need any more testimony?” they declared. “We have heard ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        " for ourselves from His own lips.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "23",
      "sid": "LUK 23"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Jesus before Pilate"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 27:11-14",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 27:11–14"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JHN 18:28-40",
          "content": [
            "John 18:28–40"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "LUK 23:1"
        },
        "Then the whole council rose ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " led ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "away"
          ]
        },
        " to Pilate. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "LUK 23:2"
        },
        "And they began to accuse Him, saying, “We found this ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "man"
          ]
        },
        " subverting our nation, forbidding payment of taxes to Caesar, and proclaiming Himself to be Christ, a King.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "LUK 23:3"
        },
        "So Pilate asked Him, “Are You the King of the Jews?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“You have said ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "so"
              ]
            },
            ",”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " replied."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "LUK 23:4"
        },
        "Then Pilate said to the chief priests and the crowds, “I find no basis for a charge against this man.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "LUK 23:5"
        },
        "But they kept insisting, “He stirs up the people all over Judea ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "with His"
          ]
        },
        " teaching. He began in Galilee ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and has come"
          ]
        },
        " all the way here.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Jesus before Herod"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "LUK 23:6"
        },
        "When Pilate heard ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        ", he asked if the man was a Galilean. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "LUK 23:7"
        },
        "And learning that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " was under Herod’s jurisdiction, he sent Him to Herod, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who"
          ]
        },
        " himself was in Jerusalem at that time."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "LUK 23:8"
        },
        "When Herod saw Jesus, he was greatly pleased. He had wanted to see Him for a long time, because he had heard about Him and was hoping to see Him perform a miracle. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "LUK 23:9"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Herod"
          ]
        },
        " questioned ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " at great ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "length"
          ]
        },
        ", but He gave no answer."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "LUK 23:10"
        },
        "Meanwhile, the chief priests and scribes stood there, vehemently accusing Him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "LUK 23:11"
        },
        "And even Herod and his soldiers ridiculed and mocked ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        ". Dressing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        " in a fine robe, they sent Him back to Pilate."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "LUK 23:12"
        },
        "That day Herod and Pilate became friends; before this ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "time"
          ]
        },
        " they had been enemies."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Crowd Chooses Barabbas"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 27:15-23",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 27:15–23"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 15:6-11",
          "content": [
            "Mark 15:6–11"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "LUK 23:13"
        },
        "Then Pilate called together the chief priests, the rulers, and the people, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "LUK 23:14"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said to them, “You brought me this man as ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "one who"
          ]
        },
        " was inciting the people ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to rebellion"
          ]
        },
        ". I have examined ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        " here in your presence ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " found ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        " not guilty of your charges against Him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "LUK 23:15"
        },
        "Neither ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "has"
          ]
        },
        " Herod, for he sent Him back to us. As you can see, He has done nothing deserving of death. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "LUK 23:16"
        },
        "Therefore I will punish Him ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " release ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        ".”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "23:16 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "BYZ and TR include "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fv",
                  "content": [
                    "17"
                  ]
                },
                "Now Pilate was obligated to release to the people one prisoner at the feast"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; see ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "MAT 27:15",
                  "content": [
                    "Matthew 27:15"
                  ]
                },
                " and Mark 15:6."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "LUK 23:18"
        },
        "But they all cried out in unison: “Away with this ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "man"
          ]
        },
        "! Release Barabbas to us!” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "LUK 23:19"
        },
        "(",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Barabbas"
          ]
        },
        " had been imprisoned for an insurrection in the city, and for murder.)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "LUK 23:20"
        },
        "Wanting to release Jesus, Pilate addressed them again, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "LUK 23:21"
        },
        "but they kept shouting, “Crucify ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        "! Crucify Him!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "LUK 23:22"
        },
        "A third ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "time"
          ]
        },
        " he said to them, “What evil ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "has"
          ]
        },
        " this ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "man"
          ]
        },
        " done? I have found in Him no offense worthy of death. So after I punish Him, I will release ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        ".”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "LUK 23:23"
        },
        "But they were insistent, demanding with loud voices for ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " to be crucified. And their clamor",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "23:23 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "BYZ and TR include "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "and that of the chief priests"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " prevailed. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "LUK 23:24"
        },
        "So Pilate sentenced ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " their demand be met. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "LUK 23:25"
        },
        "As they had requested, he released the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "one"
          ]
        },
        " imprisoned for insurrection and murder, and he handed Jesus over to their will."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Crucifixion"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "PSA 22:1-31",
          "content": [
            "Psalm 22:1–31"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 27:32-44",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 27:32–44"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 15:21-32",
          "content": [
            "Mark 15:21–32"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JHN 19:16-27",
          "content": [
            "John 19:16–27"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "LUK 23:26"
        },
        "As ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the soldiers"
          ]
        },
        " led Him away, they seized Simon of Cyrene on his way in from the country, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " they put the cross on him to carry behind Jesus."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "LUK 23:27"
        },
        "A great number of people followed Him, including women who kept mourning and wailing for Him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "LUK 23:28"
        },
        "But Jesus turned to them ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Daughters of Jerusalem, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "do"
              ]
            },
            " not weep for Me, but weep for yourselves and for your children. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "29",
              "sid": "LUK 23:29"
            },
            "Look, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " days are coming when ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "people"
              ]
            },
            " will say, ‘Blessed ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "are"
              ]
            },
            " the barren ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "women"
              ]
            },
            ", the wombs that never bore, and breasts that never nursed!’ ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "30",
              "sid": "LUK 23:30"
            },
            "At that time"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "‘they will say to the mountains, “Fall on us!”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "and to the hills, “Cover us!”’",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "23:30 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "ref",
                      "loc": "HOS 10:8",
                      "content": [
                        "Hosea 10:8"
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "LUK 23:31"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "For if ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "men"
              ]
            },
            " do these things ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "while"
              ]
            },
            " the tree ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "is"
              ]
            },
            " green, what will happen ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "when"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "it is"
              ]
            },
            " dry?”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "LUK 23:32"
        },
        "Two others, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who were"
          ]
        },
        " criminals, were also led away to be executed with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "LUK 23:33"
        },
        "When they came to the place called The Skull,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "23:33 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Greek "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Kranion"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; Vulgate "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Calvariae"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                ", rendered in some translations as "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Calvary"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " they crucified Him there, along with the criminals, one on ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His"
          ]
        },
        " right and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the other"
          ]
        },
        " on ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His"
          ]
        },
        " left."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "LUK 23:34"
        },
        "Then Jesus said, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Father, forgive them, for they do not know what they are doing.”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "23:34 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Some manuscripts do not include "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Then Jesus said, “Father... what they are doing.”"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " And they divided up His garments by casting lots.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "23:34 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "See ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PSA 22:18",
                  "content": [
                    "Psalm 22:18"
                  ]
                },
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "LUK 23:35"
        },
        "The people stood watching, and the rulers sneered at ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        ",",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "23:35 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "See ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PSA 22:7",
                  "content": [
                    "Psalm 22:7"
                  ]
                },
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " saying, “He saved others; let Him save Himself if ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He"
          ]
        },
        " is the Christ of God, the Chosen ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "One"
          ]
        },
        ".”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "36",
          "sid": "LUK 23:36"
        },
        "The soldiers also mocked Him ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " came up to offer Him sour wine.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "23:36 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "to offer Him wine vinegar"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "LUK 23:37"
        },
        "“If You are the King of the Jews,” they said, “save Yourself!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "38",
          "sid": "LUK 23:38"
        },
        "Above Him was ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "posted"
          ]
        },
        " an inscription:",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "23:38 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "BYZ and TR include "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "written in Greek, Latin, and Hebrew"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; see ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "JHN 19:20",
                  "content": [
                    "John 19:20"
                  ]
                },
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "pc",
      "content": [
        "THIS ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "IS"
          ]
        },
        " THE KING OF THE JEWS."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "39",
          "sid": "LUK 23:39"
        },
        "One of the criminals who hung ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there"
          ]
        },
        " heaped abuse on Him. “Are You not the Christ?” he said. “Save Yourself and us!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "40",
          "sid": "LUK 23:40"
        },
        "But the other ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "one"
          ]
        },
        " rebuked him, saying, “",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Do"
          ]
        },
        " you not even fear God, since you are under the same judgment? ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "41",
          "sid": "LUK 23:41"
        },
        "We  ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "are punished "
          ]
        },
        " justly, for we are receiving what our actions deserve. But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        " man has done nothing wrong.” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "42",
          "sid": "LUK 23:42"
        },
        "Then he said, “Jesus, remember me",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "23:42 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "BYZ and TR "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "said to Jesus, “Remember me, Lord,"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " when You come into Your kingdom!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "43",
          "sid": "LUK 23:43"
        },
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " said to him, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Truly I tell you, today you will be with Me in Paradise.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Death of Jesus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "PSA 31:1-24",
          "content": [
            "Psalm 31:1–24"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 27:45-56",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 27:45–56"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 15:33-41",
          "content": [
            "Mark 15:33–41"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JHN 19:28-30",
          "content": [
            "John 19:28–30"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "44",
          "sid": "LUK 23:44"
        },
        "It was now about ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " sixth hour, and darkness came over all the land until ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " ninth hour.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "23:44 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "That is, from noon until three in the afternoon"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "45",
          "sid": "LUK 23:45"
        },
        "The sun was darkened,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "23:45 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "failed "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "was obscured"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; BYZ and TR "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "became dark"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " and the veil of the temple was torn down ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " middle."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "46",
          "sid": "LUK 23:46"
        },
        "Then Jesus called out in a loud voice, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Father, into Your hands I commit My Spirit.”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "23:46 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PSA 31:5",
                  "content": [
                    "Psalm 31:5"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " And when He had said this, He breathed His last."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "47",
          "sid": "LUK 23:47"
        },
        "When the centurion saw what had happened, he gave glory to God, saying, “Surely this was ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "a"
          ]
        },
        " righteous man.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "23:47 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "an innocent man"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "48",
          "sid": "LUK 23:48"
        },
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " all the people who had gathered for this spectacle saw what had happened, they returned ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "home"
          ]
        },
        " beating ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " breasts. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "49",
          "sid": "LUK 23:49"
        },
        "But all those who knew ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        ", including ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " women who had followed Him from Galilee, stood at a distance watching these things."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Burial of Jesus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ISA 53:9-12",
          "content": [
            "Isaiah 53:9–12"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 27:57-61",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 27:57–61"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 15:42-47",
          "content": [
            "Mark 15:42–47"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JHN 19:38-42",
          "content": [
            "John 19:38–42"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "50",
          "sid": "LUK 23:50"
        },
        "Now ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there was"
          ]
        },
        " a Council member named Joseph, a good and righteous man, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "51",
          "sid": "LUK 23:51"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who"
          ]
        },
        " had not consented to their decision ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " action. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He was"
          ]
        },
        " from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Judean town ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of"
          ]
        },
        " Arimathea ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " was waiting for the kingdom of God. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "52",
          "sid": "LUK 23:52"
        },
        "He went to Pilate to ask ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "for"
          ]
        },
        " the body of Jesus. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "53",
          "sid": "LUK 23:53"
        },
        "Then he took it down, wrapped it in a linen cloth, and placed it in a tomb cut into the rock, where no one had yet been laid. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "54",
          "sid": "LUK 23:54"
        },
        "It was Preparation Day, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Sabbath was beginning.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "23:54 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "was about to begin"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "55",
          "sid": "LUK 23:55"
        },
        "The women who had come with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " from Galilee followed, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " they saw the tomb and how His body was placed. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "56",
          "sid": "LUK 23:56"
        },
        "Then they returned to prepare spices and perfumes. And they rested on the Sabbath, according to the commandment."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "24",
      "sid": "LUK 24"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Resurrection"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MAT 28:1-10",
          "content": [
            "Matthew 28:1–10"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 16:1-8",
          "content": [
            "Mark 16:1–8"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JHN 20:1-9",
          "content": [
            "John 20:1–9"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "LUK 24:1"
        },
        "On the first ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "day"
          ]
        },
        " of the week,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "24:1 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "But on the first of the Sabbaths,"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " very early in the morning, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the women"
          ]
        },
        " came to the tomb, bringing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " spices they had prepared. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "LUK 24:2"
        },
        "They found the stone rolled away from the tomb, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "LUK 24:3"
        },
        "but when they entered, they did not find the body of the Lord Jesus. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "LUK 24:4"
        },
        "While they were puzzling over this, suddenly two men in radiant apparel stood beside them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "LUK 24:5"
        },
        "As ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the women"
          ]
        },
        " bowed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " faces to the ground in terror, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the two men"
          ]
        },
        " asked them, “Why do you look for the living among the dead? ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "LUK 24:6"
        },
        "He is not here; He has risen! Remember how He told you while He was still in Galilee: ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "7",
              "sid": "LUK 24:7"
            },
            "‘The Son of Man must be delivered into ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " hands of sinful men, and be crucified, and on the third day rise again.’"
          ]
        },
        "”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "LUK 24:8"
        },
        "Then they remembered His words. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "LUK 24:9"
        },
        "And when they returned from the tomb, they reported all these things to the Eleven and to all the others. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "LUK 24:10"
        },
        "It was Mary Magdalene, Joanna, Mary the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "mother"
          ]
        },
        " of James, and the other women with them ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who"
          ]
        },
        " told ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        " to the apostles. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "LUK 24:11"
        },
        "But their words seemed like nonsense to them, and they did not believe ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the women"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "LUK 24:12"
        },
        "Peter, however, got up ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " ran to the tomb. And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "after"
          ]
        },
        " bending down ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " seeing only the linen cloths, he went away, wondering to himself what had happened."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Road to Emmaus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 16:12-13",
          "content": [
            "Mark 16:12–13"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "LUK 24:13"
        },
        "That same day two of them were going to a village called Emmaus, about seven miles",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "24:13 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Greek "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "being sixty stadia in distance"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; that is, approximately 6.9 miles or 11.1 kilometers"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " from Jerusalem. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "LUK 24:14"
        },
        "They were talking with each other about everything that had happened. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "LUK 24:15"
        },
        "And as they talked and deliberated, Jesus Himself came up ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " walked along with them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "LUK 24:16"
        },
        "But their eyes were kept from recognizing Him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "LUK 24:17"
        },
        "He asked them, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“What are you discussing so intently as you walk along?”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "They stood still, with sadness on their faces. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "LUK 24:18"
        },
        "One ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of them"
          ]
        },
        ", named Cleopas, asked Him, “",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Are"
          ]
        },
        " You the only visitor to Jerusalem ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "does"
          ]
        },
        " not know the things that have happened ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there"
          ]
        },
        " in recent days?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "19",
              "sid": "LUK 24:19"
            },
            "“What things?”"
          ]
        },
        " He asked."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "“The events involving Jesus of Nazareth,” they answered. “",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "This"
          ]
        },
        " man was a prophet, powerful in speech and action before God and all the people. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "LUK 24:20"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Our"
          ]
        },
        " chief priests and rulers delivered Him up to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " sentence of death, and they crucified Him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "LUK 24:21"
        },
        "But we were hoping He was the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "One who"
          ]
        },
        " would redeem Israel. And besides all ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        ", ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        " is ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " third day since these things took place."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "LUK 24:22"
        },
        "Furthermore, some of our women astounded us. They were at the tomb early this morning, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "LUK 24:23"
        },
        "but they did not find His body. They came ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " told ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "us"
          ]
        },
        " they had seen a vision of angels, who said that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " was alive. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "LUK 24:24"
        },
        "Then some of our companions went to the tomb and found ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        " just as the women had described. But Him they did not see.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "LUK 24:25"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " said to them, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“O foolish ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "ones"
              ]
            },
            ", and slow of heart to believe all that the prophets have spoken! ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "26",
              "sid": "LUK 24:26"
            },
            "Was it not necessary for the Christ to suffer these things and then to enter His glory?”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "LUK 24:27"
        },
        "And beginning with Moses and all the Prophets, He explained to them what  ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "was written "
          ]
        },
        " in all the Scriptures about Himself."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "LUK 24:28"
        },
        "As they approached the village where they were headed, He seemed to be going farther. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "LUK 24:29"
        },
        "But they pleaded with Him, “Stay with us, for it is nearly evening and the day is almost over.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "So He went in to stay with them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "LUK 24:30"
        },
        "While He was reclining ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "at the table"
          ]
        },
        " with them, He took bread, spoke a blessing and broke ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        ", ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " gave ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        " to them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "LUK 24:31"
        },
        "Then their eyes were opened and they recognized ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " — and He disappeared from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their sight"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "LUK 24:32"
        },
        "They asked each other, “Were not our hearts burning within us as He spoke with us on the road ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " opened the Scriptures to us?” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "LUK 24:33"
        },
        "And they got up ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " very hour ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " returned to Jerusalem."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "There"
          ]
        },
        " they found the Eleven and those with them, gathered together ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "LUK 24:34"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " saying, “The Lord has indeed risen and has appeared to Simon!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "LUK 24:35"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the two"
          ]
        },
        " told what had happened on the road, and how they had recognized ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " in the breaking of the bread."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Jesus Appears to the Disciples"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JHN 20:19-23",
          "content": [
            "John 20:19–23"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "1JN 1:1-4",
          "content": [
            "1 John 1:1–4"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "36",
          "sid": "LUK 24:36"
        },
        "While they were describing these ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "events"
          ]
        },
        ", ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " Himself stood among them and said, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Peace ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "be"
              ]
            },
            " with you.”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "LUK 24:37"
        },
        "But they were startled and frightened, thinking they had seen a spirit."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "38",
              "sid": "LUK 24:38"
            },
            "“Why are you troubled,”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " asked, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“and why ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "do"
              ]
            },
            " doubts arise in your hearts? ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "39",
              "sid": "LUK 24:39"
            },
            "Look at My hands and My feet. It is I Myself. Touch Me and see — for a spirit ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "does"
              ]
            },
            " not have flesh and bones, as you see I have.”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "40",
          "sid": "LUK 24:40"
        },
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " He had said this, He showed them ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His"
          ]
        },
        " hands and feet."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "41",
          "sid": "LUK 24:41"
        },
        "While they were still in disbelief because of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " joy and amazement, He asked them, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Do you have anything here to eat?”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "42",
          "sid": "LUK 24:42"
        },
        "So they gave Him a piece of broiled fish,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "24:42 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "BYZ and TR include "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "and some honeycomb"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "43",
          "sid": "LUK 24:43"
        },
        "and He took ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " ate ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        " in front of them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "44",
          "sid": "LUK 24:44"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " said to them, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“These ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "are"
              ]
            },
            " the words I spoke to you while I was still with you: Everything must be fulfilled that ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "is"
              ]
            },
            " written about Me in the Law of Moses, the Prophets, and ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " Psalms.”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "45",
          "sid": "LUK 24:45"
        },
        "Then He opened their minds to understand the Scriptures."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "46",
          "sid": "LUK 24:46"
        },
        "And He told them, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“This ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "is"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "what"
              ]
            },
            " is written: The Christ will suffer and rise from ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " dead ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "on"
              ]
            },
            " the third day, ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "47",
              "sid": "LUK 24:47"
            },
            "and in His name repentance and",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "24:47 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "NA, NE, and WH "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "repentance for"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            " forgiveness of sins will be proclaimed to all nations, beginning in Jerusalem. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "48",
              "sid": "LUK 24:48"
            },
            "You are witnesses of these things."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "49",
          "sid": "LUK 24:49"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "And behold, I am sending the promise of My Father upon you. But remain in the city until you have been clothed with power from on high.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Ascension"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 16:19-20",
          "content": [
            "Mark 16:19–20"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ACT 1:6-11",
          "content": [
            "Acts 1:6–11"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "50",
          "sid": "LUK 24:50"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " had led them out as far as Bethany, He lifted up His hands ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " blessed them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "51",
          "sid": "LUK 24:51"
        },
        "While He was blessing them, He left them and was carried up into heaven. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "52",
          "sid": "LUK 24:52"
        },
        "And they worshiped Him ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " returned to Jerusalem with great joy, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "53",
          "sid": "LUK 24:53"
        },
        "praising God continually in the temple."
      ]
    }
  ]
}